System.register([],function(e,t){"use strict";return{execute:function(){const t=e("domain","messages"),n=e("locale_data",JSON.parse('{"messages":{"":{"domain":"messages","plural_forms":"nplurals=2; plural=(n != 1);","lang":"en_US"},"Add to conference":[""],"All selected abonents were disconnected due to timeout":[""],"Are you sure you want to hang up the selected abonents?":[""],"copy":[""],"Create group":[""],"Disconnecting abonent":[""],"Do you really want to stop incoming presentation?":[""],"Free":[""],"ID:":[""],"Incoming presentation successfully stopped":[""],"less than a second":[""],"Log out":[""],"Move":[""],"Not specified":[""],"PIN:":[""],"Roles:":[""],"Route:":[""],"Stop incoming presentation":[""],"Successfully added %n/%m":[""],"“Cascading” is a term used related to an MCU (multipoint control unit) or the device needed for connecting several video conferencing endpoints. Sometimes, the number of endpoints can be larger than the number of ports on an MCU. In this case one has to connect one MCU to another MCU. This process is called cascading. The word you need to translate is a subheading. Here, one can check if cascading is currently enabled. Nominative case.\\u0004Cascading":[""],"“Cascading” is a term used related to an MCU (multipoint control unit) or the device needed for connecting several video conferencing endpoints. Sometimes, the number of endpoints can be larger than the number of ports on an MCU. In this case one has to connect one MCU to another MCU. This process is called cascading. The word you need to translate is a subheading. Here, one can check if cascading is currently enabled. Nominative case.\\u0004Cascading:":[""],"A brief description for the role of an administrator.\\u0004Given all the rights by default":[""],"A button\\u0004Delete":[""],"A button enabling a user to move to the next stage\\u0004Continue":[""],"A button enabling a user to start the selected conferences\\u0004Start":[""],"A button ending an outgoing call.\\u0004End call":[""],"A button for moving a participant from one virtual meeting to another (up to 10 characters including spaces)\\u0004Move":[""],"A button in the dialogue window\\u0004Install":[""],"A button in the dialogue window\\u0004Remove":[""],"A button in the pop-up window\\u0004Reboot":[""],"A button in the pop-up window\\u0004Restart":[""],"A button in the pop-up window\\u0004Save":[""],"A button in the pop-up window\\u0004Shut down":[""],"A button needed for redialling a conference participant.\\u0004Redial":[""],"A button opening a context menu\\u0004More":[""],"A button opening a context menu enabling\\u0004More":[""],"A button or an option in the context menu. This option is needed for adding an item on the list. For example, we can add a user to the list of conference participants.\\u0004Add":[""],"A button removing a participant from an ongoing conference\\u0004Disconnect":[""],"A button that sends (exports) system log to a desktop\\u0004Export":[""],"A button that will save the changes.\\u0004Save":[""],"A button that will send a text message to the conference chat\\u0004Send":[""],"A button which opens the menu for viewing and editing layouts.\\u0004Layout settings":[""],"A chart indicating the extent to which CPUs are loaded. Please note that in this case we are talking about multiple CPUs.\\u0004CPUs load":[""],"A checkbox enabling automatic gain control.\\u0004Enable AGC":[""],"A checkbox enabling noise cancelation (reduction)\\u0004Enable noise cancellation":[""],"A checkbox enabling the display of information about a user’s audio codec.\\u0004Audio codec":[""],"A checkbox enabling the display of information about a user’s video codec.\\u0004Video codec":[""],"A checkbox enabling the display of information about the resolution of a user’s video.\\u0004Video resolution":[""],"A checkbox enabling the system administrator to view a conference participant’s avatar. \\u0004Participant’s avatar":[""],"A checkbox enabling the system administrator to view a conference participant’s video. \\u0004Participant’s preview":[""],"A checkbox, if the checkbox is marked, the participants, who were disconnected from the conference due to connection problems, will be redialled automatically.\\u0004Auto redial participants  if the connection is lost":[""],"A checkbox. A layout is the arrangement of video windows during a virtual meeting. If this box is marked, the information about layouts will be saved when the database will be exported.\\u0004Layouts":[""],"A checkbox. A role is a set of permissions given to a user or user group. If this box is marked, information about roles will be saved when the database will be exported.\\u0004Roles":[""],"A checkbox. An audio channel is a group of participants who can send and receive audio from each other during a video meeting. If this checkbox is marked, information about audio channels will be saved when the database is exported.\\u0004Audio channels":[""],"A checkbox. If this box is marked, information about conference schedules will be saved when the database will be exported.\\u0004Schedule":[""],"A checkbox. If this box is marked, information about server configurations will be saved when the database will be exported.\\u0004Configurations":[""],"A checkbox. If this box is marked, information about the participants, who were invited to the conference, will be saved when the database will be exported.\\u0004Scheduled participants":[""],"A checkbox. If this box is marked, information about user groups will be saved when the database will be exported.\\u0004Groups":[""],"A checkbox. If this box is marked, information about users will be saved when the database is exported.\\u0004Users":[""],"A checkbox. If this box is marked, the general information about conferences will be saved when the database is exported. If the rules of the target language allow, do not, do not add the word “information”. The word “General” is also used as one of the tabs\\u0004General":[""],"A checkbox. If this checkbox is activated, a system administrator will be able to see participant’s videos when checking the list of people currently participating in a conference. These videos will be more like animations.\\u0004Show previews (animated icons) in the list of participants in an ongoing conference":[""],"A column header where the administrator can check the date and time when network traffic was captured (collected).\\u0004Date and time":[""],"A conference type in which there are no fixed presets, and the admin can customize the settings in any way depending on the event type and participants’ needs.\\u0004General":[""],"A conference type in which there is only one participant (lecturer) who will be seen and heard by other participants. Other participants (attendees) will only be allowed to watch and listen. Nominative case.\\u0004Lecture":[""],"A conference type in which there is only one participant (lecturer) who will be seen and heard by other participants. The attendees will only be allowed to watch and listen.\\u0004Lecture":[""],"A counter indicating how many items have been selected.\\u0004Selected: %n":[""],"A counter indicating how many items have been selected. Please do not delete %n because it will be replaced with an integer. The noun is deliberately omitted after “selected” because this phrase may be used in multiple situations.\\u0004Selected: %n":[""],"A counter indicating the number of days. If the word “day” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the numeral, please provide multiple translations of this word.\\u0004%n day":["","%n days"],"A counter indicating the number of hours. If the word “hour” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the numeral, please provide multiple translations of this word.\\u0004%n hour":["","%n hours"],"A counter indicating the number of minutes. If the word “minute” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the numeral, please provide multiple translations of this word.\\u0004%n minute":["","%n minutes"],"A counter indicating the number of participants in a group. %n will be replaced with an integer. So, please don’t delete or translate this part of the string.\\u0004Participants: %n":[""],"A counter indicating the number of seconds. If the word “second” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the numeral, please provide multiple translations of this word.\\u0004%n second":["","%n seconds"],"A counter indicating the number of years. If the word “year” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the numeral, please provide multiple translations of this word.\\u0004%n year":["","%n years"],"A default text in the date picker. Please note that here, a user can select multiple dates. This is why the plural form is used.\\u0004Select dates":[""],"A drop-down list for selecting the interface language.\\u0004Language":[""],"A header in a dialogue box\\u0004Deleting a layout":[""],"A header in a dialogue box\\u0004Deleting an audio channel":[""],"A header in a dialogue box\\u0004Ending content sharing":[""],"A heading displayed above three radio buttons enabling a system administrator to configure settings for audio calls.\\u0004Audio call settings":[""],"A heading for a chart indicating the extent to which reserved server resources are being used.\\u0004Reserved resources":[""],"A heading for a chart. Please note that in this context, a threat is a shortened version of “thread of execution” or the smallest sequence of programmed instructions that can be managed by a computer. So, you need to keep this term in mind when translating this phrase.\\u0004Computing thread load":[""],"A heading for a list of conferences that are not being held at the moment.\\u0004Inactive conferences (%n)":[""],"A heading for a section where the administrator can select how participants’ names will be displayed in a video meeting.\\u0004Display name style":[""],"A heading in the dialogue window\\u0004Delete update":[""],"A heading in the dialogue window\\u0004Installing a new TrueConf MCU version (%n_version)":[""],"A heading in the dialogue window. In this section the administrator can select what kind of additional information should be displayed about a user. For example, this information might include data about audio bitrate or video resolution (up to 37 characters including spaces).\\u0004Display additional information":[""],"A hint indicating that the administrator can select multiple layouts when recording a video conference. A layout is the arrangement of video windows. The word “predefined” is used to indicate that the layout has to be selected before the start of video recording.\\u0004You can record this conference with multiple predefined layouts":[""],"A legend for a diagram\\u0004Available disk space (Gb)":[""],"A legend for a diagram\\u0004Current load":[""],"A legend for a diagram\\u0004Download speed: %N kbps":[""],"A legend for a diagram\\u0004Upload speed: %N kbps":[""],"A legend for a diagram\\u0004Used (Gb)":[""],"A list item secondary text\\u0004Participants: %n":[""],"A notification\\u0004Another layout has been broadcast to the specified address":[""],"A notification\\u0004Video storage is full. Please increase your storage capacity or delete some video recordings":[""],"A notification about a successful update\\u0004Successfully updated to version %n_version":[""],"A notification displayed if the admin enters an incorrect domain name in the input field. The notification also indicates that the admin may contact the technical support department. Please note that “TrueConf” is a company name. If the rules of the target language allow, do not transliterate this word. Use the English word instead.\\u0004Please try to enter the domain again or contact TrueConf technical support":[""],"A notification displayed in case of some problems with the software license (incorrect serial number). Please note that “TrueConf” is a company name. If the rules of the target language allow, do not transliterate this word. Use the English word instead.\\u0004Please try to enter the serial number again or contact TrueConf technical support":[""],"A notification displayed in case of some problems with the software license validity. Please note that “TrueConf” is a company name. If the rules of the target language allow, do not transliterate this word. Use the English word instead.\\u0004Invalid license. Please contact TrueConf technical support":[""],"A notification displayed in case of some problems with the software license. Please note that “TrueConf” is a company name. If the rules of the target language allow, do not transliterate this word. Use the English word instead.\\u0004Please contact TrueConf technical support":[""],"A notification displayed to a meeting moderator. It will be displayed when he/she tries to appoint one of the participants as lecturer. The \\"lecturer\\" is the user who can be seen and heard by all other participants. However, to do it, the moderator has to turn on this participant\'s camera. Please note that the word \\"lecturer\\" is already used in the GUI. So, you will need to check how it was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004To appoint as lecturer, enable video":[""],"A notification displayed to a meeting moderator. It will be displayed when he/she tries to appoint one of the participants as lecturer. The “lecturer” is the user who can be seen and heard by all other participants. However, to do it, the moderator has to turn on this participant’s camera. Please note that the word “lecturer” is already used in the GUI. So, you will need to check how it was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004To appoint the participant as lecturer, the camera should be turned on":[""],"A notification displayed to a meeting moderator. The term \\"lecturer\\" may refer to a person, video file, or an image that can be seen and heard by all conference participants. Here, the problem is that the image cannot be given the role of a lecturer because at this point, it is not displayed to other conference participants.\\u0004To appoint as lecturer, show the image":[""],"A notification displayed to a server administrator. Here, we are talking about the certificate needed for the correct work of the HTTPS protocol. The certificate will be valid within a certain period, e.g., from May to December. The problem is that this certificate cannot be used before the start of its validity period, e.g., in April.\\u0004The certificate validity period has not started yet":[""],"A notification displayed to a system administrator when he/she creates a video meeting. The hint indicates that one of the conference participants was unavailable when the conference started and could not be reached. Please don’t delete or translate %Date, %StartTime, and %EndTime because these parts of the string will be replaced with actual values for date and time.\\u0004Unable to call participant at %StartTime (%Date)":[""],"A notification displayed to a user when he/she changes some settings of a video conference. This notification is displayed when the new settings are being applied. At this point, the process is not yet complete.\\u0004Changes are being applied to the conference":[""],"A notification displayed to the admin. An audio channel is a group of participants who can send and receive audio from each other during a video meeting.\\u0004An audio channel will be automatically created when the conference starts":[""],"A notification displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server. Here, we are speaking about the mechanism which enables a conference participant to be displayed in an enlarged window, if he/she is speaking at the moment.\\u0004Voice activity detection has been disabled":[""],"A notification displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server. Here, we are speaking about the mechanism which enables a conference participant to be displayed in an enlarged window, if he/she is speaking at the moment. In this case, voice activity detection is used.\\u0004Voice activity detection has been enabled":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator when he/she adds new data to the account. In this case, we are not talking about the creation of a new account. More likely, the admin will add new data to the existing account.\\u0004Account data has been added":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator when he/she creates a new group in the address book. Please note that %GroupName will be replaced with an actual name. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004The group “%GroupName” has been created":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator when he/she deletes information which is needed for the configuration of a server.\\u0004The server data has been deleted":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator when he/she saves data needed for server configuration.\\u0004The server data has been saved":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator when he/she sends email invitations to the participants of a video conference.\\u0004Conference invitations have been sent to all scheduled participants":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator when he/she sends invitations to multiple conference participants. In this case, the invitations have been sent only to some of the selected participants. Please note that %n will be replaced with a number greater than 1. If the word “participants” has multiple endings depending on the preceding numeral, please provide multiple translations of this sentence.\\u0004Conference invitation has been sent to %n scheduled participant out of  %m":["","Conference invitations have been sent to %n scheduled participants out of  %m"],"A notification displayed to the server administrator when he/she tries to update the firmware or settings of multiple video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004Update may take some time.The web interface will be unavailable during this period. All ongoing conferences held on the endpoints will be ended and restarted.":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator.  Please note that in this case, we will not be deleting an account (more likely, the admin will be deleting some data related to the account).\\u0004Account data has been deleted":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator. Here, we are referring to the certificate and key used in HTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure).\\u0004The certificate and key have been generated":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator. In this case the words %TerminalName1 and %TerminalName2 refer to hardware-based video conferencing endpoints. The admin can link a video conferencing endpoint to a contact (%DisplayName). If an endpoint is linked to a contact, each call to this user will be directed to this endpoint.  The admin can also link the contact to a different video conferencing endpoint. Please note that %TerminalName1, %TerminalName2 and %DisplayName will be replaced with actual names. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The contact “%DisplayName” is already linked to the endpoint “%TerminalName1”. Do you want to link this contact to the endpoint “%TerminalName2”?":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator. In this case, the term “audio channel” refers to a group of participants who can send or receive audio. Please note that some of them are only allowed to receive audio Others can both send and receive audio. This term will be used in the context of multi-language meetings requiring the assistance of interpreters.\\u0004The audio channel “%ChannelName” has been created":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator. The hint indicates that at present, one cannot send email invitations for conference participants because the data needed for the configuration of the SMTP (Simple Mail Transfer Protocol) server has not been provided.\\u0004The SMTP server data has not been specified":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator. The lecturer is the only participant in a video meeting who is visible to other participants. In this case, %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username. Do not delete or replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004“%DisplayName” has been appointed as a lecturer":[""],"A notification displayed to the server administrator. This person tries to find information about a certain layout (the arrangement of video windows during  a conference). It is possible to search for layouts by their names.\\u0004Unable to find the layout":[""],"A notification displayed to the system\\u0004The database has been successfully imported":[""],"A notification displayed when a new user is added to the conference. Please note that %DisplayName and %ConfName will be replaced with a username and conference name. So, do not delete these parts of the phrase.\\u0004“%DisplayName” has been added to the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"A notification displayed when a role with a custom name (%NameRole) is given to a user (%DisplayName).Please do not delete or translate  %NameRole and %DisplayName because they will be replaced with actual names for a role and user.\\u0004The role \\"%NameRole\\" has been added for \\"%DisplayName\\"":[""],"A notification displayed when a role with a custom name is given to multiple users. A role is a set of rights and permissions. Do not delete or replace %NameRole. In this case, %n is a counter indicating the number of users.\\u0004The role \\"%NameRole\\" has been added for multiple users (%n)":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin adds a file to a video conference. This media file may be used for content sharing or slideshow. Please note both %FileName and %ConfName will be replaced with the names of a file and a conference. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The file “%FileName” has been added to the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin adds a network address for the selected user. This address will be needed for calling this person. %Displayname will be replaced with the username. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Added an address for the user \\"%DisplayName\\"":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin adds a new schedule for a video conference (a conference may have multiple schedules). Please note that there are multiple types of schedule. %ScheduleType will be replaced with a type name. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Added a schedule with the type \\"%ScheduleType\\"":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin adds a new user to a certain group. Please note that %DisplayName and %GroupName will be replaced with the names of a user and group. So, do not edit or delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Added the user \\"%DisplayName\\" to the group \\"%GroupName\\"":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin adds multiple media files to a video conference. These media files may be used for content sharing or slideshow. Please note that %ConfName will be replaced with the names of a conference. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence. Besides. %n will be replaced with a number.\\u0004Several files (%n) have been added to the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin adds multiple users to the selected group. Please note that %GroupName and %n will be replaced with a group name and number. So, do not edit or  delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Added several users (%n) to the group \\"%GroupName\\"":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin deletes a network address for the selected user. This address was used for calling this person. %Displayname will be replaced with the username. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Deleted the address of the user \\"%DisplayName\\"":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin deletes multiple  network addresses for the selected user. These addresses are needed for calling this person. %Displayname will be replaced with the username. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Deleted several addresses (%n) of the user \\"%DisplayName\\"":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin deletes several users. Please note that %n will be replaced with an actual number of deleted users. Do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Deleted several users (%n)":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin physically deletes multiple files. %n will be replaced with a number. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Deleted several files (%n)":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin removes a user from the selected group. Please note that %DisplayName and %GroupName will be replaced with the names of a user and group. So, do not edit or delete these parts of the sentence. The verb “remove” is used because information about the user will not be physically deleted.\\u0004Removed the user \\"%DisplayName\\" from the group \\"%GroupName\\"":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin removes several users (%n) from the selected group.  Please note that %GroupName and %n will be replaced with a number. So, do not edit or replace these parts of the sentence. The verb “remove” is used because information about the users will not be physically deleted.\\u0004Removed multiple users (%n) from the group \\"%GroupName\\"":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin sends a text message to a video conference. Please note that %ConfName will be replaced with the name of a video conference. So, do not edit or delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Sent a message to the conference \\"%ConfName\\"":[""],"A notification displayed when an admin uploads multiple files on the server.  %n will be replaced with a number. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Uploaded several files (%n)":[""],"A notification displayed when an information has been copied to clipboard.\\u0004Copied to clipboard":[""],"A notification displayed when clicking on the button starts video recording of the selected conference (%ConfName). It is possible to select a layout (%LayoutName) that will be used for recording. %ConfName and %LayoutName will be replaced with actual names. So, don’t delete or translate these parts of the string.\\u0004Recording “%ConfName” conference with “%LayoutName” layout":[""],"A notification displayed when clicking on the button that ends video recording of the selected conference (%ConfName). The word “end” was used in this string instead of “paused” or “stopped” to indicate that recording cannot be resumed in a single click. It is possible to select a video layout (%LayoutName) that will be used for recording. %ConfName and %LayoutName will be replaced with actual names. So, don’t delete or translate these parts of the string.\\u0004Ended recording of “%ConfName” conference with “%LayoutName” layout":[""],"A notification displayed when clicking the button that ends streaming of the selected conference (%ConfName). The word “ended” is used to indicate that streaming cannot be resumed in a single click. It is possible to select the type of a video layout (%LayoutName) that will be used for recording. %ConfName and %LayoutName will be replaced with actual values. So, don’t delete or translate these parts of the string.\\u0004Ended streaming of “%ConfName” conference with “%LayoutName”":[""],"A notification displayed when clicking the button that starts streaming of the selected conference (%ConfName). It is possible to select a video layout (%LayoutName) that will be used for streaming. %ConfName and %LayoutName will be replaced with actual names. So, don’t delete or translate these parts of the string.\\u0004Streaming “%ConfName” conference with “%LayoutName” layout":[""],"A notification displayed when multiple participants are added to the conference. Please note that %ConfName will be replaced with a conference name. So, do not delete this part of the phrase. Besides, %n is a counter indicating the number of users. Do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Multiple participants (%n)  have been added to the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"A notification displayed when the admin clicks on an icon button. If this button is clicked, the call address will be permanently displayed (pinned) in the contact list (in the small menu providing brief information about a user). Please note that a call address is a network address needed for making a call over IP networks, e,g., one can mention SIP or H.323 addresses. Here, we are using the word “pin” because a user may have multiple call addresses, but only one of them can be displayed. In this context, pinning an address is similar to pinning a message in the chat.\\u0004The user address has been pinned in the contact list":[""],"A notification displayed when the admin creates a new video conference. Please note that %ConfName will be replaced with an actual conference name. So, don’t delete or translate this part of the string.\\u0004“%ConfName” conference has been created":[""],"A notification displayed when the admin is saving some changes.\\u0004Your changes have been saved":[""],"A notification displayed when the administrator copies the settings of a video conference (e.g, audio and video, layout settings, and so forth). These settings can be used for other conferences. Please don’t delete or translate %ConfName because it will be replaced with an actual conference name.\\u0004“%ConfName” conference settings have been copied":[""],"A notification displayed when the administrator deletes several user groups. Please note that %n will be replaced with an actual number of deleted groups. Do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Deleted several groups (%n)":[""],"A notification displayed when the administrator exports the database.\\u0004The database has been successfully exported":[""],"A notification displayed when the administrator imports a database. Please note that in this case, the word “address” refers to the network address needed for making a call over the Internet. For example, it is possible to mention SIP or H.323 addresses. Besides, an alias is an identifier needed for generating a hyperlink that will enable a user to join the conference.\\u0004If imported [s]user addresses[/s] and [s]conference aliases[/s] match the current data, the priority will be given to the current data.":[""],"A notification displayed when the administrator removes multiple participants from the selected conference. %n is the number of participants who have been removed. %ConfName will be replaced with an actual conference name. Please do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Multiple participants (%n) have been removed from the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"A notification displayed when the administrator resets the video conferencing server to its default values.\\u0004[s]Return to default settings[/s] will result in the complete loss of data, conferences, users, and all other information stored on the server. All active conferences will be ended.":[""],"A notification displayed when the administrator sets the server settings to their default values. \\u0004The web interface will be unavailable while default settings are restored. All active conferences will be ended. When the task is completed, the server will be restarted.":[""],"A notification displayed when the administrator starts content sharing during a video meeting (or multiple meeting). For example, he/she can show an image and video file to conference participants. Please note that %n will be replaced with a number of files. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Started sharing multiple files (%n)":[""],"A notification displayed when the administrator starts content sharing during a video meeting. For example, he/she can show an image or video file to conference participants.  Please note that %FileName will be replaced with a file name. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Started sharing the file “%FileName”":[""],"A notification displayed when the server administrator imports a new contact to the address book. Please note that %m is the total number of contacts that can be imported. It will be replaced with a number. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Successfully imported 1 contact out of %m":[""],"A notification displayed when the server administrator imports multiple address book contacts. Please note that %n is the number of contacts that was imported while %m is the total number of contacts. If the word “contacts” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the preceding numeral, please provide multiple translations of this sentence. %n and %m will be replaced with an integer; so do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Successfully imported %n contact out of %m":["","Successfully imported %n contacts out of %m"],"A notification displayed when the server administrator links a hardware-based endpoint to a certain contact in the address book. In this case, each call to this contact will be directed to this endpoint. Please note that %DisplayName and %TerminalName will be replaced with the name of the contact and endpoint. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The endpoint “%TerminalName” has been linked to the contact “%DisplayName”":[""],"A notification displayed when the server administrator starts a video conference. Please note that %ConferenceName will be replaced with an actual conference name. So, do not delete or replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004The conference “%ConferenceName” has been started":[""],"A notification displayed when the server administrator uploads a file on the server. This file will be  needed for updating the video conferencing software.\\u0004An update has been uploaded.":[""],"A notification displayed when the server administrator uploads the license file. Here, the possible cause of the problem is that the web page has not been refreshed. Please note that “TrueConf” is a company name. If the rules of the target language allow, do not transliterate this word. Use the English word instead.\\u0004Please try to refresh the page or contact TrueConf technical support":[""],"A notification displayed when two users are added to the conference. Please note %DisplayName1 and %DisplayName2 will be replaced with actual usernames. Besides, %ConfName will be replaced with an actual conference name. So, do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004“%DisplayName1” and “%DisplayName2” have been added to the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"A notification indicating that data is now being deleted from the server.\\u0004Clearing data from the server":[""],"A notification indicating the reserve copy of the database is now created.\\u0004Creating database backup":[""],"A notification that the server database is now being exported.\\u0004Exporting database":[""],"A notification that the server database is now being imported.\\u0004Importing database":[""],"A notification to a system administrator when he/she tries to change the server settings.\\u0004Settings change will lead to MCU restart. You will not be able to hold any conferences during this period. All conferences that were started before the restart will be ended.":[""],"A notification to the server administrator if a certain action cannot be performed because there are license restrictions on the number of user connections to the server.  Please note that this phrase will be used in multiple contexts.\\u0004This action is unavailable. The maximum number of connections has been reached":[""],"A notification when the server administrator deletes all of data stored on the server.\\u0004Deletion of data has been completed successfully":[""],"A page header\\u0004Send a message to conference chat":[""],"A part of the text hint. In this section, a user can either select a file in the explorer or drag-and-drop it right in the application. Please note that this phrase should not be capitalized because it is a part of the larger sentence: “Select a file or drag and drop it here”.\\u0004or drag and drop it here":[""],"A pop-up header\\u0004Add users to this group":[""],"A pop-up header\\u0004Deleting a group":[""],"A pop-up header\\u0004Edit network interface":[""],"A pop-up header. The pop up will be displayed when the administrator adds a user to a group.\\u0004Adding to a group":[""],"A pop-up heading. The heading indicates that in this menu the administrator can control volume (both microphone and speakers) for a group of conference participants.\\u0004Volume control for selected participants":[""],"A pop-up hint displayed when a mouse is pointed to an icon. It means that some features are not available for a certain type of connection\\u0004Not supported for this type of connection":[""],"A pop-up hint displayed when a mouse is pointed to an icon. It means that some features like muting a microphone or disabling a camera are not supported for a certain type of connection protocol.\\u0004Not supported for this type of address":[""],"A pop-up hint displayed when the mouse is hovered over an icon button. If the button is clicked, new users will be allowed to join an ongoing video meeting.\\u0004Unlock the meeting":[""],"A pop-up hint displayed when the mouse is hovered over an icon button. If the button is clicked, new users will be unable to join an ongoing video meeting.\\u0004Lock the meeting":[""],"A pop-up hint for a button, The button enables users to sort the names of users, e.g., in direct or reverse alphabetical order.\\u0004Sort":[""],"A pop-up hint for an icon button that opens the menu where the admin can create a new user.\\u0004Create user":[""],"A pop-up hint for an icon button. If the button is clicked, a participant will receive an invitation call when the conference starts (up to 36 characters including spaces).\\u0004Call upon the conference start":[""],"A pop-up hint for an icon button. If the button is clicked, the participant will not receive an invitation call when the conference starts. However, he/she may join this meeting later (up to 36 characters including spaces).\\u0004Don’t call upon the conference start":[""],"A pop-up hint for an icon button. The button enables an administrator to delete a user account.\\u0004Delete":[""],"A pop-up title\\u0004Starting conferences":[""],"A question displayed on the conference web page. The user is able to join the meeting either from a browser or from a client application (mobile or desktop).\\u0004How would you like to join the conference?":[""],"A question displayed when an administrator tries to clear the history of conferences held on the video conferencing server.\\u0004It will be impossible to restore information about past conferences. Do you want to clear the history of conferences?":[""],"A question in the  pop-up window displayed when the admin tries to delete a video layout of a conference. Please note that a layout may have a custom name like %LayoutName. So, do not delete or translate this part of the phrase.\\u0004Do you want to delete the layout “%LayoutName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window\\u0004Are you sure you want to restart the MCU?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window\\u0004Are you sure you want to restart the OS?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window\\u0004Are you sure you want to shut down the server?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window\\u0004Do you want to delete “%ChannelName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window\\u0004Do you want to remove the selected audio channels from the scheduled session?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window\\u0004Do you want to remove the selected participants from the conference?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server. The lecturer is the only participant in a video meeting who is visible to other participants. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username. So, do not delete or replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to remove the current lecturer “%DisplayName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the admin deletes a file needed for updating the software or its settings. Please note that %FileName will be replaced with an actual filename. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to delete the update file “%FileName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the admin ends content sharing during a video meeting. In this case, he/she is  sharing the selected file (e.g., an image or a video file). Please note that in this case %FileName will be replaced with a filename. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to end sharing the file “%FileName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the admin tries to delete account information. This step is necessary so that it is possible to register video conferencing endpoints on the server. Please note that in this case, we will not be deleting an account (more likely, the admin will be deleting some data related to the account).\\u0004Do you want to delete account data to register endpoints?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator changes the settings for displaying participants in the layout. In this case, to “spotlight” means to display the participant in an enlarged video window. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with a username. So, do not delete or replace this part of the string.\\u0004In the current mode, the window of the active speaker is automatically spotlighted. If “%DisplayName” is selected, this participant will be pinned in the spotlighted window. Do you want to change the participant display mode?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator deleted a user account. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with a real user name. So, don’t delete or translate this part of the string.\\u0004Do you want to delete “%DisplayName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator deletes an address book group. Please note that %GroupName will be replaced with an actual group name. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to delete the group “%GroupName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator deletes multiple files from an ongoing conference. For example, these files may be used for content sharing. Please note that %n and %ConfName will be replaced with a number of files and the conference name. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to delete the selected files (%n) from the conference “%ConfName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator removes a user from one of the user groups. Please note that both %DisplayName and %GroupName will be replaced with actual names. So, don’t delete or translate these parts of the strings.\\u0004Do you want to remove “%DisplayName” from “%GroupName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator removes a user from the address book group. Please note that %DisplayName and %GroupNames will be replaced with an actual username and group name. So, do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to remove the user “%DisplayName” from the group “%GroupName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator sends the firmware update file to several video conferencing endpoints. Please note that %FileName will be replaced with an actual filename. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to send the firmware update file “%FileName” to the endpoints?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator tries to change the conference mode. A conference mode is a fixed group of settings for a video meeting. Please note that the words %ConferenceMode1 and %ConferenceMode2 will be replaced with the names of conference modes. Do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The current mode is “%ConferenceMode1”. Do you want to change the mode to “%ConferenceMode2”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator tries to delete a file used by the participants of an ongoing conference. For example, one of the participants may be using the file for content sharing. Please note that %FileName and %ConfName will be replaced with a filename and conference name. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to delete the file “%FileName” from the conference “%ConfName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator tries to delete two files used by the participants of an ongoing conference. For example, these files may be used for content sharing. Please note that %FileName1, %FileName2 and %ConfName will be replaced with filenames and the conference name. So, do not delete or remove these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to delete the files “%FileName1” and “%FileName2” from the conference “%ConfName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator tries to update the configurations of multiple video conferencing endpoints.  Please note that %File will be replaced with an actual filename. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence. The word “send” is used here instead of “update” because the  configuration file will only be sent to the video conferencing endpoint. However, it does not mean that the firmware will be immediately updated.\\u0004Do you want to send the configuration update “%FileName” to the endpoints?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator will be trying to delete the information about the server that will be used for sending emails.\\u0004Do you want to delete the data of the outgoing mail server?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the selected user (%UserName) is dismissed (removed) from a certain role (%RoleName). Please note that %UserName and %RoleName will be replaced with the  username and role name. So, do not delete or replace these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to remove the user “%DisplayName” from the role “%RoleName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator deletes a schedule from a conference. Please note that %ConferenceName will be replaced with the actual conference name. The conference may have multiple schedules and one of the schedules may be deleted. In this case, %ScheduleType will be replaced with a word describing the type of schedule, e.g., weekly, monthly or any other. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to delete the schedule with type “%ScheduleType” from the conference “%ConferenceName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator disconnects the selected participant from a conference. %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to disconnect “%DisplayName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator ends an ongoing conference. Please note that %ConferenceName will be replaced with an actual conference name. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to end the conference “%ConferenceName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator ends two ongoing conferences. Please note %ConferenceName1 and ConferenceName2 will be replaced with actual conference names. So, do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to end the conferences “%ConferenceName1” and “%ConferenceName2”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator is deleting a video conference. Please note that %ConferenceName will be replaced with an actual conference name. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to delete the conference “%ConferenceName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator is deleting multiple video conferences (more than two). %n is a counter indicating how many conferences have been selected. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to delete selected (%n) conferences?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator is deleting two video conferences. Please note that %ConferenceName1 and %ConferenceName2  will be replaced with actual conference names. So, do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to delete the conferences “%ConferenceName1” and “%ConferenceName2”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator removes a user from the list of conference participants. Please note that %DisplayName and %ConferenceName will be replaced with an actual username and the name of the conference; so, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to remove \\"%DisplayName\\" from the conference  \\"%ConferenceName\\"?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator removes a user from the list of conference participants. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username; so, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to remove “%DisplayName” from the conference?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator removes a user from the list of conference participants. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username; so, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to remove %DisplayName from the conference?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator removes multiple participants from the conference. In this case %n is a counter indicating how many users will be removed. Besides, %ConferenceName will be replaced with the name of the conference. Please do not delete or edit these  parts of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to remove selected participants (%n) from the conference \\"%ConferenceName\\"?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator removes multiple participants from the conference. In this case %n is a counter indicating how many users will be removed. Please do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to remove selected participants (%n) from the conference?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator removes two users from the list of conference participants. Please note that %DisplayName1 and %DisplayName2 will be replaced with usernames; so, do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to remove “%DisplayName1” and “%DisplayName2” from the conference?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator starts a video conference. Please note that %ConferenceName will be replaced with an actual conference name. So, do not delete or replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to start the conference “%ConferenceName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator starts multiple selected conferences. In this case, %n is the number of selected conferences. It will be replaced with an integer. So, do not delete or replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to start selected (%n) conferences?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator starts two video conferences. Please note that %ConferenceName1 and %ConferenceName2 will be replaced with the conference names. So, do not delete or replace these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to start the conferences “%ConferenceName1” and “%ConferenceName2”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator tries to delete a user account.\\u0004Do you want to delete the account?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator tries to delete information about a hardware video conferencing endpoint. Please note that %TerminalName will be replaced with an actual endpoint name. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to delete the endpoint “%TerminalName”?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator tries to end content sharing for multiple files (images or videos). Please note that %n will be replaced with a number of files. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to end sharing multiple (%n) files?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window, displayed when the server administrator ends multiple selected conferences. Please note that %n is the counter indicating how many conferences have been selected. Do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to end selected (%n) conferences?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window. Here, the administrator tries to change the value of maximum frame rate during video meetings. This change can take effect only after  the system (video conferencing server) is restarted.  So, the admin is asked to confirm his/her choice.\\u0004Do you want to save changes and restart the system?":[""],"A question in the dialogue window. The lecturer is the only participant in a video meeting who is visible to other participants. Please note that %DisplayName1 and %DisplayName2 will be replaced with usernames. So, do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004“%DisplayName1” is the current lecturer. Do you want to change the lecturer to “%DisplayName2”?":[""],"A question in the pop-up window displayed when the administrator tries to generate a new certificate and key needed for HTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure).\\u0004The uploaded certificate and key will be deleted. Do you want to generate new ones?":[""],"A radio button\\u0004Accept audio calls (the participant will be added to the layout with “No video caption”)":[""],"A radio button\\u0004Accept audio calls (the participant will not be displayed in the layout)":[""],"A radio button\\u0004Decline audio calls":[""],"A radio button. If this radio button is selected, a default background will be used for a video layout.\\u0004No skin":[""],"A section sub-header\\u0004Ping":[""],"A section sub-header\\u0004Traceroute":[""],"A section sub-header\\u0004Traffic capture":[""],"A status displayed if at the moment it is not known whether the application time is synchronized with the time server or not. It will be used in a phrase like “Status: no information”. The word “synchronization” was omitted because it will be used in other parts of the UI.\\u0004No information":[""],"A status indicating if the application time is currently synchronized with the time on the NTP (network time protocol) server. Please note that %Synchronized will be replaced with phrases like “Synchronized” or “Not synchronized”. So, do not delete or replace this part of the phrase when translating.\\u0004Status: %SynchronizationStatus":[""],"A status indicating that a certain feature is now disabled. Here, we are referring to the stream from an MCU (multipoint control unit). However, it may be used in other contexts as well.\\u0004Disabled":[""],"A sub-heading\\u0004H.460.1 settings":[""],"A sub-heading\\u0004Port range for BFCP":[""],"A sub-heading\\u0004Port range for H.245":[""],"A sub-heading\\u0004Public IPv4 address  (WAN)":[""],"A sub-heading\\u0004SIP settings":[""],"A sub-heading\\u0004TURN settings":[""],"A subheader\\u0004Control panel":[""],"A subheader\\u0004Main":[""],"A subheader\\u0004Settings":[""],"A subheading\\u0004Conference recording: %ConferenceName":[""],"A subheading\\u0004Disconnection reason:":[""],"A subheading\\u0004Video layout: %LayoutName":[""],"A subheading displayed if the video conferencing server is currently unavailable due to some reason.\\u0004The server is unavailable":[""],"A subheading for a list of conferences that are being held at the moment\\u0004Active conferences (%n)":[""],"A subheading for a section. In this section, the administrator will be able to select the font color.\\u0004Font color":[""],"A subheading for a slider. The slider will help the administrator to position text vertically.\\u0004Vertical alignment:":[""],"A subheading for a slider. This slider will help the administrator select the width of a container where conference participants’ names will be displayed.\\u0004Width:":[""],"A subheading for section. In this section, an administrator will select where participants’ names will be displayed in  a video meeting.\\u0004Display name position":[""],"A subheading for the section where the administrator will configure text alignment.\\u0004Text alignment":[""],"A subheading in the menu providing information about a video meeting.\\u0004Creator:":[""],"A subheading in the menu providing information about a video meeting.\\u0004Started by:":[""],"A subheading in the menu providing information about an ongoing conference call. In this subsection, the administrator can check information about the audio stream.\\u0004Audio":[""],"A subheading in the menu providing information about an ongoing conference call. In this subsection, the administrator can check information about the video stream.\\u0004Video":[""],"A subheading in the menu where one can check information about an event. In this case, the object is any kind of entity affected by an event. For example, it may be a user whose role was changed. Additionally, it can be the software version that was updated.\\u0004Object":[""],"A subheading in the menu where the admin can check information about a video conference. In this case, the word “mode” refers to a video conferencing mode or a group of settings for a video meeting. Nominative case.\\u0004Mode:":[""],"A subheading in the menu where the admin can check information about a video meeting. The lecturer is the only participant allowed to speak during a video meeting. Nominative case.\\u0004Lecturer:":[""],"A subheading in the menu where the admin can create a new video conference. A conference mode is a fixed group of settings (e.g., the video layout, participants’ rights, AV settings and so forth). The admin can select one of the conference modes. Nominative case.\\u0004Conference mode":[""],"A subheading in the menu where the admin can view information about a video meeting. Here, one can check who ended the video conference. We are using the noun “end” instead of “ended by” because the conference could also end automatically according to the schedule or due to some emergency e.,g, system crash or server shutdown.\\u0004End":[""],"A subheading in the menu where the admin can view information about a video meeting. Here, one can check who started the video conference. We are using the noun “start” instead of “started by” because the conference could also start automatically according to the predefined schedule.\\u0004Start":[""],"A subheading in the menu where the admin can view information about the network. This subheading will be followed by a MAC (Media Access Control) address.\\u0004MAC address:":[""],"A subheading in the menu where the admin can view information about the network. This subheading will be followed by an IP address.\\u0004IP address":[""],"A subheading.\\u0004E-mail:":[""],"A subheading.\\u0004Login:":[""],"A subheading.\\u0004Phone:":[""],"A subheading.\\u0004User name:":[""],"A subheading. Firmware is a piece of software needed for low-level control of a device (e.g., a video conferencing endpoint), The word “firmware” should be in the nominative case.\\u0004Firmware":[""],"A subheading. Here, one can check information about the schedule of a video meeting.\\u0004Schedule":[""],"A subheading. Here, one can check the reason why a participant could not be connected to a video conference.\\u0004Reason for not connecting":[""],"A subheading. Here, one can choose how to display content (e.g., slides or images) in video recordings of a conference or during streaming.\\u0004Content display in recording and streaming":[""],"A subheading. Here, one can configure notifications that will be displayed to users.\\u0004Notifications":[""],"A subheading. Here, one can configure settings for streaming a video conference to third-party services like YouTube.\\u0004Stream settings":[""],"A subheading. Here, one can find the network address needed for connecting to a video conference. The word is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Conference address:":[""],"A subheading. Here, the admin can check information about the call address of a video conferencing endpoint (e.g., one can mention SIP or H.323 address). This address is needed for making calls over the Internet.\\u0004Address":[""],"A subheading. Here, the admin can check the information about the firmware version of a hardware-based video conferencing endpoint. A firmware is a piece of software needed for the low-level control of a device.\\u0004Firmware version:":[""],"A subheading. Here, the admin can check the name of a contact or user associated with (linked to) a video conferencing endpoint. The calls made to this user will be directed to this endpoint.\\u0004Contact name:":[""],"A subheading. Here, the admin can check the serial number of a video conferencing endpoint.\\u0004Serial number:":[""],"A subheading. Here, the admin can check when the video conferencing endpoint was registered on the server.\\u0004Registration date and time:":[""],"A subheading. Here, the admin can configure settings for passwords, for example, their length.\\u0004Passwords":[""],"A subheading. Here, the admin can configure settings for passwords, for example, their length.\\u0004Requirements for account passwords":[""],"A subheading. Here, the admin can find the host address needed for connecting with the video conferencing endpoint.\\u0004Host:":[""],"A subheading. Here, the admin can find the list of users who have not been invited to the video conference yet. However, later the admin will call these users to invite them to the conference.\\u0004Selected: %n":[""],"A subheading. Here, the admin can find the list of users who have not been invited to the video conference yet. However, later the admin will call these users to invite them to the conference.\\u0004Stand-by":[""],"A subheading. Here, the administrator can configure settings for a video conferencing endpoint. In particular, he/she can upload a configuration file. The word “configuration” should be in the nominative case.\\u0004Configuration":[""],"A subheading. Here, the administrator can configure the settings of layout windows in which conference participants will be displayed.\\u0004Video windows settings":[""],"A subheading. Here, the administrator can set the requirements for the passwords that users are allowed to enter when signing in. For example, the admin can choose if it is necessary to use uppercase letters or digits. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Mandatory password requirements":[""],"A subheading. Here, the server can check the type of the current license. We are using the word “current” because the admin may have multiple licenses, but only one of them is used at the moment.\\u0004Current license type":[""],"A subheading. Here, the word “system” may refer to the version of the server currently used or the version of the video conferencing system. So, here, the word “system” does not necessarily refer to the operating system. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004System version":[""],"A subheading. Here, we are talking about the certificate and key needed for the work of the HTTPS protocol. The word “custom” is used because both the certificate and key were uploaded by the user (he/she did not use the default certificate). The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Custom certificate and key":[""],"A subheading. Here, we are talking about the certificate and key needed for the work of the HTTPS protocol. The word “default” means that the certificate and key are provided out of the box. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Default certificate and key":[""],"A subheading. Here, we are talking about the IP of the source of the event.\\u0004Source IP":[""],"A subheading. In this case, the word “system” is a part of the phrase “”system notifications”. The phrase has to be used in the nominative case.\\u0004System":[""],"A subheading. The subheading will be followed by the names of the groups in which the user participates.\\u0004Groups:":[""],"A switcher\\u0004Display by groups":[""],"A switcher\\u0004IP precedence":[""],"A switcher\\u0004Use ICE":[""],"A tab\\u0004NAT traversal":[""],"A tab name for the user profile (e.g, email, profile, time zone, and so forth).\\u0004Profile":[""],"A tab name. Here, a user can configure settings for video recording a conference and streaming it to third-party services. e.g., YouTube.\\u0004Recording and streaming":[""],"A tab name. Here, one can configure the settings for Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure.\\u0004HTTPS":[""],"A tab name. Here, the admin can find the list of files needed for updating the firmware of video conferencing endpoints or their settings.\\u0004Updates":[""],"A tab name. Here, the administrator can check some additional information about a user. In this case “additional” does not mean “advanced”.\\u0004Additional":[""],"A tab name. Here, the administrator can check the list of hardware-based video conferencing endpoints registered on the server. Nominative case.\\u0004List of endpoints":[""],"A tab name. Here, the administrator can configure settings for registering video conferencing endpoints on the server.\\u0004Registration settings":[""],"A tab name. Here, the administrator can configure settings for SMTP (Simple Mail Transfer Protocol).\\u0004SMTP":[""],"A tab name. Here, the administrator can find information about a user account (password, login).\\u0004User account":[""],"A tab name. Here, the administrator can find information about the address or addresses that will be needed for making a call over the Internet. For example, it may be an SIP or H.323 address (SIP and H.323 are the protocols).\\u0004Address":[""],"A tab name. Here, the administrator can find some general information about a user.\\u0004Information":[""],"A tab name. In this tab, the administrator can adjust various settings for a particular user, for example, it is possible to change the sound volume or enable (disable) noise cancellation (up to 15 characters including spaces).\\u0004Settings":[""],"A tab name. In this tab, the administrator can check information about the content a user shares during a video meeting (up to 15 characters including spaces).\\u0004Content":[""],"A tab where the administrator can check where a participant’s video window is positioned in the layout.\\u0004Layout":[""],"A tab where the administrator can find data about bitrate, resolution, frame rate and other information about an ongoing conference call (up to 15 characters including spaces).\\u0004Video and audio":[""],"A tab where the administrator can find general information about a conference participant, for example, his/her display name in a video meeting (up to 15 characters including spaces).\\u0004General":[""],"A table column\\u0004User":[""],"A table column header. Here, the admin can check information about the contact (user) who is associated with a specific video conferencing endpoint. Each call to this user will be directed to this video conferencing endpoint.\\u0004Contact name":[""],"A table column header. Here, the administrator can check information about a hardware video conferencing endpoint; in particular, one can check the name of the video conferencing endpoint and its host address. The phrase “system name” refers to the name of the endpoint because it is a more accurate technical term.\\u0004System name and host":[""],"A table column header. Here, the administrator can check information about the duration of video conferences (up to 14 characters).\\u0004Duration":[""],"A table column header. Here, the administrator can check information about the number of participants in a video conference (up to 14 characters).\\u0004Participants":[""],"A table column header. Here, the server administrator can check information about a hardware-based video conferencing endpoiunt. A firmware is a piece of software needed for the low-level control of the device.\\u0004Firmware and serial number":[""],"A table column header. Here, the server can check how a conference ended. For example, it could be ended automatically according to the predefined schedule or it could be ended manually by the administrator (up to 14 characters).\\u0004End mode":[""],"A table column header. Here, the server can check how a conference was started. For example, it could be started automatically according to the predefined schedule or it could be started manually by the administrator (up to 14 characters).\\u0004Start mode":[""],"A table column header. Nominative case. Here, the admin can check the names of users.\\u0004Username":[""],"A table column header. The “event source” is the programming entity that caused a certain event. For example, a certain error could be caused by the work of the database.\\u0004Event source":[""],"A table column header. This column contains a list of additional information about the server event.\\u0004Additional":[""],"A table column header. This column contains the date and time when the server event occurred.\\u0004Date and Time":[""],"A table column header. This column contains the ID of the occurred server event.\\u0004ID":[""],"A table column header. This column contains the name of the occurred server event.\\u0004Event":[""],"A table column header. This column displays a symbol indicating the category of the server event.\\u0004Category":[""],"A table column heading. Here, the admin can check the name of a person who is using a video conferencing endpoint.\\u0004Contact name":[""],"A table column heading. Here, the admin can check the name of a video conferencing endpoint. The phrase “system name” is used here because it is a more accurate technical term.\\u0004System name":[""],"A table column heading. Here, the admin can check the network status of a video conferencing endpoint (online vs offline). Noun in the nominative case.\\u0004Status":[""],"A table column heading. Here, the admin can check the serial number of a video conferencing endpoint. Nominative case.\\u0004Serial number":[""],"A table column heading. Here, the admin can check the version of the firmware used on a hardware video conferencing endpoint. A firmware is a piece of software needed for the low-level control of a device.\\u0004Firmware version":[""],"A table column heading. Here, the admin can check when a video conferencing endpoint was registered on the server.\\u0004Registration date and time":[""],"A table column heading. Here, the admin can find the host address needed for connecting with the endpoint.\\u0004Host":[""],"A table column where one can find the number of participants in each virtual meeting\\u0004Participants":[""],"A table column where one can find the titles of virtual meetings.\\u0004Conference name":[""],"A table with the personal data of participants\\u0004Settings":[""],"A text displayed when the mouse is hovered over an icon. Here, we are talking about the devices connected to a video conference via certain protocols. VNC stands for Virtual Computer Networking, while RTSP stands for Real-time Streaming Protocol.\\u0004Connected devices (VNC/RTSP) and media files":[""],"A text field label\\u0004End":[""],"A text field label\\u0004Start":[""],"A text hint\\u0004[//]host[:port][/path]":[""],"A text hint\\u0004[username@]host[:port]":[""],"A text hint\\u0004%time_zone — your current time zone":[""],"A text hint\\u0004All events":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Audio codecs":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Automatically":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Busy":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Displayed: %n out of %m":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Enter a DTMF command":[""],"A text hint\\u0004File is ready for import":[""],"A text hint\\u0004For all participants":[""],"A text hint\\u0004From %DateTime":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Information":[""],"A text hint\\u0004kbps":[""],"A text hint\\u0004More":[""],"A text hint\\u0004No audiochannels created":[""],"A text hint\\u0004No layouts created":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Participants":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Please select active session or scheduled conference from list":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Please, select user or group from list":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Primary contact name: “%FileName”":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Primary contact name: “%name”":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Recording":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Remove validity end":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Selected: %n out of %m":[""],"A text hint\\u0004The list is empty":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Until %DateTime":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Video codecs":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Video settings":[""],"A text hint\\u0004Video windows: %N":[""],"A text hint\\u0004When start a conference, default layout would be created automatically":[""],"A text hint describing a video layout. A layout is the arrangement of conference participants’ windows on the screen.\\u0004Four large video windows in the center with smaller windows around them":[""],"A text hint describing a video layout. A layout is the arrangement of conference participants’ windows on the screen.\\u0004Two large windows in the center with small windows on the right and left":[""],"A text hint describing a video layout. A layout is the arrangement of conference participants’ windows on the screen.\\u0004Two large windows on the left with small windows on the right":[""],"A text hint describing how the application will select the participant who is speaking at the moment.\\u0004There can be only one speaker in the conference. This person is automatically selected with the help of voice activity detection":[""],"A text hint describing the layout (arrangement of video windows on the screen) for a video meeting.\\u0004When present, the speaker is displayed in a single full-screen video window that replaces all layouts previously configured for other participants. Preconfigured layouts will be displayed without any changes to the speaker during the presentation and to all other participants when the speaker is absent":[""],"A text hint describing the layout during a video conference. Here, we are talking about the video conferencing mode in which the user, who is speaking at the moment, is always seen and heard by other meeting participants.\\u0004The active speaker is displayed in a single fullscreen video window that will replace the layouts created for other participants. Previously configured layouts will be displayed to the speaker during the presentation and to all other participants when the speaker is absent.":[""],"A text hint describing the layout for the video conferencing mode in which every user can see and hear the participant who is speaking at the moment. The speaker is identified through the voice detection mechanism.\\u0004The active speaker is displayed in an enlarged video window in the layout with a spotlighted view or in the upper left corner in the grid-view layout. Layout settings are not changed. When the active speaker is absent, everyone receives preconfigured layouts without any changes.":[""],"A text hint describing the requirements for a password.  In this case, %n will be replaced with a number. If the phrase “lowercase letter” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the preceding numeral, please provide multiple translations of this sentence. This phrase is not capitalized because it is preceded by the phrase: “The password should include at least”.\\u0004%n lowercase letter (a-z)":["","%n lowercase letters (a-z)"],"A text hint describing the requirements for a password.  In this case, %n will be replaced with a number. If the phrase “special character” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the preceding numeral, please provide multiple translations of this sentence. This phrase is not capitalized because it is preceded by the phrase: “The password should include at least”.\\u0004%n special character (* - _ ! + = { } [ ] % $ ^ : & @ )":["","%n special characters (* - _ ! + = { } [ ] % $ ^ : & @ )"],"A text hint describing the requirements for a password.  In this case, %n will be replaced with a number. If the phrase “uppercase letter” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the preceding numeral, please provide multiple translations of this sentence. This phrase is not capitalized because it is preceded by the phrase: “The password should include at least”.\\u0004%n uppercase letter (A-Z)":["","%n uppercase letters (A-Z)"],"A text hint describing the requirements for a password.  In this case, %n will be replaced with a number. If the word “digit” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the preceding numeral, please provide multiple translations of this sentence. This phrase is not capitalized because it is preceded by the phrase: “The password should include at least”.\\u0004%n digit (0-9)":["","%n digits (0-9)"],"A text hint describing the requirements for a password. In this case, %n will be replaced with a number. If the word “character” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the preceding numeral, please provide multiple translations of this sentence. This phrase is not capitalized because it is preceded by the phrase: “The password should include at least”.\\u0004%n character":["","%n characters"],"A text hint describing the requirements for a password. This hint will be followed by specific requirements such as the number of characters,\\u0004A password has to include at least:":[""],"A text hint describing the schedule of a video conference. This hint will be displayed for a conference that will be held only once.\\u0004The conference will not be repeated":[""],"A text hint describing the schedule of a video conference. This hint will be displayed for a recurring meeting.\\u0004The conference will be held on the selected dates":[""],"A text hint describing the schedule of a video conference. This hint will be displayed for a recurring meeting.\\u0004The conference will be held weekly on the selected days":[""],"A text hint describing the type of a conference in which  there is only one participant (lecturer) who can be seen and heard by other participants. Please note that the word “lecturer” is already used in the GUI. So, if possible, check how it was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004A default conference mode in which the appointed lecturer is always displayed in a single full-screen window in the layout of other participants. All participants see preconfigured layouts when the lecturer is absent":[""],"A text hint describing the video conferencing mode in which a participant is immediately seen and heard by other users as soon as he/she starts speaking (voice detection mechanism is used).\\u0004Everyone can see and hear participants when they start speaking":[""],"A text hint describing the video layout (arrangement of video windows on the screen) for an online lecture. The lecturer is the only conference participant who is visible to other users. Please note that the word “lecturer” is already used in the GUI. So, if possible, check how it was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004When present, the lecturer is displayed in a single full-screen video window that replaces all layouts previously configured for other participants. Preconfigured layouts will be displayed without any changes to the lecturer during the presentation and to all other participants when the lecturer is absent":[""],"A text hint describing the video layout. A layout is the arrangement of participants’ video windows on the screen.\\u0004All layout parameters are set manually":[""],"A text hint describing the video layout. A layout is the arrangement of participants’ video windows on the screen. The word “scheme” is used to refer to the initial pattern according to which the layout will be created. For example, there may be a large window in the center and smaller windows around it.\\u0004The layout is changed depending on the selected pattern. The number of slots is set manually.":[""],"A text hint displayed below the input field where the maximum size of an RTP package has to be specified\\u0004from 1280 to 1500 (bytes)":[""],"A text hint displayed for a participant who joined a virtual meeting from a browser.\\u0004Joined from browser":[""],"A text hint displayed for a video window in the conference layout. This window will be used for displaying a media file (image or video).\\u0004Select a media file that will be displayed in this video window":[""],"A text hint displayed for an icon. By clicking on one of these icons, the administrator will select a way of aligning the text.\\u0004Center":[""],"A text hint displayed for an icon. By clicking on one of these icons, the administrator will select a way of aligning the text.\\u0004Left":[""],"A text hint displayed for an icon. By clicking on one of these icons, the administrator will select a way of aligning the text.\\u0004Right":[""],"A text hint displayed for one of the conference participants. The hint indicates that the participant was removed (disconnected) from the conference at a certain moment. hh:mm and %date will be replaced with actual values for date and time. So, do not delete these parts of the phrase. Besides, %ConnectionTime is the amount of time the user was participating in a conference. Do not delete or translate this part of the phrase.\\u0004Disconnected at %hh:mm on %date (%ConnectionTime)":[""],"A text hint displayed for one of the conference participants. The hint indicates that the participant was removed (disconnected) from the conference at a certain time (%hh:mm). hh:mm will be replaced with digits like “15:27”. So, do not delete this part of the phrase. Please note that %ConnectionTime is the amount of time the user was participating in a conference. Do not delete or translate this part of the phrase.\\u0004Disconnected at %hh:mm (%ConnectionTime)":[""],"A text hint displayed if the Fixed Participant option is chosen.\\u0004Select the participant who will be permanently displayed in this slot":[""],"A text hint displayed in the application that supports the preview of some files, e.g., images. However, some file formats are not supported.\\u0004Preview is unavailable for this type of file":[""],"A text hint displayed in the input field\\u0004Display the module":[""],"A text hint displayed in the input field\\u0004Exclude the module":[""],"A text hint displayed in the input field\\u0004Type your message":[""],"A text hint displayed in the search field\\u0004Enter a command":[""],"A text hint displayed in the section where the admin can check why the conference ended. Here, the conference ended due to some emergency (e.g, system crash or server shutdown). Here, the word “emergency” is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Emergency":[""],"A text hint displayed to a conference moderator who tries to display a certain image in an enlarged window. However, at this point, this image is not displayed to other conference participants.\\u0004To display in an enlarged window, show the image":[""],"A text hint displayed to a conference moderator. Here, we are talking about the image (picture) displayed to conference participants.\\u0004The image cannot be hidden":[""],"A text hint displayed to a server administrator if the disk (hard disk drive or solid-state drive) is almost full and does not have enough free space.\\u0004Your disk is almost full":[""],"A text hint displayed to a server administrator when he/she links a video conferencing endpoint to a new contact. If an endpoint is linked to a contact, each call to this user will be directed to this endpoint. In this case, the word “address” refers to the address needed for making  calls over the Internet, e.g., one can mention SIP or H.323 addresses.\\u0004All endpoint addresses that were added to the linked contact will remain in the card of this contact and will not be moved to the card of the new contact":[""],"A text hint displayed to a server administrator when there is little space on the disk drive.\\u0004Please free up space on the disk":[""],"A text hint displayed to a server administrator. It is used in the context of MCU and cascading. An   MCU (multipi-point control unit) is a hardware or software solution used for connecting several video conferencing endpoints. \\"Cascading\\" refers to the method of connecting multiple MCUs together to create a larger video conference that can support a high number of participants. If a conference gets the type “Center”, its video layout will be used for all participants connected to an MCU. By contrast, the conference with the “Periphery” status  will receive the layout created for the central conference.\\u0004Current cascading status of the conference: Center. New participants can be added only with the Periphery status.":[""],"A text hint displayed to a server administrator. The layout is the arrangement of video windows on the screen. The layout will be seen only by participants who connect to the meeting via SIP or H.323 protocols. SIP stands for Session Initiation Protocol.\\u0004The layout will be seen only by SIP and H.323 connections":[""],"A text hint displayed to a server administrator. This hint will be displayed when there is little space on the disk drive. Besides, at this point, the application video records ongoing conferences which decreases available disk space.\\u0004Please free up space on the disk or end video recording of ongoing conferences":[""],"A text hint displayed to a user before a physical server shutdown.\\u0004A shutdown will cut the server off its power supply. All active conferences will be ended.":[""],"A text hint displayed to a user before an MCU server restart.\\u0004An MCU restart may take some time. You will not be able to hold conferences during this period.":[""],"A text hint displayed to a user before an OS restart.\\u0004 An OS restart may take some time. The MCU web interface will be inaccessible during this period.":[""],"A text hint displayed to a user if connection to the server (or connection to a video conference) from a certain browser is unavailable.\\u0004Connection from this browser is unavailable":[""],"A text hint displayed to a user when he/she tries to access a virtual room. A virtual room is a video meeting that has no schedule. It can be accessed by participants when they need to.\\u0004This virtual room has not been opened":[""],"A text hint displayed to a user who is configuring the settings of a slot (window)  in the layout created for a video meeting. In this case, the word “content”  may refer to slides, PDF documents, and application windows.\\u0004The slot will be used for sharing content. This slot can be selected only once.":[""],"A text hint displayed to a user whose login or password has expired (ceased to be valid).\\u0004Your account information has expired":[""],"A text hint displayed to a user whose password will expire today (will no longer be valid).\\u0004Your password will expire today at %hh:mm":[""],"A text hint displayed to a user whose password will soon expire (will no longer be valid). If the word “day” has multiple endings depending on the preceding numeral, please provide multiple translations of this sentence.\\u0004Your password will expire in %n day":["","Your password will expire in %n days"],"A text hint displayed to a user.\\u0004Please contact the server administrator":[""],"A text hint displayed to a user. The hint indicates that the user can enter a certain network address in his/her browser or video conferencing application (desktop or mobile).\\u0004Enter in your browser or application":[""],"A text hint displayed to the admin if a certain action (e.g., file deletion) cannot be performed at the moment. This text hint can be used in multiple situations.\\u0004This action is unavailable":[""],"A text hint displayed to the admin. Here, we are talking about the password which remains valid for a limited period of time.\\u0004If the specified lifetime is less than the current lifetime, it will be necessary to change the password within 24 hours.":[""],"A text hint displayed to the admin. The hint indicates that the admin should change the password for a certain user since this current password is no longer valid. %Login will be replaced with a username. So, do not delete or replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004Change the password for the user %Login":[""],"A text hint displayed to the admin. The hint indicates that the password of a certain user will expire today (will no longer be valid).\\u0004The password will expire today at %hh:mm":[""],"A text hint displayed to the admin. The hint indicates that the password of a certain user will expire today (will no longer be valid).  If the word “day” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the preceding numeral, please provide multiple translations of this sentence.\\u0004The password will expire in %n day":["","The password will expire in %n days"],"A text hint displayed to the admin. The hint indicates that the password of a certain user will soon expire (will no longer be valid). Please note that this phrase will be followed by the time when the password will expire. For example, the password will expire today (or in two days).\\u0004The password will expire":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server when he/she adds a meeting participant. The admin has to choose at least one of the audio or video codecs that will be used for processing media streams from the participant. Please note that this phrase is supposed to be used in multiple situations when a user is expected to select at least one of the available options.\\u0004Please select at least one of the options":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server.  Please note that TrueConf is a company name. If possible, do not translate or transliterate this name. Use the English spelling instead.\\u0004Please restart the server or contact TrueConf technical support":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server.  This notification is displayed when a search query is made.\\u0004Unable to find the conference":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server. The admin has to change the settings of maximum frame rate during video meetings (e.g., he/she wants to increase or decrease it). Such changes will apply only after the system (server) is restarted. Besides, all conferences that are being held at the moment will end automatically.\\u0004The changes in maximum frame rate will take effect only after the system restart. All ongoing conferences will end automatically":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server. This hint will be displayed for an icon button that unmutes the microphone. Please note that a conference participant can mute his/her microphone. However, the administrator can unmute it on the server side.\\u0004The microphone was muted by the participant. Unmute on the server side":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server. This tooltip will be displayed for an icon button that mutes a participants’ microphone. Please note that a conference participant can mute his/her microphone. However, the microphone can also be muted by the administrator. In this case, even if the participant unmutes his/her microphone, this person will not be heard by other participants.\\u0004The microphone was muted by the participant. Mute on the server side":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of the video conferencing server. Here, we are talking about the application which enables administrators to connect one video conference to another. This hint refers to the section in the UI where the admin can connect a conference to another conference. If possible, please check how this UI element was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004To connect a conference hosted on your server, use the «Adding participants» window":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of the video conferencing server. Here, we are talking about the network address needed for making a call to a user. This hint will be displayed when a participant with this address has already been connected to a conference. On such occasions, it is impossible to save certain changes.\\u0004The address is connected to a conference. Changes cannot be saved.":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of the video conferencing server. Here, we are talking about the network address needed for making a call to a user. This hint will be displayed when the admin tries to edit this address. The problem is that a participant with this address has already been connected to a conference. So, at this point, the address cannot be edited.\\u0004The address is connected to a conference; address editing is unavailable.":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of the video conferencing server. It is used in the context of MCU and cascading. An  MCU (multipi-point control unit) is a hardware or software solution used for connecting several video conferencing endpoints. \\"Cascading\\" refers to the method of connecting multiple MCUs together to create a larger, scalable video conference that can support a very high number of participants. The word “Basic” is used because here we are talking about the simplest form of cascading.\\u0004Connection of new participants is available only in Basic cascading mode":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of the video conferencing server. The layout is the arrangement of video windows on the screen. The thing is that the application enables users to connect a conference to another conference. In such a case, the layout of the connected conference will be displayed in a separate window.\\u0004The participant will receive the conference layout in a separate video window":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator of the video conferencing server. This hint is used in the context of MCU and cascading. An   MCU (multipi-point control unit) is a hardware or software solution used for connecting several video conferencing endpoints. \\"Cascading\\" refers to the method of connecting multiple MCUs together to create a larger video conference that can support a high number of participants. If a conference gets the type “Center”, its video layout will be used for all participants connected to an MCU. By contrast, the conference with the “Periphery” status  will receive the layout created for the central conference.\\u0004Current cascading status of the conference: Periphery. Connection of new participants is unavailable":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator when he/she tries to add a new participant to a video conference. In this case, the administrator will be using the so-called call address (SIP or H.323) needed for sending audio and video over the network. This notification will be displayed if the selected user is already participating in the conference.\\u0004The user with this address has already joined the conference":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator when he/she tries to select and stream multiple media files. Please note that this hint may be used in other situations as well.\\u0004This action is unavailable for this type of file":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator who creates a video meeting. A virtual room is a constantly available meeting space that can be accessed by participants at any time.\\u0004By default, a conference without a schedule becomes a virtual room.":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator who tries to stream a video conference. Here, we are talking about the stream of a particular conference.\\u0004The stream is unavailable. Stream settings are not specified.":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator.\\u0004If the domain address is not specified, the current IP address of the server will be used":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator. The admin can select who should be displayed in the current window during a video meeting.\\u0004The participant, who is speaking at the moment, will be displayed in this slot":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator. The admin can select who should be displayed in the current window during a video meeting. The admin can make sure that only the selected participant is displayed in the window. However, the participant can also be randomly selected.\\u0004A randomly-selected participant will be displayed in this slot":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator. The hint indicates that a certain file cannot be deleted due to some reason.\\u0004Unable to delete":[""],"A text hint displayed to the administrator. This hint indicates that the software cannot operate in a closed network (offline), but this restriction can be removed if the full version of the software is purchased.\\u0004Please note that your license  does not support offline operation. To remove this restriction, you need to buy the full version of this product or test it for a limited period.":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator if the password of a user will soon expire. Here, we are talking about the password which is valid only for a certain time period.\\u0004The password will expire tomorrow at %hh:mm ":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator if there are no video conferencing endpoints registered on the server.\\u0004No registered endpoints":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator when he/she creates a new user. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username. So, do not delete this part of the sentence. In this case the term “user account” is not quite appropriate because the user account normally includes both login and password required for authorization. Here, we are talking about only an entry in the database.\\u0004The user “%DisplayName” has been created":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator when he/she imports address book contacts. An MCU (multi-point control unit) is a solution needed for connecting several video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004The MCU contact list will end all ongoing conferences. The web interface will be unavailable while contacts are imported.":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator when he/she needs to register a software solution. “Create registration file” is a text hint for a button that creates (generates) a new registration file. The “Next” button enables the admin to proceed to the next stage of registration. If possible, check how the text hints for these UI elements were previously translated into the target language.\\u0004Enter the registration key and server name and click «Create registration file». After downloading the file, click the «Next» button.":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator when he/she needs to register a software solution. Please note that the verb “Register” is a text hint for a button. If possible, check how this verb was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004Enter the registration key and server name and click «Register»":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator when he/she tries to send email to conference participants. However, in this case, none of the participants provided an email address.\\u0004No participants with an email address":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator when/he tries to delete a file. In this case, the selected file is permanently displayed (pinned) in the video layout created for a meeting. This is why it cannot be deleted.\\u0004The file cannot be deleted. It is pinned in the layout":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator when/he tries to delete a file. In this case, the selected file is used for video streaming. This is why it cannot be deleted.\\u0004The file cannot be deleted. It is now being streamed.":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator who needs to register a software solution. Please note that “Offline registration” is an option specifically intended for the cases when the server is within the closed network that has no access to the Internet. The button “Offline registration” is already used in the UI. If possible check how this text was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004Choose “Offline registration” if you are working in a closed network without access to the Internet":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator.\\u0004Click the button to download the archive with all system logs.":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator. Here, we are talking about the certificate which is needed for the correct work of the HTTPS protocol.\\u0004The certificate expired":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator. Please note that TrueConf MCU is a product name. If the rules of the target language allow it, do not transliterate this part of the sentence. Use the English spelling instead. MCU stands for multipoint control unit or a solution needed for connecting several video conferencing endpoints. Besides, this text will include a hyperlink. This is why the following markup elements [a] and [/a] are used. Do not delete them.\\u0004To learn more about the server features and its work, go to the [a]TrueConf MCU page[/a]":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator. The hint indicates that automatic playback for audio or video files has been disabled for the file.\\u0004Playback upon conference start is disabled":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator. The hint indicates that it is possible to create accounts (register) for video conferencing endpoints. Please note that MCU refers to a multi-point control unit or a system connecting multiple video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004To register endpoints on the MCU, please specify the login information in the fields below":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator. The hint indicates that the file (audio or video) is no longer shared with other meeting participants.\\u0004Content sharing was ended":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator. The lecturer is the only conference participant who can be seen by the users who have joined the meeting. Please note that the word “lecturer” is already used in the GUI. So, if possible, check how it was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004Participants can see only the lecturer. Any conference participant can be appointed as lecturer":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator. This hint indicates that a participant can be displayed in an enlarged window, only if the admin turns on his/her camera.\\u0004To display in an enlarged window, enable video":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator. This hint indicates that a participant can be displayed in an enlarged window, only if the admin turns on his/her camera.\\u0004To display in an enlarged window, turn on the camera":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator. This hint is intended for the case when the administrator does not have the registration key. Please note that the button “Get a FREE key” is already used in the UI.  If possible check how this text was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004Click “Get a FREE key” if you have not received the registration key yet":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator. This hint is intended for the case when the administrator does not have the registration key. Please note that the button “Get a FREE key” is already used in the UI.  If possible check how this text was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004Click «Get a FREE key» if you have not received the registration key yet":[""],"A text hint displayed to the server administrator. This hint will be displayed for a window in the conference layout. This message indicates that one cannot disable the video stream for the selected window.\\u0004The video stream cannot be disabled":[""],"A text hint displayed when a file is added with the help of drag-and-drop.\\u0004Add file":[""],"A text hint displayed when the administrator tries to delete the history of video conferences held on the server. In such a case other information stored on the server, e.,g., user accounts, will not be deleted.\\u0004If the history of conferences is cleared, all information about past events and their participants will be lost completely. Other data stored on the server will not be affected.":[""],"A text hint displayed when the administrator tries to import a database.\\u0004Select a file for importing.":[""],"A text hint displayed when the application is connecting to the server. At this point, the process is not yet complete. This is why the “ing” ending is used. Please note that %n is the countdown timer. If the timer reaches zero, an error message will be displayed. %n will be replaced with a number. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Connecting to the server %n":[""],"A text hint displayed when the cursor is pointed to the icon.\\u0004Install update":[""],"A text hint displayed when the mouse cursor is pointed to the icon.\\u0004Add to address book":[""],"A text hint displayed when the mouse is hovered over an icon. Here, we are speaking about the detection of participants’ speech during a video conference. The application may change the layout if one of the participants starts speaking.\\u0004Voice activity detection is disabled":[""],"A text hint displayed when the mouse is hovered over an icon. Here, we are speaking about the detection of participants’ speech during a video conference. The application may change the layout if one of the participants starts speaking.\\u0004Voice activity detection is enabled":[""],"A text hint displayed when the mouse is hovered over an icon. Here, we are talking about the users who joined the conference via SIP (Session Initiation Protocol) and H.323 protocols.\\u0004Connected participants (SIP/H.323)":[""],"A text hint displayed when the server administrator is uploading a new file on the server. At this point, the process has not been completed yet. This is why the “ing” ending and three dots are used.\\u0004Uploading… Please wait":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004All video windows are equal in size":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004The largest window is above other windows":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004The largest window is below other windows":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004The largest window is in the center and surrounded by other windows":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004The largest window is in the center while other windows are above and below it":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004The largest window is in the upper left corner":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004The largest window is on the left":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004The largest window is on the right":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004The largest window is the center while other windows are on the right and on the left":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004The largest window is the lower left corner":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004The largest window with smaller ones on both sides and below":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004Two largest windows above smaller ones":[""],"A text hint displayed, when the cursor is directed to the layout icon.\\u0004Two largest windows are in the center while other windows are above and below them":[""],"A text hint explaining when a certain event will take place.\\u0004When a conference starts and when a participant is added to an ongoing conference":[""],"A text hint explaining when a lecturer can be appointed or changed during a video meeting. The lecturer is the only conference participant who is seen and heard by all other users. This phrase will be followed by several bullet points. This is why this phrase ends in a colon.\\u0004The lecturer can be appointed or changed:":[""],"A text hint explaining when it will be possible to appoint a lecturer in an online lesson or appoint a new one. The lecturer is the only conference participant who is seen and heard by all other users. This phrase is the continuation of this sentence: “The lecturer can be appointed or changed:”.\\u0004Before the conference start (selected from invited participants)":[""],"A text hint explaining when it will be possible to appoint a lecturer in an online lesson or select a new one. The lecturer is the only conference participant who is seen and heard by all other users. This phrase is the continuation of this sentence: “The lecturer can be appointed or changed:”.\\u0004During an ongoing conference (from the participants who have already joined the meeting)":[""],"A text hint for a chart providing information about a meeting. It will be displayed for the time interval between the moment when the call was started and the moment when the call reached its destination\\u0004connecting":[""],"A text hint for a chart providing information about a meeting. It will be displayed for the time interval during which the user was not present in the meeting.\\u0004not connected":[""],"A text hint for a date picker.\\u0004Select date and time":[""],"A text hint for a media file (audio or video). This hint indicates that a file has been added to a video conference. However, its playback will not start. Later, this file may be needed for content sharing.\\u0004Added without playback":[""],"A text hint for a radio button. If this button is selected, a certain video conferencing mode will be disabled.\\u0004Disabled":[""],"A text hint for a slider. A conference ID is an identifier of a virtual meeting. A participant may have to enter it in order to join a virtual meeting. The administrator can select for how long to display a screen for entering a conference ID.\\u0004Set a time limit (in minutes) to display a menu for entering conference ID":[""],"A text hint for an icon button. If the button is clicked, the video will start playing as soon as it finishes.\\u0004Auto replay":[""],"A text hint for an icon button. If this button is clicked, the selected conference participant will no longer be displayed in an enlarged video window in the layout.\\u0004Do not display in an enlarged window":[""],"A text hint for an icon button. This button enables the administrator to display the selected participant in an enlarged (spotlighted window) in the layout.\\u0004Display in an enlarged window":[""],"A text hint for an input field\\u0004Application":[""],"A text hint for an input field\\u0004Login":[""],"A text hint for an input field\\u0004New password":[""],"A text hint for an input field\\u0004Password":[""],"A text hint for an input field\\u0004Server address":[""],"A text hint for an input field\\u0004Stream name/key":[""],"A text hint for an input field\\u0004Username":[""],"A text hint for an input field where the admin can enter some additional information about the user.\\u0004Description":[""],"A text hint for an input field where the administrator can select the end time of a video meeting.\\u0004End time":[""],"A text hint for an input field where the administrator can select the start time of a video meeting.\\u0004Start time":[""],"A text hint for an input field.\\u0004Login":[""],"A text hint for an input field.\\u0004Password":[""],"A text hint for an input field.\\u0004User name":[""],"A text hint for an input field. Here, the admin can configure the size of the storage used for video recordings.\\u0004Video storage capacity (GB)":[""],"A text hint for an input field. Here, the admin can enter the address of the main server that will be needed for time synchronization. This phrase is the shortened version of “primary time server”. The word “time” was omitted because it is mentioned in other parts of the UI. Nominative case.\\u0004Primary server":[""],"A text hint for an input field. Here, the admin can enter the address of the secondary server needed for time synchronization. This server will be used if the primary time server is unavailable. Please note that the word “time” was omitted from this phrase because it is used in other parts of the UI. Nominative case.\\u0004Secondary server 1":[""],"A text hint for an input field. Here, the admin can enter the address of the secondary server needed for time synchronization. This server will be used if the primary time server is unavailable. Please note that the word “time” was omitted from this phrase because it is used in other parts of the UI. Nominative case.\\u0004Secondary server 2":[""],"A text hint for an input field. Here, the admin can enter the current time. Nominative case.\\u0004Time":[""],"A text hint for an input field. Here, the admin can specify the number of the port needed for connecting to the server.\\u0004Port":[""],"A text hint for an input field. Here, the admin will specify a part of the URL address, e.g. companyemail.com\\u0004Host":[""],"A text hint for an input field. Here, the administrator will enter an address needed for calling a user over the Internet. For example, it may be a SIP or H.323 address (SIP and H.323 are the network protocols).\\u0004Enter an address":[""],"A text hint for an input field. In this case, the word “sender” is the name of a person who will send the email.\\u0004Sender name":[""],"A text hint for an input field. In this case, the word “sender” is the name of a person who will send the email.\\n\\u0004Sender email":[""],"A text hint for an input field. The hint indicates that this field does not have to be filled.\\u0004Email (optional)":[""],"A text hint for an input field. The hint indicates that this field does not have to be filled.\\u0004Phone (optional)":[""],"A text hint for an input field. The hint is displayed when the administrator tries to change the password for a user.\\u0004Change password":[""],"A text hint for an input field. The hint is displayed when the administrator tries to change the password for a user.\\u0004Enter the current password":[""],"A text hint for an input field. The hint is displayed when the administrator tries to set a new password for a user.\\u0004Confirm the new password":[""],"A text hint for an option in the drop-down list. The hint indicates that if a certain option is chosen (it will be called “Automatically”) , the server will automatically decide which parameters to use.\\u0004Automatically selected by the server":[""],"A text hint for indicate the unit of measurement of the memory unit.\\u0004GB":[""],"A text hint for radio buttons\\u0004Type of address":[""],"A text hint for the administrator of a video conferencing server. In this case, some of the users participating in the video meeting will not be displayed in the video layout. Besides, each user, who is currently displayed in the layout, may be replaced with another participant at some moment. This process will be repeated throughout the meeting.\\u0004If the number of participants is larger than the number of available video windows, participants will be displayed in the layout by turns":[""],"A text hint for the name of a virtual meeting. The hint will be followed by the meeting name.\\u0004Conference name:":[""],"A text hint in the dialogue window\\u0004Are you sure you want to delete the «%n_version» file?":[""],"A text hint in the dialogue window\\u0004Installation may take some time.  TrueConf MCU web interface will be unavailable during this period. All active conferences will be ended.":[""],"A text hint in the dialogue window displayed when the administrator imports the database. Please note that MCU (multipoint control unit) is a device needed for connecting several video conferencing endpoints.If possible, use the English version of this word in your translation.\\u0004MCU database import will end all active conferences. The web interface will be unavailable.":[""],"A text hint in the dialogue window. The hint indicates that at present, a certain participant (%DisplayName) is permanently displayed (pinned) in the layout. However, if voice activity tracking is activated, the focus may shift onto a different participant. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual user name. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004In the current mode “%DisplayName” is pinned in the layout. If voice activity detection is enabled, the focus will be automatically shifted onto the active speaker. Do you want to change the participant display mode?":[""],"A text hint in the input field\\u0004DSCP audio":[""],"A text hint in the input field\\u0004DSCP other":[""],"A text hint in the input field\\u0004DSCP video":[""],"A text hint in the input field\\u0004End port":[""],"A text hint in the input field\\u0004From 1024":[""],"A text hint in the input field\\u0004Start port":[""],"A text hint in the input field\\u0004Up to 65 534":[""],"A text hint in the menu where one can check information about an event. This event involved some change in the application state: e.g., a user’s role could be changed or the application could be updated. Here, an admin can check the info about the current state (e.g., current role or version number).\\u0004Current":[""],"A text hint in the menu where one can check information about an event. This event involved some change in the application state: e.g., a user’s role could be changed or the application could be updated. Here, an admin can check the info about the previous state (e.g., previous role or version number).\\u0004Previous":[""],"A text hint in the section where a user can select a file and upload it on the server.\\u0004Select a file":[""],"A text hint in the section where the admin can configure settings for sending emails. An outgoing mail server is the server that will deliver emails to the users.\\u0004Outgoing mail server":[""],"A text hint in the section where the administrator can check why a certain service (process) was stopped. It will be followed by an explanation. This is why the colon is used. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Service interruption cause":[""],"A text hint in the table where the admin can check why a video conference ended. In this case, the conference ended because the video conferencing system was restarted by the administrator.\\u0004System was restarted":[""],"A text hint indicating no conference participants can be selected at the moment. This hint will be displayed if there are no users who meet certain criteria.\\u0004No participants are available for selection":[""],"A text hint indicating that  participants will join a video conference either by following a link in a browser or by using the client application (desktop or mobile). It will also be possible to join the conference from a video conferencing endpoint (a hardware device that can be connected to a video meeting).\\u0004Via a link, application and video conferencing endpoint":[""],"A text hint indicating that a certain feature is currently disabled\\u0004Disabled":[""],"A text hint indicating that a certain feature is currently enabled\\u0004Enabled":[""],"A text hint indicating that a certain feature is disabled by default\\u0004Disabled by default":[""],"A text hint indicating that a certain feature is enabled by default\\u0004Enabled by default":[""],"A text hint indicating that a certain feature is not available because there is not enough disk space.\\u0004Not enough disk space":[""],"A text hint indicating that a certain feature is now disabled. This hint can be used in multiple parts of the UI for various features.\\u0004disabled":[""],"A text hint indicating that a certain feature is now disabled. This hint can be used in multiple parts of the UI for various features.\\u0004Disabled":[""],"A text hint indicating that a certain feature is now enabled. This hint can be used in multiple parts of the UI for various features.\\u0004enabled":[""],"A text hint indicating that a certain file is not being used for content sharing. In other words, it is not streamed to other conference participants. Here, we are talking about an image or video file.\\u0004Not streamed":[""],"A text hint indicating that a certain video layout is intended for the selected participants of a video conference. %n is the number of selected participants. It will be replaced with a number. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004For selected participants (%n)":[""],"A text hint indicating that a certain video layout or an audio channel is intended for selected participants of a video conference. %n is the number of selected participants. It will be replaced with a number. So, do not delete or replace this part of the sentence. Please do not include the words “layout” and “audio channel” in the translation because they will be mentioned in other parts of the GUI.\\u0004For selected participants (%n)":[""],"A text hint indicating that a conference was either started or ended automatically (according to the specified schedule).\\u0004Automatically":[""],"A text hint indicating that a layout window is intended for a certain participant. This person will be constantly displayed in this window. If this participant does not join the meeting, this window will remain empty.\\u0004Fixed participant":[""],"A text hint indicating that a network protocol can be used, only if the administrator enables registration via the gatekeeper. A gatekeeper is a physical device or a software application that performs IP address translation, routing, and authentication.\\u0004To use this protocol, please enable registration via the gatekeeper in the [a]server settings[/a]":[""],"A text hint indicating that a new version of the software is installed. An MCU (multipoint control unit) is a device needed for connecting video conferencing endpoints. Please note that TrueConf MCU is a product name; so, keep the English version in your translation.\\u0004Installing a new TrueConf MCU version (%VersionNumber)":[""],"A text hint indicating that a participant is not connected to a video conference at the moment\\u0004Not connected":[""],"A text hint indicating that a randomly-selected participant will be displayed in the video layout.\\u0004Autofill ":[""],"A text hint indicating that a search query gave no result. This hint will be used in multiple parts of the GUI; this is why the word “matches” was used.\\u0004No matches found":[""],"A text hint indicating that a video conference is now being streamed. Please do not use the word “conference” because it will be mentioned in other parts of the GUI.\\u0004Streaming":[""],"A text hint indicating that a video window will be used for sharing content (e.g., slides, images, app windows, and so forth).\\u0004Content":[""],"A text hint indicating that at present no one has been added to the list of participants.\\u0004No scheduled participants":[""],"A text hint indicating that at present, the application system is not synchronized with the time on the NTP server. It will be used in a phrase like “Status: not synchronized”\\u0004Not synchronized":[""],"A text hint indicating that at present, the application time is synchronized with the time on the NTP server. It will be used in a phrase like “Status: Synchronized”\\u0004Synchronized":[""],"A text hint indicating that at the moment, the layout is not displayed to (received by) any of the conference participants.\\u0004No receivers":[""],"A text hint indicating that at the moment, the lecturer has not joined the meeting. A lecturer is the only participant who is allowed to speak during a video meeting. Other participants (attendees) can only watch and listen.\\u0004The lecturer is absent":[""],"A text hint indicating that at the present moment, the lecturer is not selected. Please note that the lecturer is the only participant allowed to speak during a conference.\\u0004Not selected":[""],"A text hint indicating that automatic gain control (AGC) is now disabled.\\u0004AGC is disabled":[""],"A text hint indicating that automatic gain control (AGC) is now working.\\u0004AGC is working":[""],"A text hint indicating that connection between a conference participant and the server was lost due to some reason (e.g., a network error). This hint will be displayed in the table where the administrator can check information about the users who did not join the conference.\\u0004Lost connection":[""],"A text hint indicating that media files (audio and video) will be played after they are added to a video conference. These files are needed for content sharing.\\u0004Playback after adding is enabled":[""],"A text hint indicating that media files (audio and video) will not be played after they are added to a video conference. Later, these files may be used for content sharing. \\u0004Playback after adding is disabled":[""],"A text hint indicating that no files have been uploaded on the server.\\u0004No uploaded files":[""],"A text hint indicating that no participant or content is currently displayed in the certain layout window.\\u0004Empty slot":[""],"A text hint indicating that no schedule has been configured for a video conference.\\u0004No schedule":[""],"A text hint indicating that no users have been added to the conference.\\u0004No participants":[""],"A text hint indicating that noise cancellation is now disabled.\\u0004Noise cancellation is disabled":[""],"A text hint indicating that noise cancellation is now working.\\u0004Noise cancellation is working":[""],"A text hint indicating that some video layout will be displayed to all participants.\\u0004For all participants":[""],"A text hint indicating that the account of a certain user was deleted at some moment in the past (the past indefinite tense or its equivalent in the target language has to be used). Here, we are referring to the person who created or started the conference. This is why the word “user” is selected instead of the “user account”.\\u0004The user was deleted":[""],"A text hint indicating that the layout can be configured only for SIP and H.323 endpoints. SIP (Session Initiation Protocol) and H.323 are the network protocols needed for audio and video communication via the Internet.\\u0004The layout settings are available only for SIP and H.323 endpoints":[""],"A text hint indicating that the server administrator can add a lecturer to the video conference. A lecturer is the only participant allowed to speak during a video meeting.\\u0004Add a lecturer or select from the participants who have already joined the meeting":[""],"A text hint indicating that the server administrator can customize the conference settings in any way he/she sees fit. There will be no fixed presets that cannot be changed.\\u0004No restrictions on conference customization ":[""],"A text hint indicating that the server receives video with a certain resolution from a participant. %WidthxHeight@%fps is a variable name that should not be translated.\\u0004Incoming resolution: %WidthxHeight@%fps":[""],"A text hint indicating that the server sends video with a certain resolution to a participant. %WidthxHeight@%fps is a variable name that should not be translated.\\u0004Outgoing resolution: %WidthxHeight@%fps":[""],"A text hint indicating that the user can drag and drop a file. Please note that this string should not be capitalized because it is only the second part of the sentence.\\u0004or just drag and drop it here":[""],"A text hint indicating that the video conferencing server receives audio with a certain bitrate from a participant. %n is a variable that should not be translated.\\u0004Incoming audio bitrate: %n":[""],"A text hint indicating that the video conferencing server receives video with a certain bitrate from a conference participant. %n is a variable that should not be translated.\\u0004Incoming video bitrate: %n":[""],"A text hint indicating that the video conferencing server sends audio with a certain bitrate to a participant. %n is a variable that should not be translated.\\u0004Outgoing audio bitrate: %n":[""],"A text hint indicating that the video conferencing server sends video with a certain bitrate to a conference participant. %n is a variable that should not be translated.\\u0004Outgoing video bitrate: %n":[""],"A text hint indicating that the video layout was created for only for 1 user. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username. So, do not replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004For “%DisplayName”":[""],"A text hint indicating that the video or audio file will be played on repeat.\\u0004Repeat playback is enabled":[""],"A text hint indicating that the video or audio file will not be played repeatedly.\\u0004Repeat playback is disabled":[""],"A text hint indicating that the video window will be used for displaying the participant who will be speaking at the moment.\\u0004Active speaker":[""],"A text hint indicating that there are no items on the list. This hint is intended to be used in multiple parts of the UI.\\u0004The list is empty":[""],"A text hint indicating that there are no items on the list. This hint will be used in different parts of the UI.\\u0004The list is empty":[""],"A text hint indicating that there are no participants in the video conference\\u0004No conference participants":[""],"A text hint indicating the number of the port used for connecting to the server. %n will be replaced with an integer. So, do not delete or edit this part of the phrase. The word “port” is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Port: %n":[""],"A text hint indicating when a user was last seen online. Please note that %DD:MM:YY will be replaced with the values for day, month, and year. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Last seen on %DD.MM.YY":[""],"A text hint indicating when a user was last seen online. Please note that %hh:mm will be replaced with values for hours and minutes. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Last seen at %hh:mm":[""],"A text hint indicating when the conference will be repeated on every selected date or (dates) of a month.  Please note that %selected_date will be replaced with digits corresponding to the selected dates.\\u0004every %selected_date date of a month":[""],"A text hint indicating when the conference will start\\u0004The conference will start in:":[""],"A text hint indicating when the password will expire (will no longer be valid). This hint is preceded by the phrase “the password will expire”. If the word “day” has multiple endings in the target language depending on the preceding numeral, please provide multiple translations of this phrase.\\u0004in %n day":["","in %n days","in %n days"],"A text hint indicating when the password will expire. These words are preceded by the phrase “the password will expire”. Here, we are talking about the password which is valid only for a certain time period.\\u0004today at %hh:mm":[""],"A text hint indicating when the password will expire. These words are preceded by the phrase “the password will expire”. Here, we are talking about the password which is valid only for a certain time period.\\u0004tomorrow at %hh:mm":[""],"A text hint indicating when the recurrence of a meeting will end. For example, a meeting can be held weekly on Tuesdays up until a certain date. The word “end” is used as a noun.\\u0004Recurrence end:":[""],"A text hint indicating when the recurrence of a meeting will start. For example, a meeting can be held weekly on Tuesdays starting from March 1. The word “start” is used as a noun.\\u0004Recurrence start:":[""],"A text hint on the conference web page. The hint will be followed by the actual conference name.\\u0004Conference name:":[""],"A text hint that can be used as a table column header or subheading. Here, one can check information about a certain event related to the work of a server (e.g., restart or shutdown). The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Event information":[""],"A text hint that will be displayed if a conference moderator either removes a participant from a video meeting or simply ends the invitation call before the user could accept it. This hint will be displayed in the table where the administrator can check information about the users who did not join the conference.\\u0004Session was ended by moderator":[""],"A text hint that will be displayed if a user either leaves a video meeting or just ends an outgoing call before a moderator can accept this call and allow the user to join the meeting. This hint will be displayed in the table where the administrator can check information about the users who did not join the conference.\\u0004Session was ended by participant":[""],"A text hint when the cursor is pointed to an icon.\\u0004Create a conference":[""],"A text hint when the cursor is pointed to an icon.\\u0004Delete a conference":[""],"A text hint when the cursor is pointed to an icon.\\u0004End conference":[""],"A text hint when the cursor is pointed to an icon.\\u0004Start conference":[""],"A text hint when the mouse cursor is pointed to the icon\\u0004Stop":[""],"A text hint which indicates that an audio file does not have a video track.\\u0004The video track is missing":[""],"A text hint which indicates that the name of a certain object is not being displayed in the video layout. Here, the word “name” may refer to a file name or a person’s name. If possible, try to find an equivalent that fits both cases.\\u0004The name is not displayed in the layout":[""],"A text hint. Here, one can check how much of the disk space is currently used.\\u0004Used":[""],"A text hint. Here, one can check the overall size of available disk space (storage). The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Total storage size":[""],"A text hint. Here, one can check the software version number after the update. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Version after update":[""],"A text hint. Here, one can check the software version number before the update. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Version before update":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are referring to the certificate and key used in HTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure).\\u0004The self-signed certificate and key are used":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are referring to the certificate used in HTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure). Please note that DD:MM:YYYY will be replaced with a date. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004The certificate expired on DD:MM:YYYY":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are referring to the certificate used in HTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure). Please note that DD:MM:YYYY will be replaced with a date. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004The certificate is valid until DD:MM:YYYY":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are referring to the network route (path across one or more networks). The word is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Route":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are talking about an audio or video codec. This codec cannot be used for the selected video conference. So, it cannot be used for participants who connect to this conference.\\u0004The codec is disabled for the conference and cannot be used for connection":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are talking about an audio or video codec. This codec is disabled in the global settings of the video conferencing server. Moreover, it is disabled for the selected conference. So, it cannot be used for a participant who connects to a video conference.\\u0004The codec is disabled globally and for the conference. It will not be used for connection":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are talking about an audio or video codec. This codec is disabled in the global settings of the video conferencing server. So, it cannot be used for a participant who connects to a video conference.\\u0004The codec is disabled globally, and cannot be used for conference connection":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are talking about the key needed for the HTTPS certificate.\\u0004Enter the password for the key":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are talking about the layout (arrangement of windows) created for a video conference.\\u0004The layout is changed automatically depending on the number of participants":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are talking about the layout of a video conference (arrangement of participants’ windows on the screen). The hint means that participants will be added to the layout automatically (if needed, they can be added manually).\\u0004The layout will be filled automatically":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are talking about the password which is valid only for a certain time period. The word “your” is used because we are talking about the user’s password and not someone else’s.\\u0004Your password will expire tomorrow at %hh:mm":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are talking about the unique identifier of a certain object.\\u0004ID":[""],"A text hint. Here, we are talking about the video layout for a conference. A layout is the arrangement of conference participants’ video windows on the screen. %n will be replaced with a number. Please, do not delete or edit this text variable.\\u0004Maximum number of participants in the layout — %n":[""],"A text hint. In this case, one of the meeting participants (%DisplayName) is constantly displayed in the layout. However, if the moderator changes the conference mode, this person may not be displayed in the layout or displayed in a smaller window. In the voice detection mode, the participant, who is speaking at the moment, is displayed either in an enlarged window or a fullscreen window. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004In the current mode “%DisplayName” is pinned in the layout. If the voice activity detection mode is enabled, the focus will be automatically shifted to the active speaker.":[""],"A text hint. The hint indicates that the user can join a video meeting from a desktop or mobile application.\\u0004Join from TrueConf client application":[""],"A text hint. This hint describes the cases when the display names of participants will become visible in the conference layout. The display names of all participants will become visible when one of the participants joins or leaves the conference or when the admin changes the layout (re-arranges video windows in some way). This sentence is made incomplete intentionally because the part about display names will be included in other parts of the UI.\\u0004When participants are connected/disconnected and when the layout is changed":[""],"A text hint. This hint may be followed either by the error code or error description. The word “error” is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Error":[""],"A text hint. This hint refers to an interval after which the conference should end automatically. For example, the conference should end automatically if no one joins for 10 or 15 minutes. Please note that the ending of the word “minute” will change dynamically depending on the preceding numeral. If there are multiple endings of this word in the target language, please provide several translations of this phrase.\\u0004minute":["","minutes"],"A text. Here, we are talking about the conference participants connected to an MCU (multi-point control unit).\\u0004The connected participant will receive the layout of this conference":[""],"A text. Here, we are talking about the conference participants connected to an MCU (multi-point control unit).\\u0004The participants will receive the layout of the connected conference":[""],"A time measure unit\\u0004%n day":["","%n days"],"A time measure unit\\u0004%n hour":["","%n hours"],"A time measure unit\\u0004%n minute":["","%n minutes"],"A time measure unit\\u0004%n month":["","%n months"],"A time measure unit\\u0004%n second":["","%n seconds"],"A time measure unit\\u0004%n week":["","%n weeks"],"A tooltip for a button. This button sends a file used for updating the firmware of a video conferencing endpoint. This file will be sent directly to the endpoint. The word “send” is used instead of “update” because the endpoint firmware will not be immediately updated.\\u0004Send update to endpoint":[""],"A tooltip for an icon button. If the button is clicked, the user will be able to see the characters of the password that he/she enters into the input field.\\u0004Show password":[""],"A tooltip for an icon button. If the button is clicked, the user will be unable to see the characters of the password that he/she enters into the input field.\\u0004Hide password":[""],"A tooltip for an icon button. If this button is clicked, the selected call address will be permanently displayed (pinned) in the contact list (in the small menu providing brief information about a user). Please note that a call address is a network address needed for making a call over IP networks, e,g., one can mention SIP or H.323 addresses. Here, we are using the word “pin” because a user may have multiple call addresses, but only one of them can be displayed. In this context, pinning an address is similar to pinning a message in the chat.\\u0004Pin the user address in the contact list":[""],"A tooltip. The hint indicates that a conference participant will be able to play the audio track of a file when sharing content during a meeting.\\u0004Audio is enabled":[""],"A tooltip. The hint indicates that a conference participant will not be able to play the audio track of a file when sharing content. However, he/she may be able to show the video stream.\\u0004Audio is disabled":[""],"A tooltip. The hint indicates that the video file will not be played as soon as the conference starts. Here, we are talking about content sharing during a conference. A user can share images, slides, and video files during the meeting.\\u0004Playback upon conference start is disabled":[""],"A tooltip. This hint indicates that the video file will be played as soon as the conference starts. Here, we are talking about content sharing during a conference. A user can share images, slides, and video files during the meeting.\\u0004Playback upon conference start is enabled":[""],"A type of a conference. In this conference, each of the participants will be seen and heard by other users as soon as he/she starts speaking.\\u0004Speaker mode":[""],"A type of a conference. In this conference, each of the participants will be seen and heard by other users as soon as he/she starts speaking. Only one participant can be speaking at the moment. Nominative case.\\u0004Speaker":[""],"A type of a video conference in which there are no fixed presets, and the admin can customize the settings in any way depending on the event type and participants’ needs.\\u0004General mode":[""],"A widget header\\u0004Hard disk":[""],"A widget header\\u0004RAM":[""],"Abbreviations for weekdays.\\u0004Fri":[""],"Abbreviations for weekdays.\\u0004Mon":[""],"Abbreviations for weekdays.\\u0004Sat":[""],"Abbreviations for weekdays.\\u0004Sun":[""],"Abbreviations for weekdays.\\u0004Thu":[""],"Abbreviations for weekdays.\\u0004Tue":[""],"Abbreviations for weekdays.\\u0004Wed":[""],"Additional Information about server events. Here you can find the сonference ID where the event occurred.\\u0004Conference ID":[""],"Additional Information about server events. Here you can find the name of the conference where the event occurred.\\u0004Conference":[""],"Additional Information about server events. Here you can find the reason for the failed authorization with the error name.\\u0004Reason for non-authorization":[""],"Administration statistic subheader\\u0004Network":[""],"An error message\\u0004An error occurred while installing the update":[""],"An error message\\u0004An error occurred while uploading the file":[""],"An error message\\u0004Incorrect old password":[""],"An error message\\u0004Login already exists":[""],"An error message\\u0004The password does not meet security requirements":[""],"An error message\\u0004The passwords do not match":[""],"An error message\\u0004This field has to be filled":[""],"An error message displayed  when the server administrator tries to start a video conference. The message indicates that there is a license limit on the number of conferences that can be held at the same time. Please note that %n will be replaced with a number; so, not delete or replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004Unable to start the conference. The maximum number of active conferences in the current license:  %n":[""],"An error message displayed if the uploaded file exceeds the maximum size.\\u0004File size cannot be larger than 100kb":[""],"An error message displayed if there is an incorrect value in the input field.\\u0004Input value has to be an even number":[""],"An error message displayed if there is an incorrect value in the input field.\\u0004Input value is greater than the maximum limit":[""],"An error message displayed if there is an incorrect value in the input field.\\u0004Input value is less than the minimum limit":[""],"An error message displayed to a server administrator. Here, we are talking about a  video conference. The admin can export information about this event, e.g. its start time or the number of participants. The word “occurred” is omitted because this text is not a notification, but an event type.\\u0004An error while exporting the  history of a conference":[""],"An error message displayed to a server administrator. Here, we are talking about the application which enables administrators to connect one video conference to another.\\u0004An error occurred while adding conferences":[""],"An error message displayed to a server administrator. Here, we are talking about the application which enables administrators to connect one video conference to another.\\u0004An error occurred while adding the conference":[""],"An error message displayed to a user if he/she does not have the permission to view a certain web page page.\\u0004Error 403":[""],"An error message displayed to a user if he/she does not have the permission to view a certain web page page.\\u0004Not enough rights to view this page. Please contact your server administrator.":[""],"An error message displayed to a user when he/she fills out a form. The error message will be displayed if the values specified in two fields are identical (even though they cannot match).\\u0004The values in the fields cannot match":[""],"An error message displayed to an admin.\\u0004Installation error":[""],"An error message displayed to an administrator when he/she tries to change the password and the new password is identical to the old password.\\u0004The new password must not match the old password":[""],"An error message displayed to the administrator if the version of the database is not compatible with the application.\\u0004Incompatible version of the database":[""],"An error message displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server. It is displayed when the invited number of participants is larger than the maximum number of participants in a conference.\\u0004This action is unavailable. The maximum number of participants has been reached":[""],"An error message displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server. It is displayed when the invited number of participants is larger than the maximum number of participants in a conference. Please note that in this case, the admin tries to add participants via such network protocols as SIP (Session Initiation Protocol) and H.323.\\u0004SIP/H.323 participants cannot be added. The maximum number of connections has been reached":[""],"An error message displayed to the administrator when he/she uploads several files on the server.. Some of these files (more than two) could not be uploaded because their format is not supported. %n will be replaced with a number of files. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Unable to upload several files (%n). The format is not supported":[""],"An error message displayed to the administrator. Calibration is the process aimed at determining the most optimal configuration for a software solution depending on hardware parameters of the machine. The word “stop” is used instead of “end” because this process was stopped before it could be completed. This error message will be displayed if the admin tries to abort the calibration when this process has already been stopped by someone else. The term “calibration” is already used in the UI. Please check how this phrase was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004Calibration has already been aborted":[""],"An error message displayed to the administrator. Here, we are talking about the video rendering engine.\\u0004No connection with the engine":[""],"An error message displayed to the administrator. Here, we are talking about the video rendering engine. The noun “error” is used in the nominative case. This text hint can also be used as a filter for the list of errors.\\u0004Engine error":[""],"An error message displayed to the server administrator\\u0004Failed to connect to the server":[""],"An error message displayed to the server administrator when he/she creates a video conference. The admin is asked to select at least one audio codec, otherwise the meeting will not be created (saved).\\u0004Select an audio codec to save the conference":[""],"An error message displayed to the server administrator when he/she creates a video conference. The admin is asked to select at least one video codec, otherwise the meeting will not be created (saved).\\u0004Select a video codec to save the conference":[""],"An error message displayed to the server administrator when he/she tries to send conference invitations to the participants of a video meeting.\\u0004Unable to send invitations. A database error occurred":[""],"An error message displayed to the server administrator when he/she tries to send conference invitations to the participants of a video meeting.\\u0004Unable to send invitations. An error occurred while connecting to the mail server":[""],"An error message displayed to the server administrator when he/she tries to send conference invitations to the participants of a video meeting. To send invitations to users, the application should be able to authorize on the mail server.\\u0004Unable to send invitations. An error occurred while authorizing on the mail server":[""],"An error message displayed to the server administrator.\\u0004An error occurred while importing the database":[""],"An error message displayed to the server administrator.  Calibration is the process aimed at determining the most optimal configuration for a software solution depending on hardware parameters of the machine. This error message will be displayed if the admin tries to start the calibration when it has already been started by someone else. The term “calibration” is already used in the UI. Please check how this phrase was previously translated into the target language.\\u0004Calibration has already started":[""],"An error message displayed to the server administrator. Here, we are talking about a network port used for connection. This port can be used by a different application.\\u0004The port is already used":[""],"An error message displayed to the server administrator. Here, we are talking about the error which occurs when the firmware or configuration update is sent to a video conferencing endpoint. Please note that %TerminalName will be replaced with the name of the endpoint. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004An error occurred while sending the update to the endpoint “%TerminalName”":[""],"An error message displayed to the server administrator. Here, we are talking about the error which occurs when the firmware or configuration update is sent to multiple video conferencing endpoints. %n will be replaced with a number. Do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004An error occurred while sending updates to multiple (%n) endpoints":[""],"An error message displayed to the system administrator when he/she tries to upload a file whose format is not supported. Please preserve %filename without translation. This part of the string will later be substituted with the actual file name.\\u0004Unable to upload the “%filename” file. This format is not supported":[""],"An error message displayed to the system administrator when he/she tries to upload a file whose format is not supported. Please preserve %name without translation. This part of the string will later be substituted with the actual file name.\\u0004Unable to upload the “%name” file. This format is not supported":[""],"An error message displayed when a user tries to delete a certain object. It may be a user account or a role (a set of rights and permissions). There is no noun after “delete” because the message will be displayed in several situations. This message will not be displayed in case of some internal error. Its purpose is to indicate that the user is trying to do something that cannot be done by the application, e.g., if a user tries to delete his/her own account. This is why “unable” was used instead of “failed”.\\u0004Unable to delete":[""],"An error message displayed when an administrator tries to export certain data.\\u0004An error occurred while exporting data":[""],"An error message displayed when the admin is saving changes.\\u0004An error occurred while saving changes":[""],"An error message displayed when the administrator tries to import a database. The message indicates that the file cannot be used for import.\\u0004The file cannot be used for import.":[""],"An error message displayed when the administrator tries to send email invitations to the participants of a video meeting.\\u0004An error occurred while sending invitations":[""],"An error message displayed when the administrator uploads an incorrect license file (with incorrect extension).\\u0004This file format is not supported, please use the .mrg format":[""],"An error message displayed when the application cannot preview video from a participant’s camera.\\u0004Failed to start preview":[""],"An error message displayed when the server administrator deletes data from the server.\\u0004An error occurred while deleting data":[""],"An error message displayed when the server administrator tries to edit the information about the selected user. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username. So, do not delete or replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004An error occurred while editing the user \\"%DisplayName\\"":[""],"An error message displayed when uploading multiple files. The hint indicates that a certain number of files (%n) could not be uploaded because their file name is longer than the maximum limit.\\u0004Unable to upload %n file. The maximum file name length has been exceeded":["","Unable to upload %n files. The maximum file name length has been exceeded"],"An error message indicating that the ID (identifier of a virtual meeting) entered by the administrator has already been taken (occupied).\\u0004This ID is already in use":[""],"An error message indicating that the ID (identifier of a virtual meeting) entered by the administrator has already been taken (occupied).\\u0004This route is already in use":[""],"An error message.\\u0004An error occurred while exporting the database":[""],"An error message.\\u0004Page not found":[""],"An error message.\\u0004The schedule already exists":[""],"An error message. A .deb file is a package format used in Debian and Debian-based Linux distributions.\\u0004The deb package file was not found":[""],"An error message. Here, the problem is that the archived data could not be unpacked (extracted). The noun \\"error\\" is used in the nominative case. This text hint can also be used as a filter for the list of errors.\\u0004Archive extraction error":[""],"An error message. Here, we are referring to the certificate and key used in HTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure).\\u0004The key does not match the certificate":[""],"An error message. Here, we are talking about directories in Linux.\\u0004Incorrect directory type":[""],"An error message. Here, we are talking about the key needed for the correct work of the HTTPS protocol. There is a password for this key.\\u0004Invalid key password":[""],"An error message. In this case, the word “address” refers to the address needed for making a call over the Internet, e.g., an SIP or H.323 address (SIP and H.323 are network protocols). The string indicates that the address cannot be entered into the input field because it has already been occupied (taken) by one of the users.\\u0004Address is already taken":[""],"An error message. It will be displayed if the archive could be opened and extracted, however, it includes some invalid content (e.g., the file or files with invalid extensions). This text hint can also be used as a filter for the list of errors.\\u0004Invalid archive content":[""],"An error message. MCU stands for multipoint control unit. It is a device or software solution used for connecting multiple video conferencing endpoints. The administrator can import various types of data, e.g. configurations, user accounts, etc. Here, the problem is that imported data is not suitable for the current version of the MCU.\\u0004Imported data is incompatible with the current MCU version":[""],"An error message. This message will be displayed if a user’s password includes his/her login (this is a potential security vulnerability).\\u0004The password cannot include the login":[""],"An input field\\u0004Current IP":[""],"An input field\\u0004Display Name":[""],"An input field\\u0004Gateway":[""],"An input field\\u0004IP address":[""],"An input field\\u0004Port":[""],"An input field\\u0004Primary DNS":[""],"An input field\\u0004Secondary DNS":[""],"An input field\\u0004Subnet mask":[""],"An input field \\u0004Hostname":[""],"An input field \\u0004Password":[""],"An input field \\u0004Username":[""],"An item on the drop-down list\\u0004Address book first":[""],"An item on the drop-down list\\u0004Auto":[""],"An item on the drop-down list\\u0004Balanced":[""],"An item on the drop-down list\\u0004Default":[""],"An item on the drop-down list\\u0004Documents":[""],"An item on the drop-down list\\u0004Gatekeeper first":[""],"An item on the drop-down list\\u0004Motion":[""],"An item on the drop-down list\\u0004Movies":[""],"An item on the drop-down list\\u0004Narrator":[""],"An item on the drop-down list\\u0004Resolution":[""],"An item on the drop-down list\\u0004Slideshow":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Audio processing delay:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Audio processing state:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Calibrated codec:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Current resource usage (enc/dec):":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Encoder resource limit:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Max number of displayed participants":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Maximum number of active connections":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004MCU calibration progress:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Regular queue memory usage:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Regular queue messages:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Required resources (enc/dec):":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Scheduled jobs queue:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Urgent queue memory usage:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Urgent queue messages:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Video processing state:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Worker thread count:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Worker thread occupancy:":[""],"An item on the list\\u0004Worker thread overhead:":[""],"An item on the list.\\u0004License agreement":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004All available disc space":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Call details":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Disable conference audio":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Do not show conference video to participant":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Enable conference audio":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Hide participant’s video":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Mute":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Remove":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Show conference video to participant":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Show participant’s video":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Tone dialing (DTMF)":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Unmute":[""],"An option in the context menu\\u0004Volume control":[""],"An option in the context menu for a video/audio file. It will open the media player. The file will be played repeatedly (looped).\\u0004Play on repeat":[""],"An option in the context menu or a button. If this button is clicked, the image (picture) will not be shown to conference participants.\\u0004Hide image":[""],"An option in the context menu or a button. This button is needed for disabling a video stream, e.g., from a conference participant or from a video file.\\u0004Disable video":[""],"An option in the context menu or a button. This button is needed for enabling a video stream, e.g., from a conference participant or from a video file.\\u0004Enable video":[""],"An option in the context menu or a button. This button is needed for showing an image to other conference participants.\\u0004Show image":[""],"An option in the context menu, If this option is selected, the application will not play the file (audio or video) on repeat.\\u0004Do not repeat":[""],"An option in the context menu. Here, the admin can choose what type of encryption and certificate should be used for secure connection with the SMTP. In this case, SSL (secure sockets layer) will be used.\\u0004SSL":[""],"An option in the context menu. Here, the admin can choose what type of encryption and certificate should be used for secure connection with the SMTP. Please note that STARTTLS stand for Start TLS (transport layer security). The main peculiarity of this approach is that if TLS encryption is supported on both sides, data will be encrypted, otherwise, data will be transferred in plain text.\\u0004STARTTLS":[""],"An option in the context menu. Here, the admin can choose what type of encryption method and certificate should be used for secure connection with the SMTP server. In this case, no certificate and encryption will be used.\\u0004Don’t use":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected the file will be moved from one conference to another. This file will be used for content sharing during this conference.\\u0004Move file":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, a user will be able to share the audio track from a file with other conference participants.\\u0004Enable audio track":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, a user will not be able to share the audio track from a file with other conference participants. However, he/she can share the video stream from a file.\\u0004Disable audio track":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, participants will be sorted by the time when they joined the virtual meeting. The participants, who have joined the meeting most recently will come first.\\u0004Connection / disconnection time (recent first)":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, participants will be sorted by the time when they joined the virtual meeting. The participants, who have joined the meeting most recently will come first.\\u0004Connection time (newest to oldest)":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, participants will be sorted by the time when they joined the virtual meeting. The participants, who joined the meeting earlier, will come first.\\u0004Connection / disconnection time (old first)":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, participants will be sorted by the time when they joined the virtual meeting. The participants, who joined the meeting earlier, will come first.\\u0004Connection time (oldest to newest)":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, participants’ names will always be displayed during a video meeting.\\u0004Always display":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, participants’ names will not be displayed during a video meeting.\\u0004Do not display":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, the application will display the names of users instead of group names.\\u0004Users":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, the application will not play the video file when the conference starts.\\u0004Don’t play upon conference start":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, the application will play the selected file (audio or video) as soon as the conference starts.\\u0004Play upon conference start":[""],"An option in the context menu. If this option is selected, the applications will display the names of groups instead of group names.\\u0004Groups":[""],"An option in the context menu. In this case “move” means that a participant will be moved from one ongoing meeting to another (up to 34 characters including spaces)\\u0004Move participant":[""],"An option in the context menu. In this case, the word channel refers to an audio channel used during a video meeting (an audio channel is a group of participants who can send and receive audio from each other).\\u0004New channel":[""],"An option in the context menu. This option allows the administrator to sort the names of meeting participants in direct alphabetical order (from A to Z).\\u0004From A to Z":[""],"An option in the context menu. This option allows the administrator to sort the names of meeting participants in reverse alphabetical order (from Z to A).\\u0004From Z to A":[""],"An option in the drop-down list\\u0004Always":[""],"An option in the drop-down list\\u0004Never":[""],"An option in the drop-down list\\u0004Use default settings":[""],"An option in the drop-down list for adjusting video quality for a stream. If this option is selected, the delay during a video stream will be reduced to the minimum. However, the video quality may degrade.\\u0004Minimum delay":[""],"An option in the drop-down list needed for adjusting video quality.\\u0004Maximum quality":[""],"An option in the drop-down list needed for configuring SIP (Session Initiation Protocol) and H.323 encryption settings. SIP and H.323 are voice-over-Internet protocols needed for audio and video communication. If this option is selected, it will be impossible to make a call to a video conferencing endpoint where SIP/H.323 encryption is enabled.\\u0004No encryption":[""],"An option in the drop-down list needed for configuring SIP (Session Initiation Protocol) and H.323 encryption settings. SIP and H.323 are voice-over-Internet protocols needed for audio and video communication. If this option is selected, SIP/H.323 encryption will be used only if it is permitted by the user of a remote video conferencing endpoint. Please don’t mention “user” in your translation because a more detailed explanation of this feature will be given in a separate guide.\\u0004Encrypt when possible":[""],"An option in the drop-down list needed for configuring SIP (Session Initiation Protocol) and H.323 encryption settings. SIP and H.323 are voice-over-Internet protocols needed for audio and video communication. This option makes SIP/H.323 encryption mandatory. It will be impossible to make a call to a video conferencing endpoint where SIP/H.323 encryption is disabled.\\u0004Encrypt all":[""],"An option in the drop-down list.\\u0004Monthly":[""],"An option in the drop-down list.\\u0004Use default settings":[""],"An option in the drop-down list.\\u0004Weekly":[""],"An option in the drop-down list.  This list will be needed for selecting if the video from a user’s camera may be displayed. If this option is selected, the server will automatically decide if the self-view video may be displayed or or not.\\u0004Automatically":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. A log level or log severity is the piece of information that tells how important a given log message is. If this option is selected, the information about log level will be included when logs are displayed.\\u0004Include log level":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. A logging level or log severity is the piece of information that tells how important a given log message is. If this option is selected, the information about the log level will be excluded when logs will be displayed.\\u0004Exclude log level":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. H.323 is a network protocol used for audio and video communication over the Internet.\\u0004Use H.323":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. Here the administrator will choose if the application should display conference participants’ names in the video layout. If the Auto option is selected, the application will automatically determine if participants’ names should be displayed or not. For example, it may depend on the number of windows in the layout.\\u0004Auto":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. Here, the admin is supposed to select a time interval. This time interval is needed for determining how a chart will be displayed (the scale of this chat). If this option is selected, the chart will be reduced to the minimum so that it can fit all the period during measurements were made.\\u0004All time":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. Here, the administrator can select when the conference should end automatically. The admin can select one of the default options such as 10 or 15 minutes. However, the admin can set a custom period.\\u0004Custom":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. If this option is selected, a participant will not be called when a video conference starts. He/she may join the meeting later (up to 36 characters including spaces).\\u0004Don’t call upon the  conference start":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. If this option is selected, a participant will receive an invitation call when a video conference starts (up to 36 characters including spaces).\\u0004Call upon the conference start":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. If this option is selected, the application will not make an invitation call to participants at the beginning of the conference.\\u0004Don’t call participants":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. If this option is selected, the user will be able to see the video from his/her camera in the video layout during a meeting. This word is the shortened version of the phrase “display the self-view”. The word “self-view” should not be included in the translation because it will be mentioned in other parts of the GUI.\\u0004Display":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. If this option is selected, the user will not be able to see the self-view (video from his/her camera) in the layout during a video meeting. This word is the shortened version of the phrase “don’t display the self-view”. The word “self-view” should not be included in the translation because it will be mentioned in other parts of the GUI.\\u0004Don’t display for all":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. If this option is selected, there will be no restrictions on the video bitrate received by a participant.\\u0004No limits":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. In this case “capture” refers to network traffic capture. The administrator may capture traffic from one of the network interfaces. “Capture all” means that the traffic will be captured from all interfaces.\\u0004Capture all":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. In this list, the admin can choose for how long a user’s account should be blocked.\\u0004%n hour":["","%n hours"],"An option in the drop-down list. In this list, the admin can choose for how long a user’s account should be blocked.\\u0004%n minute":["","%n minutes"],"An option in the drop-down list. SIP (Session Initiation Protocol) and H.323 are network protocols used for audio communication over the Internet. If this option is selected, the application will use both SIP and H.323.\\u0004Use SIP/H.323":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. This drop-down list is needed for selecting the quality of video recordings. If this option is selected, the quality of video recording will be relatively high, but it will be reduced to some degree. This option will be needed to minimize the size of video recordings.\\u0004Optimal":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. This drop-down list is needed for selecting the quality of video recordings. If this option is selected, the quality of video recording will be relatively low. This option is needed for keeping the size of recordings as low as possible.\\u0004Minimum size":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. This drop-down list is needed for selecting the quality of video recordings. This option guarantees the highest quality of video recordings.\\u0004Highest":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. This option is needed for selecting when a conference should end automatically. For example, the conference may end automatically if no one joins it for 1, 5, 10, or 15 minutes.\\u00041 minute":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. This option is needed for selecting when a conference should end automatically. For example, the conference may end automatically if no one joins it for 1, 5, 10, or 15 minutes.\\u000410 minutes":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. This option is needed for selecting when a conference should end automatically. For example, the conference may end automatically if no one joins it for 1, 5, 10, or 15 minutes.\\u000415 minutes":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. This option is needed for selecting when a conference should end automatically. For example, the conference may end automatically if no one joins it for 1, 5, 10, or 15 minutes.\\u00045 minutes":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. This option may be used in multiple cases. It will be needed for the default value used in the server settings.\\u0004Use default value":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. When selected, automatic gain control (AGC) is disabled.\\u0004Disable AGC":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. When selected, automatic gain control (AGC) is enabled.\\u0004Enable AGC":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. When selected, noise cancellation is disabled.\\u0004Disable noise cancellation":[""],"An option in the drop-down list. When selected, noise cancellation is enabled.\\u0004Enable noise cancellation":[""],"An option in the drop-down menu. The administrator can configure layout settings for a video conference. If this option is selected, the current speaker will not see his/her video in an enlarged window. Please note that these settings do not affect how other users will see the speaker. They can see this person in the enlarged window.\\u0004Do not display in enlarged window":[""],"An option in the menu\\u0004Administration":[""],"An option in the menu\\u0004Conferences":[""],"An option is selected, SIP (Session Initiation Protocol) is a network protocol used for audio and video communication over the Internet.\\u0004Use SIP":[""],"Button\\u0004Add":[""],"Button\\u0004Add a color":[""],"Button\\u0004Apply":[""],"Button\\u0004Back":[""],"Button\\u0004Cancel":[""],"Button\\u0004Check equipment":[""],"Button\\u0004Continue":[""],"Button\\u0004Create":[""],"Button\\u0004Create a license file":[""],"Button\\u0004Delete":[""],"Button\\u0004Get a FREE Key":[""],"Button\\u0004Next":[""],"Button\\u0004Ok":[""],"Button\\u0004Re-register":[""],"Button\\u0004Reboot":[""],"Button\\u0004Register":[""],"Button\\u0004Remove":[""],"Button\\u0004Reset":[""],"Button\\u0004Restart MCU":[""],"Button\\u0004Restart OS":[""],"Button\\u0004Save":[""],"Button\\u0004Shut down the server":[""],"Button\\u0004Sign in":[""],"Button\\u0004Start calibration":[""],"Button\\u0004Stop":[""],"Button\\u0004Try again":[""],"Button\\u0004Upload a file":[""],"Button\\u0004Upload the file":[""],"Button\\u0004Validate":[""],"Button\\u0004View":[""],"Button name. This button allows you to add a user to the participant list and connect them to the conference.\\u0004Connect to the conference":[""],"Button name.This button allows you to add a user to the conference without connecting them.\\u0004Add without connecting":[""],"Button. Enables you to display  more contacts in the address book.\\u0004Show more":[""],"Calibration is a process aimed at determining the optimal settings for a software solution depending on the hardware parameters of the computer. Here, the admin tries to abort this process before it can end automatically. However, a certain error occurs. This text hint can be used as an error description and as a checkbox needed for filtering the list of errors. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Calibration abort error":[""],"Calibration is a process aimed at determining the optimal settings for a software solution depending on the hardware parameters of the computer. This text can be used as an error description and as a checkbox needed for filtering the list of errors. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Calibration start error":[""],"Card displaying the information about the chosen contact\\u0004Layout name":[""],"Checkbox\\u0004Adaptive bitrate":[""],"Checkbox\\u0004Allow users to share content":[""],"Checkbox\\u0004Always route H.323 calls through the gatekeeper":[""],"Checkbox\\u0004Always route SIP calls through the registration server":[""],"Checkbox\\u0004Block spam calls":[""],"Checkbox\\u0004Far-end camera control (H.281)":[""],"Checkbox\\u0004Forward error correction":[""],"Checkbox\\u0004Registration":[""],"Checkbox\\u0004Show particpant placeholder":[""],"Checkbox\\u0004Use the gatekeeper":[""],"Checkbox\\u0004Video traffic shaping":[""],"Checkbox in the menu for creating and editing a conference.\\u0004Show a volume bar":[""],"Column header\\u0004Action":[""],"Column header\\u0004Additional":[""],"Column header\\u0004Participant’s name and address":[""],"Column header\\u0004Settings":[""],"Column header\\u0004Size":[""],"Column header \\u0004Participant’s name and address":[""],"Column header. Here the administrator can find the list of network interfaces.\\u0004Network interface":[""],"Conference PIN or a PIN code of a virtual meeting.\\u0004PIN: %n":[""],"Connection to registration server\\u0004Connection to the registration server":[""],"Connection to registration server\\u0004Not required":[""],"Connection to registration server\\u0004Required":[""],"Description\\u0004Content bandwidth":[""],"Description\\u0004Status:":[""],"Description\\u0004Transport protocol":[""],"Dialog notification\\u0004All progress will be lost.":[""],"Dialog notification\\u0004Do you want to perform MCU calibration?":[""],"Dialog notification\\u0004Do you want to stop calibration?":[""],"Dialog notification\\u0004MCU calibration will stop all active conferences.":[""],"Drop-down list\\u0004Call sequence":[""],"Drop-down list\\u0004Primary video profile":[""],"Drop-down list\\u0004Protocol priority":[""],"Drop-down list\\u0004Secondary video profile":[""],"Drop-down list \\u0004BFCP transport protocol":[""],"Error\\u0004You cannot select a past date":[""],"Error message\\u0004An error occurred while saving settings":[""],"Error message\\u0004An unknown error":[""],"Error message\\u0004Enter login":[""],"Error message\\u0004Enter password":[""],"Error message\\u0004File generation error":[""],"Error message\\u0004Incorrect format":[""],"Error message\\u0004Incorrect password":[""],"Error message\\u0004Invalid PIN":[""],"Error message\\u0004Please enter at least %n character":["","Please enter at least %n characters"],"Error message\\u0004Please enter at least %n characters":[""],"Error message\\u0004Please enter at least 5 characters":[""],"Error message\\u0004Please enter no more than %n character":["","Please enter no more than %n characters"],"Error message\\u0004Please enter no more than %n characters":[""],"Error message\\u0004Please select a day for recurrence":[""],"Error message\\u0004This day has already been selected":[""],"Error message\\u0004This time slot is already occupied":[""],"fuzzy\\u0004Error User Already Has Credentials":[""],"fuzzy\\u0004None":[""],"Group edit display name placeholder\\u0004Group name":[""],"Group for users that do not participate in any other groups\\u0004No group":[""],"Header\\u0004Conferences":[""],"Header\\u0004Content sharing":[""],"Header\\u0004Copy a conference":[""],"Header\\u0004Copy session to conference":[""],"Header\\u0004Groups":[""],"Header\\u0004History":[""],"Header\\u0004Internet connection is required":[""],"Header\\u0004Language":[""],"Header\\u0004License Agreement":[""],"Header\\u0004License Renewal":[""],"Header\\u0004MCU calibration":[""],"Header\\u0004Power":[""],"Header\\u0004Users":[""],"Header\\u0004Welcome to %trueconf_mcu guest page":[""],"Header\\u0004Welcome to TrueConf MCU Activation Page":[""],"Here, we are talking about the network address needed for joining a conference. A user can enter this address in the application (desktop or mobile). Secondly, one can enter it in the UI of a video conferencing endpoint. The word “address” is omitted because it is used in a different part of the UI.\\u0004Enter in the call line of your application or endpoint":[""],"Hint\\u0004Enable custom settings":[""],"Hint\\u0004Free":[""],"Hint\\u0004Used":[""],"Hint\\u0004Used (Gb)":[""],"Hint\\u0004Using":[""],"Input box\\u0004Gatekeeper address":[""],"Input box\\u0004H.323 Alias":[""],"Input box\\u0004H.323 Extension":[""],"Input box\\u0004Login":[""],"Input box\\u0004Password":[""],"Input field\\u0004Enter the address":[""],"Input field\\u0004MAC address":[""],"Input field\\u0004System name":[""],"Layout type\\u0004Active speaker":[""],"Layout type\\u0004For all participants":[""],"Layout type\\u0004Individual layout":[""],"Message\\u0004Registration has been successful":[""],"Message shown when the search gave no results\\u0004No matches found":[""],"ne of the options for configuring the schedule of a conference. A cron expression is a method for creating a very flexible schedule for a conference.\\u0004Cron-expression":[""],"no context\\u0004File name:":[""],"no context\\u0004No listeners":[""],"no string context or value\\u0004Listeners":[""],"Non-recurring means a conference will be held only once.\\u0004Do not repeat":[""],"Notification\\u0004Your changes have been saved":[""],"One of the menu options used for filtering the list of video conferencing endpoints.  If this option is selected, the application will display only offline video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004Offline":[""],"One of the menu options used for filtering the list of video conferencing endpoints. If this option is selected, the application will display only those video conferencing endpoints that are currently online.\\u0004Online":[""],"One of the menu options used for filtering the list of video conferencing endpoints. If this option is selected, the list will not be filtered.\\u0004Show all":[""],"One of the options for a filter. If this option is selected, the app will display all video conferences.\\u0004All conferences":[""],"One of the options for a filter. If this option is selected, the app will display only the conferences created by the user.\\u0004My conferences only":[""],"One of the options for configuring the schedule of a conference. For example, the conference can be held daily, weekly, or monthly.\\u0004Daily":[""],"One of the options for configuring the schedule of a conference. For example, the conference can be held daily, weekly, or monthly.\\u0004Monthly":[""],"One of the options for configuring the schedule of a conference. For example, the conference can be held daily, weekly, or monthly.\\u0004Weekly":[""],"One of the options for configuring the schedule of a conference. If this option is selected,  the conference will be held only once.\\u0004Do not repeat":[""],"One of the options in the context menu. If this option is selected, the participants will be sorted in alphabetical order.\\u0004Alphabetically (A-Z)":[""],"One of the options in the context menu. If this option is selected, the participants will be sorted in reverse alphabetical order.\\u0004Alphabetically (Z-A)":[""],"One of the options in the drop-down list. Here, one can configure settings for calling participants at the beginning of a conference. If this option is selected, the call will be made only to the participants added to the address book.\\u0004Call only participants from address book":[""],"One of the options in the drop-down list. Here, the admin can configure the settings for calling users at the beginning of a conference. If this option is selected, the application will make a call only to the participants who were connected with the help of their network address (e.g., SIP or H.323 addresses). However, they were not added to the conference from the address book.\\u0004Call only participants connected by address":[""],"One of the options in the drop-down list. Here, the admin can select a time interval. In this case, the word “day” is abbreviated to the first letter. If possible, keep the translation as short as possible. However, if the rules of the target language require a longer abbreviation, feel free to use it.\\u00041d":[""],"One of the options in the drop-down list. Here, the admin can select a time interval. In this case, the word “hour” is abbreviated to the first letter. If possible, keep the translation as short as possible. However, if the rules of the target language require a longer abbreviation, feel free to use it.\\u00041h":[""],"One of the options in the drop-down list. Here, the admin can select a time interval. In this case, the word “hour” is abbreviated to the first letter. If possible, keep the translation as short as possible. However, if the rules of the target language require a longer abbreviation, feel free to use it.\\u00046h":[""],"One of the options in the drop-down list. Here, the admin can select a time interval. In this case, the word “minute” is abbreviated to the first letter. If possible, keep the translation as short as possible. However, if the rules of the target language require a longer abbreviation, feel free to use it.\\u000410m":[""],"One of the options in the drop-down list. Here, the admin can select a time interval. In this case, the word “minute” is abbreviated to the first letter. If possible, keep the translation as short as possible. However, if the rules of the target language require a longer abbreviation, feel free to use it.\\u000430m":[""],"One of the options in the drop-down list. Here, the admin can select a time interval. In this case, the word “minute” is abbreviated to the first letter. If possible, keep the translation as short as possible. However, if the rules of the target language require a longer abbreviation, feel free to use it.\\u00045m":[""],"One of the options in the drop-down list. If this option is selected, the applications will call all participants when the conference starts.\\u0004Call all participants":[""],"One of the radio buttons. If this option is selected, the administrator will export the entire database. It is also possible to export certain parts of the database (the second radio button).\\u0004Export entire database":[""],"One of the subheadings in the menu that provides information about a recurring video conference. The meeting can be held daily, weekly, monthly etc.\\u0004Schedule:":[""],"One of the subheadings in the menu that provides information about a recurring video meeting. Here, the admin can check the date or day when the meeting is going to be repeated.\\u0004Next session:":[""],"One of the subheadings in the menu that provides information about a video conference. ID is the unique identifier of a meeting.\\u0004ID:":[""],"One of the subheadings in the menu that provides information about a video meeting. A conference join page is a web page needed for joining a conference from a browser.\\u0004Conference join page:":[""],"One of the subheadings in the menu where the admin can select what kind of information should be saved when the database will be exported. “Other” is an umbrella term for those types of information that could not fit any category.\\u0004Other":[""],"Output field\\u0004Result":[""],"Participants receiving audio\\u0004Attendees":[""],"Participants sending audio\\u0004Presenters":[""],"Personal data table\\u0004Action":[""],"Personal data table\\u0004Actions":[""],"Personal data table\\u0004Date and time":[""],"Personal data table\\u0004File name":[""],"Personal data table\\u0004Size":[""],"Personal data table\\u0004Type":[""],"PIN field hint\\u0004Enter conference PIN":[""],"Pop-up header\\u0004Volume control for “%DisplayName”":[""],"Popup header\\u0004Tone dialing (DTMF)":[""],"Radio button\\u0004Green":[""],"Radio button\\u0004Silver":[""],"Radio button\\u0004Turquoise":[""],"Radio button\\u0004Violet":[""],"Radio buttons\\u0004DHCP":[""],"Radio buttons\\u0004Static":[""],"Registration button\\u0004Register":[""],"Removes a user from the list of chosen participants\\u0004Remove":[""],"Section\\u0004Access management":[""],"Section\\u0004Info":[""],"Section\\u0004Personalization":[""],"Section\\u0004Receivers":[""],"Section\\u0004Security":[""],"Section subheading. In this section, the server administrator can configure settings that will apply to all participants.\\u0004Conference participants":[""],"Session PIN or a PIN code of a virtual meeting.\\u0004PIN: %n":[""],"Software version\\u0004TrueConf MCU version":[""],"Sort\\u0004Alphabetically (A-Z)":[""],"Sort\\u0004Alphabetically (Z-A)":[""],"Sort\\u0004By start time":[""],"Status\\u0004Address unspecified":[""],"Status\\u0004Registered":[""],"Status\\u0004Unregistered":[""],"Sub-heading\\u0004Audio settings":[""],"Sub-heading\\u0004Conference participants settings":[""],"Sub-heading\\u0004Layout skin styles":[""],"Sub-heading\\u0004Video settings":[""],"Sub-heading\\u0004Volume control":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004About":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Calibration":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Calls":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Date and time":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Date and Time":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Diagnostics":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Import/Export":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Layout templates":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004License":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Media files":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Network":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Power":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Real-time monitoring":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Roles":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Security":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Skin styles":[""],"Sub-section\\u0004Video":[""],"Subheader\\u0004Codec settings":[""],"Subheader\\u0004H.323 settings":[""],"Subheader\\u0004Server":[""],"Subheading\\u0004License details":[""],"Subheading\\u0004Maximum size of RTP packets":[""],"Subheading\\u0004Participants":[""],"Subheading\\u0004Program info":[""],"Subheading\\u0004Quality of service parameters":[""],"Subheading\\u0004Registration details":[""],"Subheading\\u0004RTP port range":[""],"Subheading\\u0004TrueConf MCU update":[""],"Tab\\u0004Additional":[""],"Tab\\u0004Audio channel":[""],"Tab\\u0004Content":[""],"Tab\\u0004Database":[""],"Tab\\u0004Diagnostics":[""],"Tab\\u0004Execution module":[""],"Tab\\u0004General":[""],"Tab\\u0004Layouts":[""],"Tab\\u0004Network interfaces":[""],"Tab\\u0004Primary stream":[""],"Tab\\u0004Receivers %n/%m":[""],"Tab\\u0004Recordings":[""],"Tab\\u0004Schedule":[""],"Tab\\u0004Secondary stream":[""],"Tab\\u0004Skins":[""],"Tab\\u0004System data":[""],"Tab\\u0004Uploaded files":[""],"Table column header. Here, the administrator can find information about incoming bitrate (up to 10 characters).\\u0004Incoming":[""],"Table column header. Here, the administrator can find information about outgoing bitrate (up to 10 characters).\\u0004Outgoing":[""],"Table columns\\u0004Message":[""],"Table columns\\u0004Message class":[""],"Table columns\\u0004Module name":[""],"Table columns\\u0004Timestamp":[""],"Tabs\\u0004Server log":[""],"Tabs\\u0004TCP / IP ports":[""],"Text button\\u0004Remove restrictions":[""],"Text button\\u0004Renew the license":[""],"Text buttons\\u0004Copy a conference":[""],"Text buttons\\u0004Start conference":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Actions":[""],"Text hint\\u0004An error occurred while calibrating":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Auto":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Calibration has been successful":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Calibration hasn’t started yet":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Calibration in progress, please wait":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Display name":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Email":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Last calibration date: %date":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Maximum frame size":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Maximum number of participants":[""],"Text hint\\u0004MCU calibration may take some time. You will not be able to hold any conferences during this period. All active conferences will be ended.":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Never":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Participants":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Phone":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Please send offlinereg.mrg generated file at [a]sales@trueconf.com[/a]":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Please send offlinereg.vrg generated file at [a]sales@trueconf.com[/a]":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Search":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Select Automatically":[""],"Text hint\\u0004The media file will be displayed in a content window.":[""],"Text hint\\u0004The media files will be displayed in the general layout.":[""],"Text hint\\u0004Upload the verification file sent by the sales department and click on the «Register button».":[""],"Text hint\\u0004User display name and address":[""],"Text hint\\u0004You need to register TrueConf MCU in order to activate it":[""],"Text hint for the input box\\u0004RTP packet size":[""],"Text hint in the input box\\u0004Conference name":[""],"Text hint in the input box\\u0004Conference PIN":[""],"Text hint in the input box\\u0004ID":[""],"Text hint in the input box\\u0004Password":[""],"Text hint in the input box\\u0004Route":[""],"Text hint in the input box\\u0004Server address":[""],"Text hint in the input box\\u0004Username":[""],"Text hint in the input box\\u0004Video conferencing server name":[""],"Text hint in the search box\\u0004Search":[""],"Text in the footer\\u0004%trueconf_mcu %version. © %currentYear. [a]TrueConf LLC[/a]. All rights reserved.":[""],"Text inside of a popup for removing avatar from user\\u0004Are you sure that you want to remove user avatar?":[""],"Text on the button\\u0004Delete":[""],"Text on the button\\u0004End conference":[""],"Text on the button\\u0004Remove":[""],"The button\\u0004Cancel":[""],"The button\\u0004Save":[""],"The button for adding a new file to the list of files that will be used for content sharing during a video meeting. Verb in the infinitive form.\\u0004Add":[""],"The button for adding a new item on the list. The button will be used in multiple parts of the UI.\\u0004Add":[""],"The button for adding a new participant to a video conference. Here, the administrator will need to  enter the call address (SIP or H.323) of the participant.\\u0004Add by address":[""],"The button for adding a new participant to a video conference. Verb in the infinitive form.\\u0004Add participant":[""],"The button for adding a role or multiple roles for a user. In this case a role is a  set of rights and permissions given to a user. %n is a counter indicating how many roles have been added. Do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Add (%n)":[""],"The button for adding the selected user to a video conference.\\u0004Add as new participant":[""],"The button for applying new settings.\\u0004Apply":[""],"The button for applying new settings. Verb in the indefinite form.\\u0004Apply":[""],"The button for changing the current password. Here, the word “change” is used as a verb in the infinitive form.\\u0004Change password":[""],"The button for closing the dialogue window.\\u0004Cancel":[""],"The button for declining an incoming call.\\u0004Decline":[""],"The button for deleting a role.\\u0004Delete":[""],"The button for deleting a user account.\\u0004Delete":[""],"The button for deleting a user address.\\u0004Delete":[""],"The button for deleting information about a video conferencing endpoint.\\u0004Delete":[""],"The button for deleting the avatar.\\u0004Delete":[""],"The button for ending the streaming (sharing) of a video file or multiple files. Here, “end” is used as a verb in the infinitive form.\\u0004End":[""],"The button for importing a database.\\u0004Import":[""],"The button for linking the selected contact in the address book to one of the video conferencing endpoints. If an endpoint is linked to a contact, each call to this user will be directed to this endpoint.\\u0004Link contact":[""],"The button for making a call to a user.\\u0004Call":[""],"The button for playing a media file (either video or audio). In this case, “play” is a verb in the infinitive form.\\u0004Play":[""],"The button for removing a user from one of the user groups.\\u0004Remove":[""],"The button for saving changes.\\u0004Save":[""],"The button for selecting multiple video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004Select endpoints":[""],"The button for sending a file needed for updating either the settings or configuration. The word “send” is used here because the update file will only be sent, but it does not mean the software will be immediately updated.\\u0004Send update":[""],"The button for sending the firmware upgrade file to all video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004Send to all":[""],"The button for stopping the playback of a media file (audio or media file). In this case, “stop” is a verb in the infinitive form.\\u0004Stop":[""],"The button for uploading a configuration file on the server. This file will include settings for a device (video conferencing endpoint). The verb “upload” should be used in the infinitive form.\\u0004Upload configuration":[""],"The button for uploading a file on the server.\\u0004Upload file":[""],"The button for uploading a file on the server. This file includes the program which is needed for the low-level control of a device (such a program is called firmware). The verb “upload” should be used in the infinitive form.\\u0004Upload firmware":[""],"The button in the dialogue window. By clicking on this button, the admin will save certain changes and restart the video conferencing server. Both verbs should be in the infinitive form.\\u0004Save and restart":[""],"The button in the menu where the administrator can edit a network address needed for making a call to a user. If this button is clicked, the edited address (essentially a string of digits and characters) will be added as a new address for the user. However, the old address will also remain.\\u0004Add as new address":[""],"The button or an option in the context menu. This UI element is needed for removing all items from the list. For example, this button can be used for clearing call history.  The word “clear” is used as a verb in the infinitive form.\\u0004Clear":[""],"The button that enables a user to move a user to an ongoing conference. This button will be displayed in case of an incoming call to the video conferencing server. The administrator can either decline a call or select one of the ongoing conferences and move the caller to this conference.\\u0004Move":[""],"The button that enables the admin to view (check) additional information about a conference. This button may be used in several parts of the GUI.\\u0004View":[""],"The button that enables the administrator to change the conference mode. A conference mode is a fixed group of settings for a video meeting.\\u0004Change mode":[""],"The button that enables the administrator to purchase the full version of the software solution.\\u0004Buy full version":[""],"The button that enables the server administrator to send a request for getting the trial version of a software solution. Please note that here, we are using “request” instead of “get” to indicate that the admin will have to contact technical support. He/she will not be able to get it automatically.\\u0004Request trial version":[""],"The button that enables the server administrator to test and save connection parameters.\\u0004Test and save connection":[""],"The button that ends video recording or streaming. The word “end” is used here to indicate that you cannot resume recording/streaming in a single click (as it is done with audio playback in a media player).\\u0004End":[""],"The button that leads to the menu where a user can manage video conferences (e.g., change the settings of these video meetings or end them, if necessary).\\u0004Go to conferences":[""],"The button that opens the menu where the administrator can select the parts of the database that need to be exported. \\u0004Select":[""],"The button that starts conference streaming.\\u0004Start streaming":[""],"The button that starts video recording.\\u0004Start recording":[""],"The button that will change the video conferencing mode.\\u0004Change":[""],"The button that will close the dialogue window.\\u0004Cancel":[""],"The button that will delete the file needed for updating software settings.\\u0004Delete update file":[""],"The button that will enable a user to proceed to the next stage. It may be used in multiple parts of the GUI.\\u0004Continue":[""],"The button that will enable the user to go back to the main menu.\\u0004Go to main screen":[""],"The button that will return the application to its default settings.\\u0004Set to default":[""],"The button that will start capturing network traffic. If possible, it should be translated as a verb.\\u0004Capture":[""],"The button that will start the export of the database. Verb.\\u0004Export":[""],"The button which enables a user to open a specific section of the UI. This button can be used in various parts of the application.\\u0004Open":[""],"The button which opens the pop-up window where the admin can configure H.323 settings. H.323 is a network protocol needed for making audio and video calls.\\u0004H.323 settings":[""],"The button which opens the pop-up window where the admin can configure SIP settings. SIP or Session Initiation Protocol is a network protocol needed for making audio and video calls.\\u0004SIP Settings":[""],"The button will enable a user to proceed to the next stage. It may be used in multiple parts of the UI.\\u0004Continue":[""],"The button. The lecturer is the only participant in a video meeting who is visible to other participants. This button will be used for replacing the current lecturer with a new one.\\u0004Change lecturer":[""],"The chosen layout is deleted when the button is clicked on\\u0004Delete":[""],"The counter displaying how many users have been selected.\\u0004Selected: %n":[""],"The counter that indicates the number of selected users. %n will be replaced with an integer; so, don’t delete or translate this part of the string.\\u0004Selected (%n)":[""],"The default name of the layout (arrangement of video windows). #%n will be replaced with a number.\\u0004Layout #%n":[""],"The default type of a video layout available in every type of conference. Here, the adjective is used in the nominative case, singular form.\\u0004General":[""],"The description of a conference type. In this case, the user, who is speaking at the moment, will be the only participant who will be displayed in the video layout\\u0004A default conference mode in which the speaker is always displayed in a single full-screen video window in the layout of attendees. All participants see  preconfigured layouts when the speaker is absent":[""],"The description of a layout created for a video conference.\\u0004Small video window is in the lower right corner":[""],"The description of a layout created for a video conference.\\u0004Small video window is in the upper right corner":[""],"The description of a layout created for a video conference.\\u0004Small video windows are above":[""],"The description of a layout created for a video conference.\\u0004Small video windows are below":[""],"The description of a layout created for a video conference.\\u0004Small video windows are on the left":[""],"The description of a layout created for a video conference.\\u0004Small video windows are on the right":[""],"The description of a layout created for a video conference.\\u0004Small video windows are on the right and left":[""],"The description of a layout created for a video conference.\\u0004Two large video windows and small ones above":[""],"The description of a layout created for a video conference.\\u0004Two large video windows and small ones below":[""],"The description of a video conferencing mode. A mode is a fixed group of settings for a video conference. This hint will be displayed for the conference that can be customized in any way depending on the needs of conference participants.\\u0004In this mode all conference settings can be accessed and adjusted. There are no fixed presets. All parameters are set by default":[""],"The description of an error in the event log. MCU stands for multipoint control unit, a device used for connecting multiple video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004MCU update error":[""],"The description of an error or an event in the log.\\u0004OS restart error":[""],"The description of an error or an event in the log. MCU stands for a multi-point control unit, a device used for connecting several video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004MCU restart error":[""],"The description of an error or an event in the log. MCU stands for multipoint control unit, a device used for connecting several video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004MCU shutdown error":[""],"The description of an error that occurs when the admin tries to change the certificate needed for the correct work of the HTTPS protocol. This text hint can be used as an error description and as a checkbox needed for filtering the list of errors. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004HTTPS certificate change error":[""],"The description of an error that occurs when we are changing the network port. This text hint can be used as an error description and as a checkbox needed for filtering the list of errors. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Port change error":[""],"The description of an error. Here, we are talking about video conferences held on the server. The admin can export the history of all these conferences. The noun “error” is used in the nominative case. The word “occurred” is omitted because this text is not a notification, but an event type.\\u0004An error while exporting the history of all conferences":[""],"The description of an error. The noun \\"error\\" is used in the nominative case. This text hint can also be used as a filter for the list of errors.\\u0004File open error":[""],"The description of an error. This error message will be displayed if certain data (e.g., user accounts) could not be archived. The noun \\"error\\" is used in the nominative case. This text hint can also be used as a filter for the list of errors.\\u0004Data archival error":[""],"The description of an event in the log. MCU stands for multipoint control unit, a device used for connecting multiple video conferencing endpoints.  Please note that this phrase can also be used as the title of checkbox. If this box is checked, the log will include the events related to MCU shutdown.\\u0004MCU shutdown":[""],"The description of an event in the log. MCU stands for multipoint control unit, a device used for connecting multiple video conferencing endpoints. Please note that this phrase can also be used as the title of checkbox. If this box is checked, the log will include the events related to MCU restart.\\u0004MCU restart":[""],"The description of an event in the log. MCU stands for multipoint control unit, a device used for connecting multiple video conferencing endpoints. Please note that this phrase can also be used as the title of checkbox. If this box is checked, the log will include the events related to the update of MCU.\\u0004MCU update":[""],"The description of an event in the log. Please note that this phrase can also be used as the title of checkbox. If this box is checked, the log will include the events related to OS restart.\\u0004OS restart":[""],"The description of an event on the server. Here, the word “engine” refers to a video rendering engine. In this case, we are talking about the service which ensures the work of this engine. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Engine service restart":[""],"The description of an event on the server. Here, we are talking about the service that ensures the work of WEB API (application programming interface (API) for a web server). The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004WEB API service restart":[""],"The description of an event on the server. Here, we are talking about the service which handles the requests directed to the server. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Proxy service restart":[""],"The description of an event that occurs on the server.\\u0004HTTPS certificate change":[""],"The description of an event that occurs on the server.\\u0004HTTPS port change":[""],"The description of an event that occurs on the server. Here, we are talking about the certificate used for the HTTPS protocol. The event occurred at some moment in the past, So, the present perfect tense should not be used.\\u0004The certificate expired":[""],"The description of an event. This description indicates that a certain process was not terminated as expected. This hint can be used in various parts of the UI. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Unexpected termination":[""],"The description of rights and permissions given to a user.\\u0004Schedules and holds conferences, creates user accounts. Unable to access server settings and user roles.":[""],"The end of a time interval. %DD.MM.YYYY HH:MM will be replaced with date and time. Do not edit or delete this part of the phrase.\\u0004to %DD.MM.YYYY HH:MM":[""],"The first part of the license key is displayed\\u0004Server ID":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window displayed when the administrator deletes a role for a user.\\u0004Deleting a role":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window displayed when the administrator removes a user from one of the user groups.\\u0004Removing from a group":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window displayed when the administrator removes the lecturer in a video meeting. Please note that the lecturer is the only participant who is visible to other participants.\\u0004Removing the lecturer":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window displayed when the administrator tries to change the way in which conference participants will be displayed in the video layout.\\u0004Changing participants display mode":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window displayed when the server administrator adds participants to a video conference. Please note that %n is the number of participants who will be added to a conference. Besides, %m is the maximum number of participants who can be added to a conference. Please note that %m and %n will be replaced with numbers. So, do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Adding participants (%n)":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window displayed when the server administrator deletes a schedule for a conference. Please note that a conference may have multiple schedules if they do not conflict with each other.\\u0004Deleting a schedule":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window displayed when the server administrator deletes a user account.\\u0004Deleting a user account":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window displayed when the server administrator deletes a video conference.\\u0004Deleting a conference":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window. Here, the admin can select a file that will be shared during a video meeting (e.g., an image, video, or slides).\\u0004Adding a file for content sharing":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window. Here, the administrator can create a new group in the address book.\\u0004Creating a group":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window. Here, the administrator can delete the user avatar.\\u0004Deleting the avatar":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window. Here, the server administrator can create a new role (a set of rights and permissions given to a user).\\u0004Adding a role":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window. Here, the server administrator can end an ongoing video conference.\\u0004Ending a conference":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window. Here, the server administrator can enter the PIN for joining the video meeting.\\u0004Conference PIN":[""],"The heading for a dialogue window. The lecturer is the only participant in a video meeting who is visible to other participants.\\u0004Changing the lecturer":[""],"The heading for a list of ongoing video conferences\\u0004Active conferences":[""],"The heading for a list of users. Please note that %n is a counter indicating the number of users. It will be replaced with an integer. So, don’t delete or translate this part of the string.\\u0004Users (%n)":[""],"The heading for a notification. Here, we are talking about the duration of a video meeting.\\u0004Conference duration":[""],"The heading for a pop-up displayed when the system administrator deletes a user account.\\u0004Deleting a user":[""],"The heading for a pop-up where the administrator can create a new user account.\\u0004Creating a user":[""],"The heading for a pop-up window displayed when the administrator deletes the call address of a user. A call address is the address used for making an audio/video call over the Internet. For example, there may be an SIP or H,323 address (SIP and H.323 are the network protocols).\\u0004Deleting an address":[""],"The heading for a section where the admin can check how a user can be detected by the application.\\u0004Speaker detection":[""],"The heading in the dialogue window displayed when the admin deletes a file needed for updating the software or its settings.\\u0004Deleting the update file":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window displayed when the admin imports address book contacts to the server.\\u0004Contact list import":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window displayed when the administrator deletes information which is needed for the configuration of a server.\\u0004Deleting server data":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window displayed when the administrator removes a user or users from a group in the address book.\\u0004Removing from the group":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window displayed when the administrator sets the server settings to their default values.\\u0004Return to default settings":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window displayed when the administrator tries to change the conference mode. A conference mode is a fixed group of settings for a video meeting.\\u0004Changing conference mode":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window displayed when the administrator tries to delete a file.\\u0004Deleting a file":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window displayed when the administrator tries to end content sharing during a video meeting.\\u0004End content sharing":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window displayed when the server administrator tries to change the display name for a conference participant. The display name is the name shown in the layout of a video conference.\\u0004Changing the display name":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window displayed when the server administrator tries to change the maximum frame rate during video meetings.\\u0004Changing maximum frame rate":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window.\\u0004Deleting a file":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window.\\u0004Deleting files":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window.\\u0004Settings change":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window. Here, the admin can find information about a video conference. Please note that %ConferenceName will be replaced with an actual name of a video meeting. So, don’t delete or translate this part of the string.\\u0004Conference “%ConferenceName” info":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window. Here, the admin can import a database.\\u0004Database import":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window. Here, the admin will link the selected video conferencing to a specific contact in the address book. If an endpoint is linked to a contact, each call to this user will be directed to this endpoint.\\u0004Link the endpoint to a different contact":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window. Here, the administrator can check information about the participants to whom the layout will be displayed. In other words, the layout will be received by the participants.\\u0004Layout recipients":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window. Here, the administrator can tie (link) the selected contact in the address book to one of the available video conferencing endpoints. So, the calls to this contact will be directed to this endpoint.\\u0004Link the contact to an endpoint":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window. Here, the server administrator can physically shut down the server.\\u0004Shut down server":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window. Here, the server administrator can regulate the volume for multiple audio or video files shared during a video meeting.\\u0004Volume control for selected files":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window. Here, the server administrator can regulate the volume for the selected video or audio file shared during a video meeting. Please note that %FileName will be replaced with a filename. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Volume control for the file “%FileName”":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window. Here, the server administrator can restart the operating system.\\u0004Restart OS":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window. Here, the server administrator can restart the software-based MCU (multi-point control unit), a solution needed connecting several video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004Restart MCU":[""],"The heading of a dialogue window. The heading indicates that the menu provides information about a selected conference participant.\\u0004(“%DisplayName”) connection details":[""],"The heading of a notification. This notification indicates that a certain application is not available on the user’s device. Probably, it was not installed.\\u0004Unable to find the application":[""],"The heading of a pop-up window displayed when a user deletes information about a video conferencing endpoint.\\u0004Deleting an endpoint":[""],"The heading of a pop-up window displayed when the administrator adds a new participant to a conference by his/her call address (SIP or H.323). \\u0004Adding a participant by address":[""],"The heading of a pop-up window displayed when the administrator tries to delete the history of conferences held on the video conferencing server.\\u0004Clearing the history of conferences":[""],"The heading of a pop-up window displayed when the administrator updates the settings (configuration) of a video conferencing endpoint named TrueConf Group. If possible, do not translate or transliterate the name “TrueConf Group”. Use the English spelling instead.  The word “send” is used here instead of “update” because the  configuration file will only be sent to the video conferencing endpoint. However, settings will not be immediately updated.\\u0004Send the TrueConf Group configuration update":[""],"The heading of a pop-up window displayed when the server administrator tries to update the firmware of a video conferencing endpoint named TrueConf Group. If possible, do not translate or transliterate the name “TrueConf Group”. Use the English spelling instead. The word “send” is used here instead of “update” because the update file will only be sent to the video conferencing endpoint. However, the firmware will be immediately updated.\\u0004Send the TrueConf Group firmware update":[""],"The heading of a pop-up window or any other UI section. Here, the admin can check information about a certain network address. %address will be replaced with a value. Do not edit or delete this template variable.\\u0004Address %address":[""],"The heading of a pop-up window. Here, a server admin can configure audio and video settings for the selected person participating in a video conference. %DisplayName  will be replaced with the actual name. So, do not delete or edit this part of the phrase.\\u0004Participant \\"%DisplayName\\"":[""],"The heading of a pop-up window. Here, an admin can add selected users to a video conference. Please note %ConferenceName will be replaced with an actual meeting name. So, do not delete or edit this part of the phrase.\\u0004Adding participants to the conference “%ConferenceName”":[""],"The heading of a pop-up window. Here, the admin can configure  the schedule for a video meeting.\\u0004Schedule settings":[""],"The heading of a pop-up window. Here, the administrator can generate the certificate and key needed for HTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure).\\u0004Generating a certificate and key":[""],"The heading of a pop-up window. It will be displayed when the admin tries to delete account information. Please note that in this case, we will not be deleting an account (more likely, the admin will be deleting some data related to the account).\\u0004Deleting account data":[""],"The heading of a sidebar. Here, we are talking about the number of a video window in the layout. %n will be replaced with a number. So, do not delete this part of the phrase.\\u0004Video slot %n":[""],"The heading of the dialogue window. Here, the server administrator can add those participants who will be allowed to speak during a video meeting.\\u0004Adding presenters":[""],"The heading of the dialogue window. Here, the server administrator can add those participants who will only receive audio during a video meeting. They will not be allowed to speak during a meeting.\\u0004Adding attendees":[""],"The input box for entering the registration key\\u0004Registration key":[""],"The input field for entering a server domain name\\u0004Server domain name":[""],"The label for a drop-down list. Interactive voice response, or IVR, is an automated telephone system technology that enables callers to receive or provide information, or make requests using voice or menu inputs. Here, one can select the language of the IVR menu.\\u0004Language of interactive voice response menu":[""],"The lecturer is the only participant in a video meeting who is visible to other participants. This button will remove the lecturer from the video meeting. Here, “remove” is used as  a verb in the infinitive form.\\u0004Remove lecturer":[""],"The name of a drop-down list\\u0004Avatar display options":[""],"The name of a legend in the hardware disk widget\\u0004Free (Gb)":[""],"The name of a license type\\u0004Free":[""],"The name of a license type\\u0004Paid":[""],"The name of a role given all the rights and permissions.\\u0004Administrator":[""],"The name of a role given to a user. This role should not be confused with the “administrator” because the operator has fewer rights.\\u0004Operator":[""],"The name of a table column\\u0004Incoming":[""],"The name of a table column\\u0004Name":[""],"The name of a table column\\u0004Outgoing":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Bandwidth:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Bitrate:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Call direction:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Connection protocol:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Connection quality:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Content sharing (BFCP/H.239):":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Current bitrate:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Device type:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Display name:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Encryption:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Frame rate:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Jitter (msec):":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Key frame request rate:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Key frame requests:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Lost packets:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Packet loss rate:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Protocol:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Resolution:":[""],"The name of a table row with the information about connection details.\\u0004Total packets:":[""],"The name of the setting. Here we talk about the default configuration for how the participant is called when they are added to the conference.\\u0004To call participants by default":[""],"The name of the table row with the information about call direction.\\u0004Incoming":[""],"The name of the table row with the information about call direction.\\u0004Outgoing":[""],"The network status of a video conferencing endpoint.\\u0004Online":[""],"The notification\\u0004User successfully add to address book":[""],"The notification displayed to the administrator when he/she deletes a layout. Please note that a layout may have a custom name like %LayoutName. So, do not delete or translate this part of the phrase.\\u0004The layout “%LayoutName” has been deleted":[""],"The notification displayed to the administrator when he/she sends a file needed for updating the settings of a video conferencing endpoint. Please note that %FileName and %TerminalName will be replaced with the names of a file and endpoint respectively. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The configuration update file “%FileName” has been sent to the endpoint “%TerminalName”":[""],"The notification displayed to the administrator when he/she sends a file needed for upgrading the firmware of a video conferencing endpoint. Please note that %FileName and %TerminalName will be replaced with the names of a file and endpoint respectively. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The firmware update file “%FileName” has been sent to the endpoint “%TerminalName”":[""],"The notification displayed to the administrator when heshe deletes a file. Please note that %FileName will be replaced with a filename. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004The file “%FileName” has been deleted from the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"The notification displayed to the server administrator if some error occurs. The hint indicates that the admin can manually restart the services included in the software solution or contact technical support. Please note that “TrueConf” is a company name. If the rules of the target language allow, do not transliterate this word. Use the English word instead.\\u0004Please try to restart the services manually or contact TrueConf technical support":[""],"The notification displayed to the server administrator when he/she ends the selected conference. Please note that %ConferenceName will be replaced with an actual conference name. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004The conference “%ConferenceName” has been ended":[""],"The notification displayed to the server administrator when he/she ends two selected conferences. Please note that %ConferenceName1 and %ConferenceName2 will be replaced with an actual conference name. So, do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The conferences “%ConferenceName1” and ConferenceName2 have been ended":[""],"The notification displayed to the server administrator when he/she starts multiple conferences (more than 2). %n is the number of selected conferences. It will be replaced with a number. Do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Multiple conferences (%n) have been started":[""],"The notification displayed to the server administrator. The lecturer is the only participant in a video meeting who is visible to other participants. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username. So, do not delete or replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004The lecturer “%DisplayName” has been removed":[""],"The notification displayed when a user (%DisplayName) is moved from one ongoing conference to another. %DisplayName and %ConferenceName will be replaced with a username and conference name. So, do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004“%DisplayName” has been moved to the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"The notification displayed when an administrator clears the history of video conferences held on the server.\\u0004The history of conferences has been successfully cleared":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator allows participants to join a video meeting\\u0004The meeting has been unlocked":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator creates a new video layout. Please note that a layout may have a custom name like %LayoutName. So, do not delete or translate this part of the phrase.\\u0004The layout “%LayoutName” have been created":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator deletes a file used by the participants of an ongoing conference. For example, one of the participants may be using the file for content sharing. Please note that %n and %ConfName will be replaced with a number of files and the conference name. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004“%DisplayName” has been removed from the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator deletes a file used by the participants of an ongoing conference. For example, one of the participants may be using the file for content sharing. Please note that %n and %ConfName will be replaced with a number of files and the conference name. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004Multiple files (%n) have deleted from the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator deletes a file. Please note that %FileName will be replaced with an actual filename. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004The file “%FileName” has been deleted":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator deletes a group from the address book. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with a group name. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004The group “%DisplayName” has been deleted":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator deletes a role with a custom name (%NameRole) for a user (%DisplayName).  Please note that %NameRole and %DisplayName will be replaced with a role name and username. So, do not delete or translate these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The role \\"%NameRole\\" has been deleted for \\"%DisplayName\\"":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator deletes a user account. Please note that %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username. So, do not delete or replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004The user “%DisplayName” has been deleted":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator ends content sharing for multiple files during a conference. Please note that %n will be replaced with a number of files. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Ended sharing multiple files (%n)":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator ends multiple video conferences. Please note that %n is a counter indicating how many conferences have been ended by the administrator. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Multiple conferences (%n) have been ended":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator makes it impossible for users to join a video meeting\\u0004The meeting has been locked":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator removes a participant from the conference.  Please note that %DisplayName and %ConfName will be replaced with a username and conference name respectively. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004“%DisplayName” has been removed from the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator removes two participants from the conference. Please note that %DisplayName1, %DisplayName2, and %ConfName will be replaced with the names of participants and the conference name. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004“%DisplayName1” and “%DisplayName2” have been removed from the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator sends a file needed for updating the firmware of two video conferencing endpoints. Please note that %FileName, %TerminalName1, and %TerminalName2 will be replaced with the names of the file and endpoints respectively. So, do not delete or edit these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The firmware update file “%FileName” has been sent to the endpoints “%TerminalName1” and “%TerminalName2”":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator sends a file needed for updating the settings of all video conferencing endpoints connected to the server. Please note that %FileName will be replaced with a filename. So, do not edit or delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004The configuration update file “%FileName” has been sent to all endpoints":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator sends a file needed for updating the settings of multiple video conferencing endpoints. Please note that %n is the number of video conferencing endpoints. %FileName will be replaced with an actual file name. Do not edit or delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The configuration update file “%FileName” has been sent to multiple (%n) endpoints":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator sends a file needed for upgrading the firmware of all video conferencing endpoints connected to the server. Please note that %FileName will be replaced with a filename. So, do not edit or delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004The firmware update file “%FileName” has been sent to all video conferencing endpoints":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator sends a file needed for upgrading the firmware of multiple video conferencing endpoints. Please note that %n is the number of video conferencing endpoints. Do not edit or delete this part of the sentence. Similarly, do not delete or edit %FileName.\\u0004The firmware update file “%FileName” has been sent to multiple (%n) video conferencing endpoints":[""],"The notification displayed when the administrator uploads a file on the server. Please note that %FileName will be replaced with an actual filename. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004The file “%FileName” has been uploaded":[""],"The notification displayed when the application is unable to connect a user to a video conference because this process takes too much time. Here, %DisplayName will be replaced with an actual username. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Disconnected “%DisplayName” due to timeout":[""],"The notification displayed when the input field is empty.\\u0004This field has to be filled.":[""],"The notification displayed when the server administrator deletes a video conference. Please note that %ConferenceName will be replaced with an actual conference name. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004The conference “%ConferenceName” has been deleted":[""],"The notification displayed when the server administrator deletes an audio channel. The audio channel is created for a group of participants who can send and receive audio from each other. This term is used in relation to multi-language meetings requiring the assistance of translators.\\u0004The audio channel “%ChannelName” has been deleted":[""],"The notification displayed when the server administrator deletes information about a hardware-based video conferencing endpoint.  Please note that %TerminalName will be replaced with an actual endpoint name. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004The endpoint “%TerminalName” has been deleted":[""],"The notification displayed when the server administrator deletes multiple video conferences. Please note that %n is a counter indicating how many conferences have been deleted. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Multiple conferences (%n) have been deleted":[""],"The notification displayed when the server administrator deletes one of the conference schedules. Please note that a conference may have multiple schedules. %ScheduleType will be replaced with an actual schedule name, e.g, “weakly”, “monthly”, and so forth. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004The schedule type “%ScheduleType” has been deleted":[""],"The notification displayed when the server administrator deletes two video conferences. Please note that %ConferenceName1 and %ConferenceName2 % will be replaced with actual conference names. So, do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The conferences “%ConferenceName1” and “%ConferenceName2”  have been deleted":[""],"The notification displayed when the server administrator ends content sharing for the selected file (audio or video). Please note that %FileName will be replaced with a filename. So, do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Ended sharing the file “%FileName”":[""],"The notification displayed when the server administrator starts two video conferences. Please note that %ConferenceName1 and %ConferenceName2 will be replaced with actual conference names. So, do not delete or replace these parts of the sentence.\\u0004The conferences “%ConferenceName1” and “%ConferenceName2” have been started":[""],"The notification displayed when the server has been shut down.\\u0004Server shut down":[""],"The notification displayed when the server has been started.\\u0004Server running":[""],"The notification which is displayed when multiple users (%DisplayName and %DisplayName) are moved from one conference to another. %DisplayName1, %DisplayName2 and %ConferenceName will be replaced with the username and the conference name. So, do not delete these parts of the sentence.\\u0004“%DisplayName1” and “%DisplayName2” have been moved to the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"The notification which is displayed when multiple users are moved from one ongoing conference to another.  %ConfName will be replaced with a conference name. Do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Multiple participants (%n) have been moved to the conference “%ConfName”":[""],"The number of days remaining before the conference\\u0004Day":["","Days"],"The number of hours remaining before the conference\\u0004Hour":["","Hours"],"The number of minutes before the conference\\u0004Minute":["","Minutes"],"The number of seconds remaining before the conference\\u0004Second":["","Seconds"],"The pop-up heading. Here, the admin can select which parts of the database should be exported.\\u0004Export parameters":[""],"The pop-up heading. In this case, address refers to the address needed for making an audio/video call over the Internet. For example, there may be an SIP or H.323 address (SIP and H,323 are the network protocols). The pop-up will be displayed when the server administrator will add a new call address.\\u0004Adding an address":[""],"The pop-up hint for an icon. The hint indicates that a video conference is now being streamed.\\u0004Streaming conference":[""],"The pop-up hint for an icon. The hint indicates that a video conference is now being video recorded.\\u0004Recording conference":[""],"The question in a pop-up window displayed when the administrator deletes the call address of a user. A call address is the address used for making an audio/video call over the Internet. For example, there may be an SIP or H,323 address (SIP and H.323 are the network protocols).\\u0004Do you want to delete the %adres address for “%DisplayName”?":[""],"The question in the dialogue window displayed when the server administrator deletes multiple users from the address book group. Please note that %GroupName will be replaced with a group name. So, do not delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Do you want to delete selected users from the group “%GroupName”?":[""],"The section heading.\\u0004Event log":[""],"The section heading. Here, an admin can configure settings for user authorization.\\u0004Authorization":[""],"The section heading. Here, an admin can configure settings for user conferences.\\u0004Conferences":[""],"The section heading. Here, one can upload a certificate needed for HTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure). The word has to be used in the nominative case.\\u0004Certificate":[""],"The section heading. Here, one can upload the key needed for HTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure). The word has to be used in the nominative case.\\u0004Key":[""],"The section heading. Here, the admin can check information about a hardware-based video conferencing endpoint.\\u0004Endpoint information":[""],"The section heading. Here, the admin can give different roles to users.\\u0004Roles":[""],"The section heading. Here, the administrator can configure settings for deleting various types of data stored on the server.\\u0004Data deletion":[""],"The section heading. Here, the administrator can configure the settings of a video conference. Nominative case.\\u0004Conference settings":[""],"The section heading. Here, the administrator can import a database.\\u0004Import":[""],"The section heading. Here, the administrator can view the list of media files stored on the server. (images, videos, and so forth). %n is a counter indicating the number of files. Please do not edit or delete this part of the sentence.\\u0004Media files (%n)":[""],"The section heading. Here, the server administrator can find the history of conferences held on the server.\\u0004History":[""],"The section heading. Here, the server administrator can learn about the software and limitations of its free version.\\u0004Free version limitations":[""],"The section heading. Here, the server administrator can register a software solution if the server has no access to the Internet, and one can register it only in offline mode. Please note that TrueConf MCU is a product name. If the rules of the target language allow it, do not transliterate this part of the sentence. Use the English spelling instead. MCU stands for multipoint control unit or a solution needed for connecting several video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004TrueConf MCU offline registration":[""],"The section heading. Here, the server administrator can register a software solution. Please note that TrueConf MCU is a product name. If the rules of the target language allow it, do not transliterate this part of the sentence. Use the English spelling instead. MCU stands for multipoint control unit or a solution needed for connecting several video conferencing endpoints.\\u0004TrueConf MCU online registration":[""],"The section heading. This phrase refers to the type of a conference in which  there is only one participant (lecturer) who can be seen and heard by other participants (attendees). The attendees will only be allowed to watch and listen.\\u0004Lecture mode":[""],"The section heading. We are talking about hardware-based video conferencing endpoints. Noun in the nominative case.\\u0004Endpoints":[""],"The section subheading. Here, one can check the status of the automatic gain control.\\u0004AGC:":[""],"The section subheading. Here, one can check the status of the noise suppression.\\u0004Noise suppression:":[""],"The section subheading. Here, the administrator can configure some audio and video settings for a virtual meeting, e.g., noise cancellation, camera or microphone settings, and so fort\\u0004Audio and video settings":[""],"The section subheading. Here, the administrator can export the database.\\u0004Export":[""],"The section subheading. Here, the administrator can select the period during which the conference will be repeated. For example, a conference can be held weekly on Tuesdays from March 2 to March 28. These parameters will be optional.\\u0004Reccurence period":[""],"The section subheading. Here, the administrator can select the period during which the conference will be repeated. For example, a conference can be held weekly on Tuesdays from March 2 to March 28. These parameters will be optional.\\u0004Recurrence period (optional)":[""],"The section subheading. Here, the administrator can select the period when repetition of a conference will start. For example, the conference can be repeated daily starting from  a certain date. The word “start” is used as a noun.\\u0004Recurrence start":[""],"The section subheading. Here, the administrator can select when the conference should be no longer repeated. For example, the conference can be repeated daily up until a certain date. The word “end” is used as a noun.\\u0004Recurrence end":[""],"The section subheading. The subheading will be followed by a hint indicating that a user can join a video meeting from a client application (either desktop or mobile).\\u0004Application":[""],"The start of a time interval.  %DD.MM.YYYY HH:MM will be replaced with date and time. Do not edit or delete this part of the phrase.\\u0004from %DD.MM.YYYY HH:MM":[""],"The status explaining why a user could not be connected to the conference. This status will be displayed if a conference invitation was sent to a user who has no call address needed for making  calls over the Internet (for example, SIP or H.323 addresses).\\u0004No address":[""],"The status explaining why a user could not be connected to the conference. This status will be displayed if a user was added without being connected.\\u0004Added without connecting":[""],"The status indicates that the participant was moved from one ongoing conference to another by the administrator. In this case, %ConfName is the name of the conference to which the user was moved.  Do not delete or replace this part of the sentence.\\u0004Moved to the conference %ConfName":[""],"The status of a user who did not join the conference. This status will be displayed if the server administrator deliberately decided not to invite the participant when the conference was started. This may be necessary in cases when a person cannot join the conference at the very beginning, but will be able to do it later.\\u0004Invitation call was disabled upon conference start":[""],"The subheading for the list of conference participants who can speak during a video conference. Nominative case.\\u0004Presenters":[""],"The subheading for the section where the admin can configure language and time-zone preferences for a user.\\u0004Preferences":[""],"The subheading in the menu that provides information about the software license. Here, one can check the date when the license will expire. Please note that the word “current” is used here because the admin may have multiple licenses but only one of them is used at the given moment.\\u0004Current license expiry date":[""],"The subheading in the menu where the admin can configure video quality settings for a stream. A video encoder is the software needed for compressing video.\\u0004Video encoder settings":[""],"The subheading of the information menu. Here, you can find additional information about the server event.\\u0004Additionally":[""],"The subheading. Here, one can check and set the number of conference participants’ video windows on the screen.\\u0004Number of video windows":[""],"The subheading. Here, the administrator can select what kind of information about conferences should be saved when the database is exported. For example, the admin can save information about their schedule or participants.\\u0004Conferences":[""],"The subheading. Here, the administrator can select when a recurring video meeting should be repeated. This string is the shortened version of the phrase “Repeat on Mondays, Tuesdays, etc”.\\u0004Repeat on":[""],"The subheading. Here, the administrator will be able to select from different options for sorting the list of video conferences (e.g., in direct or reverse alphabetical order).\\u0004Sort":[""],"The subheading. Here, the server administrator can configure settings for the automatic ending of an ongoing video conference.\\u0004Automatic conference ending":[""],"The subheading. Here, the user can configure a filter for the list of video conferences. The app may display either all conferences or only the conferences created by the user. This subheading is the shortened version of the phrases “show all conferences” and “show only my conferences”.\\u0004Show":[""],"The subheading. Here, the user can configure the settings for voice activity detection. If this feature is activated, the participant, who is speaking at the moment, will be displayed in an enlarged window.\\u0004Voice activity detection":[""],"The subheading. It will be followed by a datepicker for selecting the start date and time of a video meeting.\\u0004Date and time":[""],"The tab where the admin can find additional information about a user.\\u0004Additional":[""],"The tab where the admin can find the general information about a user.\\u0004General":[""],"The table column header.\\u0004Group name":[""],"The table column header.\\u0004Role name":[""],"The table column heading. Here, the admin can check information about the video conferencing endpoint linked to the selected user. If an endpoint is linked to a contact, each call to this user will be directed to this endpoint.\\u0004Linked endpoint":[""],"The table column heading. Here, the admin can check the file name.\\u0004File name":[""],"The table column heading. Here, the admin can check the information about the layout received by a user.\\u0004Received layout":[""],"The table column heading. Here, the server administrator can find the name of a user. Besides, here, one can check the call address of a user. The call address is the address needed for making calls over IP networks, e.g., SIP or H.323 calls.\\u0004Username and address":[""],"The text hint describing a certain event. Calibration is the process aimed at determining the most optimal configuration for a software solution depending on hardware characteristics of the machine. The term “calibration” is already used in the UI. Please check how this phrase was previously translated into the target language. The word “end” is used instead of “stop” because the process of calibration was completed. “End” is used as a noun in the nominative case. This phrase may be used as a subheading and the name of a filter for the list of events.\\u0004Calibration end":[""],"The text hint describing a certain event. Calibration is the process aimed at determining the most optimal configuration for a software solution depending on hardware parameters of the machine. The term “calibration” is already used in the UI. Please check how this word was previously translated into the target language. The word “aborted” is used instead of “ended” because the process of calibration was stopped because it could be completed. This phrase may be used as a subheading and the name of a filter for the list of events.\\u0004Calibration aborted":[""],"The text hint describing a certain event. Calibration is the process aimed at determining the most optimal configuration for a software solution depending on hardware parameters of the machine. The term “calibration” is already used in the UI. Please check how this word was previously translated into the target language. The word “start” is used as a noun in the nominative case. This phrase may be used as a subheading and the name of a filter for the list of events.\\u0004Calibration start":[""],"The text hint describing a certain event. Here, we are talking about the export of data stored on the server (e.g., user accounts or settings). The word “export” is used as a noun in the nominative case. This phrase may be used as a subheading and the name of a filter for the list of events.\\u0004Data export":[""],"The text hint describing an event on the server. Here we are talking about the history of a single conference. For example, one can export such information as the time when this meeting started or the list of participants.\\u0004History of a conference is exported":[""],"The text hint describing an event. Here, we are talking about the export of various data (like settings, user accounts etc.). The noun “error” is used in the nominative case. This phrase may be used as a subheading and the name of a filter for the list of events.\\u0004Data export error":[""],"The text hint describing an event. Here, we are talking about the import of various data (e.g., user accounts or settings). The noun “import” is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Data import error":[""],"The text hint describing an event. Here, we are talking about the import of various data (e.g., user accounts or settings). The word “import” is used as a noun in the nominative case.\\u0004Data import":[""],"The text hint describing the type of an audio or video call. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004incoming call":[""],"The text hint describing the type of an audio or video call. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004outgoing call":[""],"The text hint describing the type of video window. Such video windows will be used for displaying media files (e.g.,  images, PDF documents, or videos).\\u0004Media file":[""],"The text hint displayed to a user if a hyperlink cannot be opened in a certain browser.\\u0004Open the link in a different browser":[""],"The text hint displayed to the admin. The hint indicates that the password of a certain user ceased to be valid (expired).\\u0004The password has expired":[""],"The text hint displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server. Here, one can check the maximum number of users who can be connected to the conference. %n will be replaced with a number. Do not delete or edit this part of the sentence.\\u0004Maximum number of available connections: %n":[""],"The text hint displayed to the administrator of a video conferencing server. In some cases, the participants may not be displayed permanently in the layout. Instead, they can be rotated at certain intervals. In other words, they may be displayed in the layout and then removed. This may be necessary when the number of participants is larger than the number of video windows. The admin can change the rotation interval by going to the specific section of the UI.  The template variables %Administration and %Video are used to make sure that the names of UI sections are always translated in the same way. Do not delete or edit these variables. In this case, %n will be replaced with a number which is greater than 1. This text includes tags which should also be used in your translation.\\u0004Rotation interval - %n seconds. You can change the rotation interval for participants in the %Administration > %Video section":["","Rotation interval - %n second. You can change the rotation interval for participants in the %Administration > %Video section"],"The text hint displayed to the administrator of the video conferencing server. To join a video conference, a user may be required to enter a PIN code. The admin can choose how many times a user can enter an incorrect PIN. If this limit is exceeded, the user will no longer be able to connect to a conference. Entering a PIN is only one of the examples, An attempt to join a conference may be failed due to other reasons as well.\\u0004Number of failed attempts to join a conference before connection blocking":[""],"The text hint displayed when the cursor is directed towards the camera icon\\u0004Hide participant\'s video":[""],"The text hint displayed when the cursor is directed towards the camera icon\\u0004Show participant\'s video":[""],"The text hint displayed when the cursor is directed towards the microphone icon\\u0004Mute":[""],"The text hint displayed when the cursor is directed towards the microphone icon\\u0004Unmute":[""],"The text hint displayed when the mouse cursor is moved to the icon button. When the icon is clicked on, the participant can no longer hear the audio from other participants\\u0004Disable conference audio":[""],"The text hint displayed when the mouse cursor is moved to the icon button. When the icon is clicked on, the participant can no longer hear the audio from other participants\\u0004Enable conference audio":[""],"The text hint displayed when the mouse cursor is pointed to the icon\\u0004Do not show conference video to participant":[""],"The text hint displayed when the mouse cursor is pointed to the icon\\u0004Show conference video to participant":[""],"The text hint displayed when the mouse cursor is pointed to the icon\\u0004Start conference recording ":[""],"The text hint displayed when the mouse cursor is pointed to the icon\\u0004Stop conference recording":[""],"The text hint displayed when the mouse cursor is pointed to the icon.\\u0004Send a message to conference chat":[""],"The text hint displayed when the mouse cursor is pointed to the icon.\\u0004Start conference streaming":[""],"The text hint displayed when the mouse cursor is pointed to the icon.\\u0004Stop conference streaming":[""],"The text hint explaining the cause of a certain problem. Here, we are talking about the certificate and key needed for the correct work of the HTTPS protocol.\\u0004The key does not match the certificate":[""],"The text hint for a button or checkbox. In this case, the word “name” may refer to the name of a conference participant or the name of a file. If this box is checked, the name will be displayed in the layout.\\u0004Show the name in the layout":[""],"The text hint for a button or checkbox. In this case, the word “name” may refer to the name of a conference participant or the name of a file. If this box is checked, the name will not be displayed in the layout.\\u0004Don’t show the name in the layout":[""],"The text hint for a button which enables an administrator to save certain information to an external drive before fully deleting this data.\\u0004Export before clearing":[""],"The text hint for a button. If this button is clicked, the application will only record the slides or content shared during a conference. Content will be maximized to full screen. The video of conference participants will not be recorded.\\u0004Full screen":[""],"The text hint for a button. If this button is clicked, the application will record video and content shared during a video conference.\\u0004Content and video":[""],"The text hint for a button. If this button is clicked, the content shared during a video conference will not be displayed during recording and streaming.\\u0004Do not display":[""],"The text hint for a button. If this button is clicked, the minimum value will be used. If possible, your translation should be up to 4 characters.\\u0004max.":[""],"The text hint for a button. If this button is clicked, the minimum value will be used. If possible, your translation should be up to 4 characters.\\u0004min.":[""],"The text hint for a button. This button enables a system admin to export some data table in the selected format, for example, we can speak about the table providing information about users.\\u0004Export table":[""],"The text hint for a button. This button enables a user to download a certain file or a group of files.\\u0004Export":[""],"The text hint for a button. This button enables a user to download a desktop or mobile app for joining a video meeting.\\u0004Download":[""],"The text hint for a button. This button enables a user to free space on the disk drive.\\u0004Free up space":[""],"The text hint for a button. This button is needed for generating a new certificate and key needed for the work of HTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure).\\u0004Generate":[""],"The text hint for a button. This button should be clicked, if the server is connected to the Internet and online registration is possible. Nominative case.\\u0004Online registration":[""],"The text hint for a button. This button should be clicked, if the server is not connected to the Internet and one can register the software only in offline mode. Nominative case.\\u0004Offline registration":[""],"The text hint for a button. This button will fill the layout windows with the videos received from conference participants.\\u0004Fill video windows with participants":[""],"The text hint for a button. This UI element may be used for multiple purposes, e.g., for restarting the server or the operating system.\\u0004Restart":[""],"The text hint for a checkbox. If this box is checked the participants will not be displayed in the layout permanently. Instead, they will be displayed and then removed from the layout at certain intervals. This may be necessary when the number of participants is larger than the number of video windows.\\u0004Rotate participants":[""],"The text hint for a checkbox. If this box is checked, the application will mute the microphones of participants who try to join a video conference. Please note that the word “incoming” is used because we are talking about the situations when a user is trying to join a conference on his/her own (not the cases when this person is invited to the conference).\\u0004Mute participants’ microphones in case of an incoming conference connection":[""],"The text hint for a checkbox. If this box is checked, the application will turn off participants’ cameras when they join a video conference. Please note that the word “incoming” is used because we are talking about the situations when a user is trying to join a conference on his/her own (not the cases when this person is invited to the conference).\\u0004Turn off participants’ cameras in case of an incoming conference connection":[""],"The text hint for a drop-down list. If this option is selected, an invitation call will not be sent to the participants of a conference. This option may be necessary if users will be able to join the meeting some time after its beginning. However, they do not want to receive an invitation call.\\u0004Don’t call participants when conference is started":[""],"The text hint for a drop-down list. SIP (Session Initiation Protocol) and H.323 are network protocols used for audio communication over the Internet. In this section, the admin can select which of these protocols should be used. \\u0004SIP/H.323":[""],"The text hint for a filter button. If this button is clicked, the list of events in the logs will not be filtered in any way.\\u0004All":[""],"The text hint for a menu option. Here, one can find the list of contacts.\\u0004Address book":[""],"The text hint for a search button\\u0004Search":[""],"The text hint for a UI element. This UI element makes it possible to sort events by their type.\\u0004Event time":[""],"The text hint for an icon button. If this button is clicked, all video windows will become empty.\\u0004Clear all video windows":[""],"The text hint for an input field.\\u0004Search":[""],"The text hint for an input field. A role is a set of permissions given to a user. Please note that in this case %n is the number of characters entered into the input field while the %m is the maximum number of characters. Don’t translate or delete these parts of the string.\\u0004Role name (%n/%m)":[""],"The text hint for an input field. Here, one can enter the number of days during which the password will be valid. The word “days” should be used in the nominative case.\\u0004Days":[""],"The text hint for an input field. Here, one can specify for how long the user account should be blocked (locked). This situation is possible if a user makes too many failed attempts to sign in. The person will be unable to log in during this period.\\u0004Lockout duration":[""],"The text hint for an input field. Here, the admin can enter the domain address of a server. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Domain address":[""],"The text hint for an input field. Here, the admin can set the minimum number of characters in a user’s password.\\u0004Minimum number of characters":[""],"The text hint for an input field. Here, the admin can specify the amount of time, e.g., 1 or 2 minutes.\\u0004Time":[""],"The text hint for an input field. Here, the admin can specify what should be done in cases when a user makes too many failed attempts to sign in. For example, the system can lock (block) this user’s account after a number of failed attempts to authenticate. The user will be unable to log in during a certain period\\u0004Number of failed authentication attempts before account locking":[""],"The text hint for an input field. Here, the admin has to enter the domain address of a video conferencing server. This address will be used to create hyperlinks that will be needed for joining video conferences.\\u0004The address will be used to generate links to conferences":[""],"The text hint for an input field. In some cases, the participants may not be displayed permanently in the layout. Instead, they can be rotated at certain intervals. In other words, they may be displayed in the layout and then removed. This may be necessary when the number of participants is larger than the number of video windows. Here, the admin can set how often conference participants should be rotated in the layout.\\u0004Participant rotation interval (seconds)":[""],"The text hint for an input field. In this case, the word “channel” refers to an audio channel during a video meeting. Please note that in this string %n is a counter indicating the number of characters typed into the input field while %m is the maximum number of characters. Don’t delete or translate these parts of the string.\\u0004Channel name (%n/%m)":[""],"The text hint for an input field.Here, the admin can select date and time. Nominative case.\\u0004Date and time":[""],"The text hint for an option in the context menu. This configuration will call all the participants when they are added to the conference.\\u0004All participants":[""],"The text hint for an option in the context menu. This configuration will call only certain server users when they are added to the conference.\\u0004Participants from the address book":[""],"The text hint for an option in the context menu. This configuration will call only unregistered SIP/H.323 endpoinds when they are added to the conference.\\u0004Connected by address":[""],"The text hint for an option in the drop-down menu. The administrator can configure layout settings for a video conference. For example, he/she can choose if the current speaker should see his/he video in the enlarged window. Please note that these settings do not affect how other users will see the speaker. They can still see the participant in the enlarged window.\\u0004The speaker will not see oneself in the enlarged window":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a button or a subheading. The term “cascading” is used in the context of MCU (multi-point control unit) used for connecting multiple video conferencing endpoints. \\"Cascading\\" refers to the method of connecting multiple MCUs together to create a larger, scalable video conference that can support a very high number of participants. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Basic cascading":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a button or subheading. The word is a part of the phrase “basic cascading”. The word “cascading” is used in the context of MCU (a multi-point control unit). An MCU is a software solution or device used for connecting multiple video conferencing endpoints. Cascading\\" refers to the method of connecting multiple MCUs together to create a larger video conference that can support a high number of participants. The word “basic” is used because here we are talking about the most simple form of cascading.\\u0004Basic":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a description of an event (someone tries to sign in to the system). Moreover, this hint will be the title of a checkbox in a filter. If this box is checked, the event log will include the cases when an authorization attempt was made.\\u0004Authorization Attempt":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a description of an event (when someone signs into the system). Moreover, this hint will be the title of a checkbox in a filter. If this box is checked, the event log will include various events related to authorization\\u0004Authorization":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a description of an event. A role is a set of permissions given to a user. Moreover, this hint can be used as the title of a checkbox in a filter. If this box is checked, the log will include the events related to adding a role.\\u0004Role adding":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a description of an event. A role is a set of permissions given to a user. Moreover, this hint can be used as the title of a checkbox in a filter. If this box is checked, the log will include the events related to the deletion of a role.\\u0004Role deletion":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a description of an event. Moreover, it can be used as the title of a checkbox in a filter. If this box is checked, the event log will include the cases when user authorization was blocked due to some reason.\\u0004Authorization Blocking":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a description of an event. Moreover, this hint can be used as the title of a checkbox in a filter. If this box is checked, the log will include the events related to login change.\\u0004Login change":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a description of an event. Moreover, this hint can be used as the title of a checkbox in a filter. If this box is checked, the log will include the events related to password change.\\u0004Password change":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a description of an event. Moreover, this hint will be the title of a checkbox in a filter. If this box is checked, the log will include the events related to account creation.\\u0004Account creation":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a description of an event. Moreover, this hint will be the title of a checkbox in a filter. If this box is checked, the log will include the events related to account deletion.\\u0004Account deletion":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a heading or table column header. The term “cascading” is used in the context of MCU. An MCU  (multi-point control unit) is a hardware or software solution used for connecting multiple video conferencing endpoints. \\"Cascading\\" refers to the method of connecting multiple MCUs together to create a larger video conference that can support a high number of participants.\\u0004Cascading mode":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a subheading or table column header. Here, one can check the start and end time of a conference or any other event.\\u0004Start and end time":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a subheading or the label for an input field. It may refer to the name of a file or the name of a person. It will be displayed in various parts of the UI.\\u0004Display name":[""],"The text hint that can be used as a table column header or a subheading. Here, one can check the name of a file.\\u0004File name":[""],"The text hint that can be used as the heading for the list of errors. Plus, it can be used as a checkbox for the list of server events. If this box is checked, the list will include only errors. The word is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Errors":[""],"The text hint that can be used as the title for an input field. Additionally, it can be used as a subheading where one can check the minimum number of characters in a password. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Minimum number of characters":[""],"The text hint that can be used either for a filter or as a brief desscription of the event type. If this filter is selected, the event log will include only the events t related to security.\\u0004Security":[""],"The text hint that can be used for a switcher or checkbox. Here, the admin can set the requirements for a password. For example, he/she can choose if it is necessary to include digits, lower or uppercase letters and special characters. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004digits":[""],"The text hint that can be used for a switcher or checkbox. Here, the admin can set the requirements for a password. For example, he/she can choose if it is necessary to include digits, lower or uppercase letters and special characters. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004lowercase letters":[""],"The text hint that can be used for a switcher or checkbox. Here, the admin can set the requirements for a password. For example, he/she can choose if it is necessary to include digits, lower or uppercase letters and special characters. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004special characters":[""],"The text hint that can be used for a switcher or checkbox. Here, the admin can set the requirements for a password. For example, he/she can choose if it is necessary to include digits, lower or uppercase letters and special characters. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004the login cannot be used as part of the password":[""],"The text hint that can be used for a switcher or checkbox. Here, the admin can set the requirements for a password. For example, he/she can choose if it is necessary to include digits, lower or uppercase letters and special characters. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004uppercase letters":[""],"The text hint that can be used in different parts of the UI. For example, it can be used as the label for an input field, subheading or a drop-down list. Here, one can check or select when a video conference will end.. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Conference end":[""],"The text hint that can be used in different parts of the UI. For example, it can be used as the label for an input field, subheading or a drop-down list. Here, one can check or select when a video conference will start. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Conference start":[""],"The text hint that specifies the maximum duration of a conference recording.  In this case, %n will be replaced with a number equal or greater than 1.\\u0004Maximum recording length - %n hour":["","Maximum recording length - %n hours"],"The text hint that specifies the maximum duration of a conference recording. %n will be replaced with a number equal or greater than 1.\\u0004Maximum recording length - %n minute":["","Maximum recording length - %n minutes"],"The text hint which can be used as a subheading or a tab name. Here, we are talking about the participants of a video conference.\\u0004Conference participants":[""],"The text hint which can be used as one of the options in the menu or a heading. It describes a video layout for a video conference. A layout is the arrangement of video windows on the screen. If this option is selected, the layout will be adjusted dynamically depending on the number of participants. The word “automatic” is fully appropriate here because some of the parameters have to be set manually.  The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Dynamic layout":[""],"The text hint which can be used as one of the options in the menu or a heading. It describes a video layout for a video conference. A layout is the arrangement of video windows on the screen. If this option is selected, the layout will be automatically adjusted depending on the number of conference participants. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Automatic selection":[""],"The text hint which can be used as one of the options in the menu or a heading. It describes a video layout for a video conference. A layout is the arrangement of video windows on the screen. If this option is selected, the user will have to configure the layout manually.\\u0004Manual configuration":[""],"The text hint which can be used in multiple parts of the UI, e,g., as a subheading or tab name. Here, one can preview a layout, image, or video. The word is used as a noun.\\u0004Preview":[""],"The text hint which describes an event in the server, Here, we are talking about the history of multiple video conferences. This is why the word “conferences” is used in the plural form.\\u0004History of all conferences is exported":[""],"The text hint which describes an event on the server. This hint is supposed to warn the administrator about a potential problem (running out of disk space).\\u0004The hard disk is full":[""],"The text hint which describes the role of a certain user who was either added or deleted (e.g., administrator). The word “role” is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Role":[""],"The text hint which describes the type of conference. This term is used in the context of MCU and cascading.  MCU (multi-point control unit) is a hardware or software device used for connecting several video conferencing endpoints. \\"Cascading\\" refers to the method of connecting multiple MCUs together to create a larger video conference that can support a high number of participants. If a conference receives the type “Periphery”, it will receive the layout created for the central conference.\\u0004Periphery":[""],"The text hint which describes the type of conference. This term is used in the context of MCU and cascading.  MCU (multi-point control unit) is a hardware or software solution used for connecting several video conferencing endpoints. \\"Cascading\\" refers to the method of connecting multiple MCUs together to create a larger video conference that can support a high number of participants. If a conference gets the type “Center”, its video layout will be used for all participants connected to an MCU.\\u0004Center":[""],"The text hint which describes the type of conference. This term is used in the context of MCU and cascading.  MCU (multipi-point control unit) is a hardware or software solution used for connecting several video conferencing endpoints. \\"Cascading\\" refers to the method of connecting multiple MCUs together to create a larger video conference that can support a high number of participants. The central conference determines the layout created for all participants.\\u0004Central cascading conference":[""],"The text hint which describes the type of conference. This term is used in the context of MCU and cascading.  MCU (multipi-point control unit) is a hardware or software solution used for connecting several video conferencing endpoints. \\"Cascading\\" refers to the method of connecting multiple MCUs together to create a larger, scalable video conference that can support a high number of participants. The peripheral conference will get the layout created for the central conference.\\u0004Peripheral cascading conference":[""],"The text hint which refers to the media files (e.g. images or videos) that will be shared by participants during a video meeting. The word “files” is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Media files in the conference":[""],"The text hint. MCU stands for multipoint control unit, a device used for connecting multiple video conferencing endpoints. Calibration is the process which is aimed at determining the most optimal configuration for the device. This text can be used as the description of an event in the event log or the phrase which explains why a video conference ended. The phrase is used in the nominative case.\\u0004MCU calibration":[""],"The text hint. This hint appears when a video does not have its own audio track and the mute/unmute function is unavailable.\\u0004Audio track missing":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004[a]Fill in the form[/a] on TrueConf website using your e-mail address.":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004Are you sure you want to delete the selected groups?":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004Are you sure you want to delete the selected user accounts?":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004Are you sure you want to delete the selected user addresses?":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004Are you sure you want to end content sharing by “%DisplayName”?":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004Do you want to delete “%file_name”?":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004Do you want to delete selected files?":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004Do you want to remove “%filename”?":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004Do you want to remove selected files?":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004Once submitted we\'ll extend your license automatically.":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004Re-enter the registration key in %trueconf_mcu Web Manager in this section":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004To renew your license for another year, please do the following:":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004To renew your license, please [a]contact our sales department[/a].":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004You are using %trueconf_mcu Free that has [a]certain limitations[/a].":[""],"The text in the pop-up message\\u0004You can test the full-featured trial version for a limited period or buy the full version of %trueconf_mcu.":[""],"The text that can be used either as a filter or as a brief description of an event type. Here, we are talking about the phrase “system event”, for example, server restart.\\u0004System":[""],"The text, which contains the ID of the occurred event.\\u0004Event ID":[""],"The time when the conference is supposed to start.\\u0004Start date and time:":[""],"The title for a list of users who have not joined the conference\\u0004Disconnected":[""],"The title hint for an input field. Here, the administrator will provide the description of a role provided by a user. Please note that in this case %n is the number of characters entered into the input field while the %m is the maximum number of characters. Don’t delete or translate these parts of the string.\\u0004Role description (%n/%m)":[""],"The title of a checkbox. Here, we are talking about the participants of a video conference. If this checkbox is enabled, the participant, who is speaking at the moment, will be displayed in an enlarged window.\\u0004Enable detection of participants’ voice activity":[""],"The title of a checkbox. If this box is checked, the conference will end automatically if all participants leave and no one joins for a certain number of minutes. Please note that the preposition “for” will be followed by the number of minutes during which users can join the conference, e.g. 10 or 15 minutes.\\u0004No participant in the conference for":[""],"The title of a checkbox. If this box is checked, the conference will end automatically if there is only one participant in the conference for a certain number of minutes. Please note that the preposition “for” will be followed by the number of minutes during which users can join the conference, e.g. 10 or 15 minutes.\\u0004Only one participant remains in the conference for":[""],"The title of a checkbox. If this box is checked, the conference will end automatically, if no one joins this meeting after its beginning. Please note that the preposition “for” will be followed by the number of minutes during which users can join the conference, e.g. 10 or 15 minutes.\\u0004The conference starts, but no one joins it for":[""],"The title of a checkbox. If this box is checked, the distance between layout windows will be increased.\\u0004Increase distance between video windows":[""],"The title of a checkbox. If this box is checked, the event log will include various events related to conferences.\\u0004Conferences":[""],"The title of a checkbox. If this box is checked, the event log will include various events related to user account information.\\u0004Accounts":[""],"The title of a checkbox. If this box is checked, the event log will include various events related to user roles.\\u0004Roles":[""],"The title of a checkbox. If this box is checked, the event log will include various server-related events.\\u0004Server":[""],"The title of a checkbox. If this box is checked, the participants, who are speaking at the moment, will be displayed in a video window that has a frame. Other participants will be displayed without a frame.\\u0004Highlight active speakers with a frame":[""],"The title of a checkbox. If this box is marked, every user who has a link will be able to join the video conference from a browser or client app.\\u0004Allow access to conference via link":[""],"The title of a checkbox. If this box is marked, the conference will be held daily.\\u0004Hold daily":[""],"The title of a drop-down list\\u0004Participants’ names":[""],"The title of a drop-down list for selecting a font.\\u0004Font":[""],"The title of a drop-down list for selecting a network interface.\\u0004Network interface":[""],"The title of a drop-down list needed for adjusting video quality settings. Please note that frame size should not be confused with resolution. These terms are close, but not interchangeable in this case. The real resolution may vary, but it won’t exceed the frame size.\\u0004Maximum frame size":[""],"The title of a drop-down list.\\u0004Noise cancellation":[""],"The title of a drop-down list.\\u0004Time zone":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. AGC (automatic gain control)\\u0004AGC":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. By selecting one of the options in this list, the administrator will determine where conference participant’s names will be displayed during a video meeting.\\u0004Position options":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. H.235 is an encryption standard used for video conferencing endpoints. The drop-down list will be needed for enabling or disabling H.235 encryption.\\u0004H.235 encryption":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, one can select the quality of video in video recordings and during streaming.\\u0004Recording and stream quality":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the admin can select if the video from a user’s camera (self-view) may be displayed in the video layout during a meeting.\\u0004Self-view in the layout":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the admin can select the end time for a video conference.\\u0004End time":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the admin can select the start time for a video conference.\\u0004Start time":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the admin can select the type of secure connection.\\u0004Secure connection":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the admin can select the value of the maximum frame rate during video meetings.\\u0004Maximum frame rate (FPS)":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the admin can specify the time period during which a user’s account will be blocked if this person makes too many failed authorization attempts.\\u0004Lockout period":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the administrator can configure settings for the call that will be made to the participants at the beginning of a conference.\\u0004Default participant call settings":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the administrator can either enable or disable SIP (Session Initiation Protocol) encryption. If it is possible, please leave “SIP” translation because it is a generally recognized term among system administrators.\\u0004SIP encryption":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the administrator can select a time zone. Nominative case.\\u0004Time zone":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the administrator can select how often the application should synchronize its time with a time server.\\u0004Synchronization frequency":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the administrator can select the video bitrate for a video stream.\\u0004Maximum bitrate (kbit/s)":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. Here, the administrator can set the duration of a video meeting.\\u0004Duration":[""],"The title of a drop-down list. This list is needed for selecting when a conference should end. For example, the meeting can end automatically if no one joins it for 10 or 15 minutes. In this drop-down list, the admin can select such options as 10 minutes or 15 minutes.\\u0004Interval":[""],"The title of a dropdown list for selecting a font size.\\u0004Size":[""],"The title of a list. This list includes the files that are not used for content sharing during ongoing conferences.\\u0004Not shared":[""],"The title of a pop-up window where the administrator can adjust settings for recording a video conference.\\u0004Conference recording":[""],"The title of a pop-up window where the administrator can configure streaming settings for a video conference.\\u0004Conference streaming":[""],"The title of a radio button. If this option is selected, the administrator will be able to export parts of the database. It is possible to select the parts of the database that should be exported.\\u0004Select export parameters":[""],"The title of a radio button. This button will be used for the video conferencing mode in which the participant, who is speaking at the moment, will always be seen by other users. If this button is selected, this participant will be displayed either in an enlarged video window or in the upper left corner. However, the video windows of other participants will remain in the layout. If the other option is selected, the participant speaking at the moment will always be displayed in a fullscreen video window; other users will be removed from the layout. The word “selective” is used here to indicate that the moderator can select the type of layout and participants who should be displayed in this layout.\\u0004Designated window":[""],"The title of a radio button. This button will be used for the video conferencing mode in which the participant, who is speaking at the moment, will always be seen by other users. If this button is selected, this participant will be displayed in a full-screen video window. If the other option is selected, this user will be displayed in an enlarged video window, but other participants will still remain visible. The word “exclusive” is used here to indicate that no one except the speaker can be seen.\\u0004Full screen":[""],"The title of a switcher. If this switcher is activated, a user will not be allowed to include his/her login as a part of the password.\\u0004Prohibit to use the login within the password":[""],"The title of a switcher. If this switcher is activated, a user will not be allowed to join a video conference if he/she enters an incorrect PIN.\\u0004Lock a conference from a user if incorrect PIN is entered":[""],"The title of a switcher. If this switcher is activated, a user’s account will be blocked, if this person makes several unsuccessful attempts to sign in. This switcher will be followed by an input field where the number of unsuccessful attempts has to be specified. \\u0004Block an account after failed authorization":[""],"The title of a switcher. If this switcher is activated, a user’s password will have to include digits.\\u0004Digits":[""],"The title of a switcher. If this switcher is activated, a user’s password will have to include lowercase letters.\\u0004Lowercase letters (a-z)":[""],"The title of a switcher. If this switcher is activated, a user’s password will have to include some special characters (e.g., hashes, ampersands, and so forth).\\u0004Special characters":[""],"The title of a switcher. If this switcher is activated, a user’s password will have to include uppercase letters.\\u0004Uppercase letters (A-Z)":[""],"The title of a switcher. If this switcher is activated, the lifetime of a user’s password will be limited (e.g. two or three days).\\u0004Limit password lifetime":[""],"The title of a switcher. If this switcher is activated, the new UI navigation will be activated. If this switcher is disabled, an older version of UI navigation will be used.\\u0004New navigation":[""],"The title of a switcher.If this switcher is activated, the application time will be synchronized with the time on an NTP (network time protocol) server.\\u0004Synchronize time with NTP server":[""],"The title of a tab where a user will configure audio channel settings. For example, the user will be able to select the participants who will send or receive audio during a video meeting.\\u0004Audio channels":[""],"The title of a video conferencing mode in which everyone can see and hear the participant who is speaking at the moment (voice detection mechanism is used). The word “mode” is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Voice activity detection mode":[""],"The title of an input field. Here, the admin can specify the number of failed authorization attempts a user can make before his/her account will be blocked.\\u0004Number of failed attempts":[""],"The title of an input field. Here, the administrator can specify the type of a network protocol used for making a call over the Internet (e.g., SIP, H.323).\\u0004Protocol":[""],"The title of an input field. In this case, %n is the number of characters that have already been typed while %m is the maximum number of characters.\\u0004User Name (%n/%m)":[""],"The title of an input field. The display name is the name shown in the video window of a conference participant. Please note that this phrase includes a counter. %n is the current number of characters entered into the input field while 128 is the maximum number of characters.\\u0004Display name (%n/128)":[""],"The tooltip displayed when the mouse is hovered over an icon button. Here, we are talking about the application that enables users to stream media files (audio or video). If the button is clicked, the app will stream audio to conference participants.\\u0004Enable audio track":[""],"The tooltip displayed when the mouse is hovered over an icon button. Here, we are talking about the application that enables users to stream media files (audio or video). If this option is selected, the application will only stream video (without audio).\\u0004Disable audio track":[""],"The tooltip for a button that enables a user to send an invitation to meeting participants.\\u0004Send conference invitation":[""],"The tooltip for a button. If the button is clicked, the name of a video conference will be used as a part of its route (the network path needed for accessing the conference).\\u0004Use the name as a route":[""],"The tooltip for a button. If the button is clicked, the name of a video conference will not be used as a part of its route (the network path needed for accessing the conference).\\u0004Do not use the name as a route":[""],"The tooltip for an icon button that  generates a new PIN for a video meeting. It will be used for joining this meeting.\\u0004Generate new PIN":[""],"The tooltip for an icon button that generates a new ID (unique identifier) for a video meeting.\\u0004Generate new ID":[""],"The tooltip for an icon button that opens a menu where the administrator can change the display name for a conference participant. The display name is the name shown in the layout of a video conference.\\u0004Change display name":[""],"The tooltip for an icon button. Here, we are talking about the devices that will be added to a video conference. However, they are not currently connected to any video meeting. VNC stands for Virtual Computer Networking, while RTSP stands for Real-time Streaming Protocol.\\u0004Devices (VNC/RTSP) and media files":[""],"The tooltip for an icon button. Here, we are talking about the users who were invited to a video conference via SIP (Session Initiation Protocol) and H.323. However, at present, they are not participating in any meeting.\\u0004Participants (SIP/H.323)":[""],"The tooltip for an icon button. If this button is clicked, the selected participant will be appointed as lecturer. In this case, the lecturer is the only participant who is allowed to speak during a conference.\\u0004Appoint as lecturer":[""],"The tooltip for an icon button. This button generates a route that will be needed for joining a video meeting hosted on a video conferencing server.\\u0004Generate new route":[""],"The tooltip for an icon button. This button opens the menu where the admin can select a file that will be shared during a video meeting (e.g., an image, video, or slides).\\u0004Add a file for content sharing":[""],"The tooltip. In this case, the lecturer is the only person allowed to speak during a video meeting. Nominative case.\\u0004Lecturer":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that changes were made to the server’s security settings.\\u0004Security settings change":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that the server event log was exported.\\u0004Event log export":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that the server was reset to default settings and data was deleted.\\u0004Server data deletion":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that the user attempted to join a conference.\\u0004Attempting to connect to the conference":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that the user’s attempt to join a conference was rejected.\\u0004Blocking connection to the conference":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that there was an error during account creation, preventing the creation of a new account.\\u0004Account creation error":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that there was an error during account deletion, preventing the deletion of the account.\\u0004Account deletion error":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that there was an error during the export of the server event log, preventing the export.\\u0004Export log error":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that there was an error during the password change, preventing the change.\\u0004Password change error":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that there was an error during the role change/addition, preventing the change/addition.\\u0004Error adding role":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that there was an error during the role removal, preventing the removal.\\u0004Role deletion Error":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that there was an error during the security settings change, preventing the change.\\u0004Settings change error":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that there was an error during the server reset to default settings.\\u0004Server data deletion error":[""],"The type of an event, indicating that there was an error during the username change, preventing the change.\\u0004Login change error":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that account credentials are not found.\\u0004Account credentials not found":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that such a user role is not assigned on the server.\\u0004Role not found":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the account of the user being searched for has been deleted or has not yet been created.\\u0004User not found":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the conference the user was looking for is either not created or has already ended.\\u0004Conference not found":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the login you tried to set is already in use on the server.\\u0004The login already exists":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the maximum number of participants for the conference has been reached, and no more users can be added.\\u0004Maximum number of participants reached":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the password you tried to set is already in use on the server.\\u0004The password already exists.":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the user does not have sufficient permissions to perform the operation.\\u0004Insufficient permissions":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the user does not have the assigned user role.\\u0004User role not found":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the user entered an incorrect conference ID.\\u0004Unknown conference ID":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the user entered an incorrect PIN for joining the conference.\\u0004Invalid conference PIN":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the user entered an unused login or made a typo in the login.\\u0004Unknown login":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the user made a mistake when entering the password.\\u0004Invalid password":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the user missed mandatory fields when filling out the data.\\u0004Required fields are not filled in.":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that the user role was already assigned earlier.\\u0004The user already has a role.":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that there was an error during the system backup.\\u0004System reset error":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that there was an error during the user\'s authorization.\\u0004Authorization Error":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that there was an error in the global settings.\\u0004Global Settings Error":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that there was an error indicating no access to the database.\\u0004Database Error":[""],"The type of the error, indicating that there was an error restarting the services; the services are not running.\\u0004Service Restart Error":[""],"The user status.\\u0004Busy":[""],"This button enables the administrator to create a new object. Verb in the infinitive form.\\u0004Create":[""],"This message shows up when the user cannot access the server or conference due to a restriction.\\u0004Access Denied":[""],"This text hint refers to a video conference. It will be a table column header or subheading. The word is used in the nominative case.\\u0004Conference":[""],"Title\\u0004Display name background":[""],"Title\\u0004Number of active conferences":[""],"Title of an informational notification about downloading the app\\u0004App not open?":[""],"Tooltip for the button and Drag-and-Drop area: This function allows you to add a user to the conference without connecting them. A user added using this function will appear in the conference list under the \\"Disconnected\\" heading.\\u0004Add without connecting":[""],"Tooltip: Appears when a user hovers over a user who was added to the conference but not connected.\\u0004Connect to the conference":[""],"Video window caption\\u0004Time rotation":[""],"When this button is clicked on, the selected participant is disconnected.\\u0004Disconnect":[""],"When this button is clicked on, the selected user is removed from the conference\\u0004Disconnect":[""],"Window title\\u0004Disconnecting participants":[""],"Window title\\u0004Remove file":[""],"Window title\\u0004Remove selected files":[""],"Window title\\u0004Removing a participant":[""]}}'));e("default",{domain:t,locale_data:n})}}});
